"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api/api.go\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Great! Let me look at the api.go file first since that's likely where the `gh api` command is implemented:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "1→package api\n     2→\n     3→import (\n     4→\t\"bytes\"\n     5→\t\"encoding/json\"\n     6→\t\"errors\"\n     7→\t\"fmt\"\n     8→\t\"io\"\n     9→\t\"net/http\"\n    10→\t\"os\"\n    11→\t\"path/filepath\"\n    12→\t\"regexp\"\n    13→\t\"runtime\"\n    14→\t\"sort\"\n    15→\t\"strings\"\n    16→\t\"time\"\n    17→\n    18→\t\"github.com/MakeNowJust/heredoc\"\n    19→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/api\"\n    20→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/gh\"\n    21→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/ghinstance\"\n    22→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/ghrepo\"\n    23→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/pkg/cmd/factory\"\n    24→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/pkg/cmdutil\"\n    25→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/pkg/iostreams\"\n    26→\t\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/pkg/jsoncolor\"\n    27→\t\"github.com/cli/go-gh/v2/pkg/jq\"\n    28→\t\"github.com/cli/go-gh/v2/pkg/template\"\n    29→\t\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n    30→)\n    31→\n    32→const (\n    33→\tttyIndent = \"  \"\n    34→)\n    35→\n    36→type ApiOptions struct {\n    37→\tAppVersion string\n    38→\tBaseRepo   func() (ghrepo.Interface, error)\n    39→\tBranch     func() (string, error)\n    40→\tConfig     func() (gh.Config, error)\n    41→\tHttpClient func() (*http.Client, error)\n    42→\tIO         *iostreams.IOStreams\n    43→\n    44→\tHostname            string\n    45→\tRequestMethod       string\n    46→\tRequestMethodPassed bool\n    47→\tRequestPath         string\n    48→\tRequestInputFile    string\n    49→\tMagicFields         []string\n    50→\tRawFields           []string\n    51→\tRequestHeaders      []string\n    52→\tPreviews            []string\n    53→\tShowResponseHeaders bool\n    54→\tPaginate            bool\n    55→\tSlurp               bool\n    56→\tSilent              bool\n    57→\tTemplate            string\n    58→\tCacheTTL            time.Duration\n    59→\tFilterOutput        string\n    60→\tVerbose             bool\n    61→}\n    62→\n    63→func NewCmdApi(f *cmdutil.Factory, runF func(*ApiOptions) error) *cobra.Command {\n    64→\topts := ApiOptions{\n    65→\t\tAppVersion: f.AppVersion,\n    66→\t\tBaseRepo:   f.BaseRepo,\n    67→\t\tBranch:     f.Branch,\n    68→\t\tConfig:     f.Config,\n    69→\t\tIO:         f.IOStreams,\n    70→\t}\n    71→\n    72→\tcmd := &cobra.Command{\n    73→\t\tUse:   \"api <endpoint>\",\n    74→\t\tShort: \"Make an authenticated GitHub API request\",\n    75→\t\tLong: heredoc.Docf(`\n    76→\t\t\tMakes an authenticated HTTP request to the GitHub API and prints the response.\n    77→\n    78→\t\t\tThe endpoint argument should either be a path of a GitHub API v3 endpoint, or\n    79→\t\t\t%[1]sgraphql%[1]s to access the GitHub API v4.\n    80→\n    81→\t\t\tPlaceholder values %[1]s{owner}%[1]s, %[1]s{repo}%[1]s, and %[1]s{branch}%[1]s in the endpoint\n    82→\t\t\targument will get replaced with values from the repository of the current\n    83→\t\t\tdirectory or the repository specified in the %[1]sGH_REPO%[1]s environment variable.\n    84→\t\t\tNote that in some shells, for example PowerShell, you may need to enclose\n    85→\t\t\tany value that contains %[1]s{...}%[1]s in quotes to prevent the shell from\n    86→\t\t\tapplying special meaning to curly braces.\n    87→\n    88→\t\t\tThe default HTTP request method is %[1]sGET%[1]s normally and %[1]sPOST%[1]s if any parameters\n    89→\t\t\twere added. Override the method with %[1]s--method%[1]s.\n    90→\n    91→\t\t\tPass one or more %[1]s-f/--raw-field%[1]s values in %[1]skey=value%[1]s format to add static string\n    92→\t\t\tparameters to the request payload. To add non-string or placeholder-determined values, see\n    93→\t\t\t%[1]s-F/--field%[1]s below. Note that adding request parameters will automatically switch the\n    94→\t\t\trequest method to %[1]sPOST%[1]s. To send the parameters as a %[1]sGET%[1]s query string instead, use\n    95→\t\t\t%[1]s--method GET%[1]s.\n    96→\n    97→\t\t\tThe %[1]s-F/--field%[1]s flag has magic type conversion based on the format of the value:\n    98→\n    99→\t\t\t- literal values %[1]strue%[1]s, %[1]sfalse%[1]s, %[1]snull%[1]s, and integer numbers get converted to\n   100→\t\t\t  appropriate JSON types;\n   101→\t\t\t- placeholder values %[1]s{owner}%[1]s, %[1]s{repo}%[1]s, and %[1]s{branch}%[1]s get populated with values\n   102→\t\t\t  from the repository of the current directory;\n   103→\t\t\t- if the value starts with %[1]s@%[1]s, the rest of the value is interpreted as a\n   104→\t\t\t  filename to read the value from. Pass %[1]s-%[1]s to read from standard input.\n   105→\n   106→\t\t\tFor GraphQL requests, all fields other than %[1]squery%[1]s and %[1]soperationName%[1]s are\n   107→\t\t\tinterpreted as GraphQL variables.\n   108→\n   109→\t\t\tTo pass nested parameters in the request payload, use %[1]skey[subkey]=value%[1]s syntax when\n   110→\t\t\tdeclaring fields. To pass nested values as arrays, declare multiple fields with the\n   111→\t\t\tsyntax %[1]skey[]=value1%[1]s, %[1]skey[]=value2%[1]s. To pass an empty array, use %[1]skey[]%[1]s without a\n   112→\t\t\tvalue.\n   113→\n   114→\t\t\tTo pass pre-constructed JSON or payloads in other formats, a request body may be read\n   115→\t\t\tfrom file specified by %[1]s--input%[1]s. Use %[1]s-%[1]s to read from standard input. When passing the\n   116→\t\t\trequest body this way, any parameters specified via field flags are added to the query\n   117→\t\t\tstring of the endpoint URL.\n   118→\n   119→\t\t\tIn %[1]s--paginate%[1]s mode, all pages of results will sequentially be requested until\n   120→\t\t\tthere are no more pages of results. For GraphQL requests, this requires that the\n   121→\t\t\toriginal query accepts an %[1]s$endCursor: String%[1]s variable and that it fetches the\n   122→\t\t\t%[1]spageInfo{ hasNextPage, endCursor }%[1]s set of fields from a collection. Each page is a separate\n   123→\t\t\tJSON array or object. Pass %[1]s--slurp%[1]s to wrap all pages of JSON arrays or objects\n   124→\t\t\tinto an outer JSON array.\n   125→\t\t`, \"`\"),\n   126→\t\tExample: heredoc.Doc(`\n   127→\t\t\t# list releases in the current repository\n   128→\t\t\t$ gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/releases\n   129→\n   130→\t\t\t# post an issue comment\n   131→\t\t\t$ gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/123/comments -f body='Hi from CLI'\n   132→\n   133→\t\t\t# post nested parameter read from a file\n   134→\t\t\t$ gh api gists -F 'files[myfile.txt][content]=@myfile.txt'\n   135→\n   136→\t\t\t# add parameters to a GET request\n   137→\t\t\t$ gh api -X GET search/issues -f q='repo:cli/cli is:open remote'\n   138→\n   139→\t\t\t# set a custom HTTP header\n   140→\t\t\t$ gh api -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github.v3.raw+json' ...\n   141→\n   142→\t\t\t# opt into GitHub API previews\n   143→\t\t\t$ gh api --preview baptiste,nebula ...\n   144→\n   145→\t\t\t# print only specific fields from the response\n   146→\t\t\t$ gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues --jq '.[].title'\n   147→\n   148→\t\t\t# use a template for the output\n   149→\t\t\t$ gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues --template \\\n   150→\t\t\t  '{{range .}}{{.title}} ({{.labels | pluck \"name\" | join \", \" | color \"yellow\"}}){{\"\\n\"}}{{end}}'\n   151→\n   152→\t\t\t# update allowed values of the \"environment\" custom property in a deeply nested array\n   153→\t\t\tgh api -X PATCH /orgs/{org}/properties/schema \\\n   154→\t\t\t   -F 'properties[][property_name]=environment' \\\n   155→\t\t\t   -F 'properties[][default_value]=production' \\\n   156→\t\t\t   -F 'properties[][allowed_values][]=staging' \\\n   157→\t\t\t   -F 'properties[][allowed_values][]=production'\n   158→\n   159→\t\t\t# list releases with GraphQL\n   160→\t\t\t$ gh api graphql -F owner='{owner}' -F name='{repo}' -f query='\n   161→\t\t\t  query($name: String!, $owner: String!) {\n   162→\t\t\t    repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) {\n   163→\t\t\t      releases(last: 3) {\n   164→\t\t\t        nodes { tagName }\n   165→\t\t\t      }\n   166→\t\t\t    }\n   167→\t\t\t  }\n   168→\t\t\t'\n   169→\n   170→\t\t\t# list all repositories for a user\n   171→\t\t\t$ gh api graphql --paginate -f query='\n   172→\t\t\t  query($endCursor: String) {\n   173→\t\t\t    viewer {\n   174→\t\t\t      repositories(first: 100, after: $endCursor) {\n   175→\t\t\t        nodes { nameWithOwner }\n   176→\t\t\t        pageInfo {\n   177→\t\t\t          hasNextPage\n   178→\t\t\t          endCursor\n   179→\t\t\t        }\n   180→\t\t\t      }\n   181→\t\t\t    }\n   182→\t\t\t  }\n   183→\t\t\t'\n   184→\n   185→\t\t\t# get the percentage of forks for the current user\n   186→\t\t\t$ gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='\n   187→\t\t\t  query($endCursor: String) {\n   188→\t\t\t    viewer {\n   189→\t\t\t      repositories(first: 100, after: $endCursor) {\n   190→\t\t\t        nodes { isFork }\n   191→\t\t\t        pageInfo {\n   192→\t\t\t          hasNextPage\n   193→\t\t\t          endCursor\n   194→\t\t\t        }\n   195→\t\t\t      }\n   196→\t\t\t    }\n   197→\t\t\t  }\n   198→\t\t\t' | jq 'def count(e): reduce e as $_ (0;.+1);\n   199→\t\t\t[.[].data.viewer.repositories.nodes[]] as $r | count(select($r[].isFork))/count($r[])'\n   200→\t\t`),\n   201→\t\tAnnotations: map[string]string{\n   202→\t\t\t\"help:environment\": heredoc.Doc(`\n   203→\t\t\t\tGH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN (in order of precedence): an authentication token for\n   204→\t\t\t\tgithub.com API requests.\n   205→\n   206→\t\t\t\tGH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN, GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN (in order of precedence): an\n   207→\t\t\t\tauthentication token for API requests to GitHub Enterprise.\n   208→\n   209→\t\t\t\tGH_HOST: make the request to a GitHub host other than github.com.\n   210→\t\t\t`),\n   211→\t\t},\n   212→\t\tArgs: cobra.ExactArgs(1),\n   213→\t\tPreRun: func(c *cobra.Command, args []string) {\n   214→\t\t\topts.BaseRepo = cmdutil.OverrideBaseRepoFunc(f, \"\")\n   215→\t\t},\n   216→\t\tRunE: func(c *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n   217→\t\t\topts.RequestPath = args[0]\n   218→\t\t\topts.RequestMethodPassed = c.Flags().Changed(\"method\")\n   219→\n   220→\t\t\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" && filepath.IsAbs(opts.RequestPath) {\n   221→\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(`invalid API endpoint: \"%s\". Your shell might be rewriting URL paths as filesystem paths. To avoid this, omit the leading slash from the endpoint argument`, opts.RequestPath)\n   222→\t\t\t}\n   223→\n   224→\t\t\tif c.Flags().Changed(\"hostname\") {\n   225→\t\t\t\tif err := ghinstance.HostnameValidator(opts.Hostname); err != nil {\n   226→\t\t\t\t\treturn cmdutil.FlagErrorf(\"error parsing `--hostname`: %w\", err)\n   227→\t\t\t\t}\n   228→\t\t\t}\n   229→\n   230→\t\t\tif opts.Paginate && !strings.EqualFold(opts.RequestMethod, \"GET\") && opts.RequestPath != \"graphql\" {\n   231→\t\t\t\treturn cmdutil.FlagErrorf(\"the `--paginate` option is not supported for non-GET requests\")\n   232→\t\t\t}\n   233→\n   234→\t\t\tif err := cmdutil.MutuallyExclusive(\n   235→\t\t\t\t\"the `--paginate` option is not supported with `--input`\",\n   236→\t\t\t\topts.Paginate,\n   237→\t\t\t\topts.RequestInputFile != \"\",\n   238→\t\t\t); err != nil {\n   239→\t\t\t\treturn err\n   240→\t\t\t}\n   241→\n   242→\t\t\tif opts.Slurp {\n   243→\t\t\t\tif err := cmdutil.MutuallyExclusive(\n   244→\t\t\t\t\t\"the `--slurp` option is not supported with `--jq` or `--template`\",\n   245→\t\t\t\t\topts.Slurp,\n   246→\t\t\t\t\topts.FilterOutput != \"\",\n   247→\t\t\t\t\topts.Template != \"\",\n   248→\t\t\t\t); err != nil {\n   249→\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n   250→\t\t\t\t}\n   251→\n   252→\t\t\t\tif !opts.Paginate {\n   253→\t\t\t\t\treturn cmdutil.FlagErrorf(\"`--paginate` required when passing `--slurp`\")\n   254→\t\t\t\t}\n   255→\t\t\t}\n   256→\n   257→\t\t\tif err := cmdutil.MutuallyExclusive(\n   258→\t\t\t\t\"only one of `--template`, `--jq`, `--silent`, or `--verbose` may be used\",\n   259→\t\t\t\topts.Verbose,\n   260→\t\t\t\topts.Silent,\n   261→\t\t\t\topts.FilterOutput != \"\",\n   262→\t\t\t\topts.Template != \"\",\n   263→\t\t\t); err != nil {\n   264→\t\t\t\treturn err\n   265→\t\t\t}\n   266→\n   267→\t\t\tif runF != nil {\n   268→\t\t\t\treturn runF(&opts)\n   269→\t\t\t}\n   270→\t\t\treturn apiRun(&opts)\n   271→\t\t},\n   272→\t}\n   273→\n   274→\tcmd.Flags().StringVar(&opts.Hostname, \"hostname\", \"\", \"The GitHub hostname for the request (default \\\"github.com\\\")\")\n   275→\tcmd.Flags().StringVarP(&opts.RequestMethod, \"method\", \"X\", \"GET\", \"The HTTP method for the request\")\n   276→\tcmd.Flags().StringArrayVarP(&opts.MagicFields, \"field\", \"F\", nil, \"Add a typed parameter in `key=value` format\")\n   277→\tcmd.Flags().StringArrayVarP(&opts.RawFields, \"raw-field\", \"f\", nil, \"Add a string parameter in `key=value` format\")\n   278→\tcmd.Flags().StringArrayVarP(&opts.RequestHeaders, \"header\", \"H\", nil, \"Add a HTTP request header in `key:value` format\")\n   279→\tcmd.Flags().StringSliceVarP(&opts.Previews, \"preview\", \"p\", nil, \"GitHub API preview `names` to request (without the \\\"-preview\\\" suffix)\")\n   280→\tcmd.Flags().BoolVarP(&opts.ShowResponseHeaders, \"include\", \"i\", false, \"Include HTTP response status line and headers in the output\")\n   281→\tcmd.Flags().BoolVar(&opts.Slurp, \"slurp\", false, \"Use with \\\"--paginate\\\" to return an array of all pages of either JSON arrays or objects\")\n   282→\tcmd.Flags().BoolVar(&opts.Paginate, \"paginate\", false, \"Make additional HTTP requests to fetch all pages of results\")\n   283→\tcmd.Flags().StringVar(&opts.RequestInputFile, \"input\", \"\", \"The `file` to use as body for the HTTP request (use \\\"-\\\" to read from standard input)\")\n   284→\tcmd.Flags().BoolVar(&opts.Silent, \"silent\", false, \"Do not print the response body\")\n   285→\tcmd.Flags().StringVarP(&opts.Template, \"template\", \"t\", \"\", \"Format JSON output using a Go template; see \\\"gh help formatting\\\"\")\n   286→\tcmd.Flags().StringVarP(&opts.FilterOutput, \"jq\", \"q\", \"\", \"Query to select values from the response using jq syntax\")\n   287→\tcmd.Flags().DurationVar(&opts.CacheTTL, \"cache\", 0, \"Cache the response, e.g. \\\"3600s\\\", \\\"60m\\\", \\\"1h\\\"\")\n   288→\tcmd.Flags().BoolVar(&opts.Verbose, \"verbose\", false, \"Include full HTTP request and response in the output\")\n   289→\treturn cmd\n   290→}\n   291→\n   292→func apiRun(opts *ApiOptions) error {\n   293→\tparams, err := parseFields(opts)\n   294→\tif err != nil {\n   295→\t\treturn err\n   296→\t}\n   297→\n   298→\tisGraphQL := opts.RequestPath == \"graphql\"\n   299→\trequestPath, err := fillPlaceholders(opts.RequestPath, opts)\n   300→\tif err != nil {\n   301→\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"unable to expand placeholder in path: %w\", err)\n   302→\t}\n   303→\tmethod := opts.RequestMethod\n   304→\trequestHeaders := opts.RequestHeaders\n   305→\tvar requestBody interface{}\n   306→\tif len(params) > 0 {\n   307→\t\trequestBody = params\n   308→\t}\n   309→\n   310→\tif !opts.RequestMethodPassed && (len(params) > 0 || opts.RequestInputFile != \"\") {\n   311→\t\tmethod = \"POST\"\n   312→\t}\n   313→\n   314→\tif !opts.Silent {\n   315→\t\tif err := opts.IO.StartPager(); err == nil {\n   316→\t\t\tdefer opts.IO.StopPager()\n   317→\t\t} else {\n   318→\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(opts.IO.ErrOut, \"failed to start pager: %v\\n\", err)\n   319→\t\t}\n   320→\t}\n   321→\n   322→\tvar bodyWriter io.Writer = opts.IO.Out\n   323→\tvar headersWriter io.Writer = opts.IO.Out\n   324→\tif opts.Silent {\n   325→\t\tbodyWriter = io.Discard\n   326→\t}\n   327→\tif opts.Verbose {\n   328→\t\t// httpClient handles output when verbose flag is specified.\n   329→\t\tbodyWriter = io.Discard\n   330→\t\theadersWriter = io.Discard\n   331→\t}\n   332→\n   333→\tif opts.Paginate && !isGraphQL {\n   334→\t\trequestPath = addPerPage(requestPath, 100, params)\n   335→\t}\n   336→\n   337→\t// Similar to `jq --slurp`, write all pages JSON arrays or objects into a JSON array.\n   338→\tif opts.Paginate && opts.Slurp {\n   339→\t\tw := &jsonArrayWriter{\n   340→\t\t\tWriter: bodyWriter,\n   341→\t\t\tcolor:  opts.IO.ColorEnabled(),\n   342→\t\t}\n   343→\t\tdefer w.Close()\n   344→\n   345→\t\tbodyWriter = w\n   346→\t}\n   347→\n   348→\tif opts.RequestInputFile != \"\" {\n   349→\t\tfile, size, err := openUserFile(opts.RequestInputFile, opts.IO.In)\n   350→\t\tif err != nil {\n   351→\t\t\treturn err\n   352→\t\t}\n   353→\t\tdefer file.Close()\n   354→\t\trequestPath = addQuery(requestPath, params)\n   355→\t\trequestBody = file\n   356→\t\tif size >= 0 {\n   357→\t\t\trequestHeaders = append([]string{fmt.Sprintf(\"Content-Length: %d\", size)}, requestHeaders...)\n   358→\t\t}\n   359→\t}\n   360→\n   361→\tif len(opts.Previews) > 0 {\n   362→\t\trequestHeaders = append(requestHeaders, \"Accept: \"+previewNamesToMIMETypes(opts.Previews))\n   363→\t}\n   364→\n   365→\tcfg, err := opts.Config()\n   366→\tif err != nil {\n   367→\t\treturn err\n   368→\t}\n   369→\n   370→\tif opts.HttpClient == nil {\n   371→\t\topts.HttpClient = func() (*http.Client, error) {\n   372→\t\t\tlog := opts.IO.ErrOut\n   373→\t\t\tif opts.Verbose {\n   374→\t\t\t\tlog = opts.IO.Out\n   375→\t\t\t}\n   376→\t\t\topts := api.HTTPClientOptions{\n   377→\t\t\t\tAppVersion:     opts.AppVersion,\n   378→\t\t\t\tCacheTTL:       opts.CacheTTL,\n   379→\t\t\t\tConfig:         cfg.Authentication(),\n   380→\t\t\t\tEnableCache:    opts.CacheTTL > 0,\n   381→\t\t\t\tLog:            log,\n   382→\t\t\t\tLogColorize:    opts.IO.ColorEnabled(),\n   383→\t\t\t\tLogVerboseHTTP: opts.Verbose,\n   384→\t\t\t}\n   385→\t\t\treturn api.NewHTTPClient(opts)\n   386→\t\t}\n   387→\t}\n   388→\thttpClient, err := opts.HttpClient()\n   389→\tif err != nil {\n   390→\t\treturn err\n   391→\t}\n   392→\n   393→\thost, _ := cfg.Authentication().DefaultHost()\n   394→\n   395→\tif opts.Hostname != \"\" {\n   396→\t\thost = opts.Hostname\n   397→\t}\n   398→\n   399→\ttmpl := template.New(bodyWriter, opts.IO.TerminalWidth(), opts.IO.ColorEnabled())\n   400→\terr = tmpl.Parse(opts.Template)\n   401→\tif err != nil {\n   402→\t\treturn err\n   403→\t}\n   404→\n   405→\tisFirstPage := true\n   406→\thasNextPage := true\n   407→\tfor hasNextPage {\n   408→\t\tresp, err := httpRequest(httpClient, host, method, requestPath, requestBody, requestHeaders)\n   409→\t\tif err != nil {\n   410→\t\t\treturn err\n   411→\t\t}\n   412→\n   413→\t\tif !isGraphQL {\n   414→\t\t\trequestPath, hasNextPage = findNextPage(resp)\n   415→\t\t\trequestBody = nil // prevent repeating GET parameters\n   416→\t\t}\n   417→\n   418→\t\t// Tell optional jsonArrayWriter to start a new page.\n   419→\t\terr = startPage(bodyWriter)\n   420→\t\tif err != nil {\n   421→\t\t\treturn err\n   422→\t\t}\n   423→\n   424→\t\tendCursor, err := processResponse(resp, opts, bodyWriter, headersWriter, tmpl, isFirstPage, !hasNextPage)\n   425→\t\tif err != nil {\n   426→\t\t\treturn err\n   427→\t\t}\n   428→\t\tisFirstPage = false\n   429→\n   430→\t\tif !opts.Paginate {\n   431→\t\t\tbreak\n   432→\t\t}\n   433→\n   434→\t\tif isGraphQL {\n   435→\t\t\thasNextPage = endCursor != \"\"\n   436→\t\t\tif hasNextPage {\n   437→\t\t\t\tparams[\"endCursor\"] = endCursor\n   438→\t\t\t}\n   439→\t\t}\n   440→\n   441→\t\tif hasNextPage && opts.ShowResponseHeaders {\n   442→\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(opts.IO.Out, \"\\n\")\n   443→\t\t}\n   444→\t}\n   445→\n   446→\treturn tmpl.Flush()\n   447→}\n   448→\n   449→func processResponse(resp *http.Response, opts *ApiOptions, bodyWriter, headersWriter io.Writer, template *template.Template, isFirstPage, isLastPage bool) (endCursor string, err error) {\n   450→\tif opts.ShowResponseHeaders {\n   451→\t\tfmt.Fprintln(headersWriter, resp.Proto, resp.Status)\n   452→\t\tprintHeaders(headersWriter, resp.Header, opts.IO.ColorEnabled())\n   453→\t\tfmt.Fprint(headersWriter, \"\\r\\n\")\n   454→\t}\n   455→\n   456→\tif resp.StatusCode == 204 {\n   457→\t\treturn\n   458→\t}\n   459→\tvar responseBody io.Reader = resp.Body\n   460→\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n   461→\n   462→\tisJSON, _ := regexp.MatchString(`[/+]json(;|$)`, resp.Header.Get(\"Content-Type\"))\n   463→\n   464→\tvar serverError string\n   465→\tif isJSON && (opts.RequestPath == \"graphql\" || resp.StatusCode >= 400) {\n   466→\t\tresponseBody, serverError, err = parseErrorResponse(responseBody, resp.StatusCode)\n   467→\t\tif err != nil {\n   468→\t\t\treturn\n   469→\t\t}\n   470→\t}\n   471→\n   472→\tvar bodyCopy *bytes.Buffer\n   473→\tisGraphQLPaginate := isJSON && resp.StatusCode == 200 && opts.Paginate && opts.RequestPath == \"graphql\"\n   474→\tif isGraphQLPaginate {\n   475→\t\tbodyCopy = &bytes.Buffer{}\n   476→\t\tresponseBody = io.TeeReader(responseBody, bodyCopy)\n   477→\t}\n   478→\n   479→\tif opts.FilterOutput != \"\" && serverError == \"\" {\n   480→\t\t// TODO: reuse parsed query across pagination invocations\n   481→\t\tindent := \"\"\n   482→\t\tif opts.IO.IsStdoutTTY() {\n   483→\t\t\tindent = ttyIndent\n   484→\t\t}\n   485→\t\terr = jq.EvaluateFormatted(responseBody, bodyWriter, opts.FilterOutput, indent, opts.IO.ColorEnabled())\n   486→\t\tif err != nil {\n   487→\t\t\treturn\n   488→\t\t}\n   489→\t} else if opts.Template != \"\" && serverError == \"\" {\n   490→\t\terr = template.Execute(responseBody)\n   491→\t\tif err != nil {\n   492→\t\t\treturn\n   493→\t\t}\n   494→\t} else if isJSON && opts.IO.ColorEnabled() {\n   495→\t\terr = jsoncolor.Write(bodyWriter, responseBody, ttyIndent)\n   496→\t} else {\n   497→\t\tif isJSON && opts.Paginate && !opts.Slurp && !isGraphQLPaginate && !opts.ShowResponseHeaders {\n   498→\t\t\tresponseBody = &paginatedArrayReader{\n   499→\t\t\t\tReader:      responseBody,\n   500→\t\t\t\tisFirstPage: isFirstPage,\n   501→\t\t\t\tisLastPage:  isLastPage,\n   502→\t\t\t}\n   503→\t\t}\n   504→\t\t_, err = io.Copy(bodyWriter, responseBody)\n   505→\t}\n   506→\tif err != nil {\n   507→\t\treturn\n   508→\t}\n   509→\n   510→\tif serverError == \"\" && resp.StatusCode > 299 {\n   511→\t\tserverError = fmt.Sprintf(\"HTTP %d\", resp.StatusCode)\n   512→\t}\n   513→\tif serverError != \"\" {\n   514→\t\tfmt.Fprintf(opts.IO.ErrOut, \"gh: %s\\n\", serverError)\n   515→\t\tif msg := api.ScopesSuggestion(resp); msg != \"\" {\n   516→\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(opts.IO.ErrOut, \"gh: %s\\n\", msg)\n   517→\t\t}\n   518→\t\tif u := factory.SSOURL(); u != \"\" {\n   519→\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(opts.IO.ErrOut, \"Authorize in your web browser: %s\\n\", u)\n   520→\t\t}\n   521→\t\terr = cmdutil.SilentError\n   522→\t\treturn\n   523→\t}\n   524→\n   525→\tif isGraphQLPaginate {\n   526→\t\tendCursor = findEndCursor(bodyCopy)\n   527→\t}\n   528→\n   529→\treturn\n   530→}\n   531→\n   532→var placeholderRE = regexp.MustCompile(`(\\:(owner|repo|branch)\\b|\\{[a-z]+\\})`)\n   533→\n   534→// fillPlaceholders replaces placeholders with values from the current repository\n   535→func fillPlaceholders(value string, opts *ApiOptions) (string, error) {\n   536→\tvar err error\n   537→\treturn placeholderRE.ReplaceAllStringFunc(value, func(m string) string {\n   538→\t\tvar name string\n   539→\t\tif m[0] == ':' {\n   540→\t\t\tname = m[1:]\n   541→\t\t} else {\n   542→\t\t\tname = m[1 : len(m)-1]\n   543→\t\t}\n   544→\n   545→\t\tswitch name {\n   546→\t\tcase \"owner\":\n   547→\t\t\tif baseRepo, e := opts.BaseRepo(); e == nil {\n   548→\t\t\t\treturn baseRepo.RepoOwner()\n   549→\t\t\t} else {\n   550→\t\t\t\terr = e\n   551→\t\t\t}\n   552→\t\tcase \"repo\":\n   553→\t\t\tif baseRepo, e := opts.BaseRepo(); e == nil {\n   554→\t\t\t\treturn baseRepo.RepoName()\n   555→\t\t\t} else {\n   556→\t\t\t\terr = e\n   557→\t\t\t}\n   558→\t\tcase \"branch\":\n   559→\t\t\tif os.Getenv(\"GH_REPO\") != \"\" {\n   560→\t\t\t\terr = errors.New(\"unable to determine an appropriate value for the 'branch' placeholder\")\n   561→\t\t\t\treturn m\n   562→\t\t\t}\n   563→\n   564→\t\t\tif branch, e := opts.Branch(); e == nil {\n   565→\t\t\t\treturn branch\n   566→\t\t\t} else {\n   567→\t\t\t\terr = e\n   568→\t\t\t}\n   569→\t\t}\n   570→\t\treturn m\n   571→\t}), err\n   572→}\n   573→\n   574→func printHeaders(w io.Writer, headers http.Header, colorize bool) {\n   575→\tvar names []string\n   576→\tfor name := range headers {\n   577→\t\tif name == \"Status\" {\n   578→\t\t\tcontinue\n   579→\t\t}\n   580→\t\tnames = append(names, name)\n   581→\t}\n   582→\tsort.Strings(names)\n   583→\n   584→\tvar headerColor, headerColorReset string\n   585→\tif colorize {\n   586→\t\theaderColor = \"\\x1b[1;34m\" // bright blue\n   587→\t\theaderColorReset = \"\\x1b[m\"\n   588→\t}\n   589→\tfor _, name := range names {\n   590→\t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"%s%s%s: %s\\r\\n\", headerColor, name, headerColorReset, strings.Join(headers[name], \", \"))\n   591→\t}\n   592→}\n   593→\n   594→func openUserFile(fn string, stdin io.ReadCloser) (io.ReadCloser, int64, error) {\n   595→\tif fn == \"-\" {\n   596→\t\treturn stdin, -1, nil\n   597→\t}\n   598→\n   599→\tr, err := os.Open(fn)\n   600→\tif err != nil {\n   601→\t\treturn r, -1, err\n   602→\t}\n   603→\n   604→\ts, err := os.Stat(fn)\n   605→\tif err != nil {\n   606→\t\treturn r, -1, err\n   607→\t}\n   608→\n   609→\treturn r, s.Size(), nil\n   610→}\n   611→\n   612→func parseErrorResponse(r io.Reader, statusCode int) (io.Reader, string, error) {\n   613→\tbodyCopy := &bytes.Buffer{}\n   614→\tb, err := io.ReadAll(io.TeeReader(r, bodyCopy))\n   615→\tif err != nil {\n   616→\t\treturn r, \"\", err\n   617→\t}\n   618→\n   619→\tvar parsedBody struct {\n   620→\t\tMessage string\n   621→\t\tErrors  json.RawMessage\n   622→\t}\n   623→\terr = json.Unmarshal(b, &parsedBody)\n   624→\tif err != nil {\n   625→\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n   626→\t}\n   627→\n   628→\tif len(parsedBody.Errors) > 0 && parsedBody.Errors[0] == '\"' {\n   629→\t\tvar stringError string\n   630→\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(parsedBody.Errors, &stringError); err != nil {\n   631→\t\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n   632→\t\t}\n   633→\t\tif stringError != \"\" {\n   634→\t\t\tif parsedBody.Message != \"\" {\n   635→\t\t\t\treturn bodyCopy, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s)\", stringError, parsedBody.Message), nil\n   636→\t\t\t}\n   637→\t\t\treturn bodyCopy, stringError, nil\n   638→\t\t}\n   639→\t}\n   640→\n   641→\tif parsedBody.Message != \"\" {\n   642→\t\treturn bodyCopy, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (HTTP %d)\", parsedBody.Message, statusCode), nil\n   643→\t}\n   644→\n   645→\tif len(parsedBody.Errors) == 0 || parsedBody.Errors[0] != '[' {\n   646→\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", nil\n   647→\t}\n   648→\n   649→\tvar errorObjects []json.RawMessage\n   650→\tif err := json.Unmarshal(parsedBody.Errors, &errorObjects); err != nil {\n   651→\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n   652→\t}\n   653→\n   654→\tvar objectError struct {\n   655→\t\tMessage string\n   656→\t}\n   657→\tvar errors []string\n   658→\tfor _, rawErr := range errorObjects {\n   659→\t\tif len(rawErr) == 0 {\n   660→\t\t\tcontinue\n   661→\t\t}\n   662→\t\tif rawErr[0] == '{' {\n   663→\t\t\terr := json.Unmarshal(rawErr, &objectError)\n   664→\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   665→\t\t\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n   666→\t\t\t}\n   667→\t\t\terrors = append(errors, objectError.Message)\n   668→\t\t} else if rawErr[0] == '\"' {\n   669→\t\t\tvar stringError string\n   670→\t\t\terr := json.Unmarshal(rawErr, &stringError)\n   671→\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   672→\t\t\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n   673→\t\t\t}\n   674→\t\t\terrors = append(errors, stringError)\n   675→\t\t}\n   676→\t}\n   677→\n   678→\tif len(errors) > 0 {\n   679→\t\treturn bodyCopy, strings.Join(errors, \"\\n\"), nil\n   680→\t}\n   681→\n   682→\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", nil\n   683→}\n   684→\n   685→func previewNamesToMIMETypes(names []string) string {\n   686→\ttypes := []string{fmt.Sprintf(\"application/vnd.github.%s-preview+json\", names[0])}\n   687→\tfor _, p := range names[1:] {\n   688→\t\ttypes = append(types, fmt.Sprintf(\"application/vnd.github.%s-preview\", p))\n   689→\t}\n   690→\treturn strings.Join(types, \", \")\n   691→}\n   692→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me search for the `httpRequest` function and understand the full request flow:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "GREP:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "GREP", "arguments": "{\"OUTPUT-MODE\": \"content\", \"pattern\": \"func httpRequest\", \"path\": \"/workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Great! I found the API command implementation. I can see the key function that's relevant to the issue is `parseErrorResponse` at line 612. This is exactly what the hint mentioned. Let me look more closely at this function:\n\n```go\nfunc parseErrorResponse(r io.Reader, statusCode int) (io.Reader, string, error) {\n\tbodyCopy := &bytes.Buffer{}\n\tb, err := io.ReadAll(io.TeeReader(r, bodyCopy))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn r, \"\", err\n\t}\n\n\tvar parsedBody struct {\n\t\tMessage string\n\t\tErrors  json.RawMessage\n\t}\n\terr = json.Unmarshal(b, &parsedBody)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn bodyCopy, \"\", err\n\t}\n\t// ... rest of the function\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is clear now. The `parseErrorResponse` function is called for JSON responses with status codes >= 400 (line 465-467), and it tries to parse the response body as JSON. However, for HEAD requests, the response body is empty even though the Content-Type header indicates JSON. This causes `json.Unmarshal` to fail with \"unexpected end of JSON input\".\n\nThe `httpRequest` function is called at line 408, so I need to find that function as well. Let me also check the `processResponse` function to understand the flow better.\n\nLet me now look for the `httpRequest` function:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" ?>\n<result>\n  <RESULT>/workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api/http.go:func httpRequest(client *http.Client, hostname string, method string, p string, params interface{}, headers []string) (*http.Response, error) {</RESULT>\n</result>", "name": "GREP", "tool_call_id": "GREP:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api/http.go\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Let me read the http.go file to see how HTTP requests are handled:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"1→package api\\n     2→\\n     3→import (\\n     4→\\t\\\"bytes\\\"\\n     5→\\t\\\"encoding/json\\\"\\n     6→\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n     7→\\t\\\"io\\\"\\n     8→\\t\\\"net/http\\\"\\n     9→\\t\\\"net/url\\\"\\n    10→\\t\\\"strconv\\\"\\n    11→\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n    12→\\n    13→\\t\\\"github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/ghinstance\\\"\\n    14→)\\n    15→\\n    16→func httpRequest(client *http.Client, hostname string, method string, p string, params interface{}, headers []string) (*http.Response, error) {\\n    17→\\tisGraphQL := p == \\\"graphql\\\"\\n    18→\\tvar requestURL string\\n    19→\\tif strings.Contains(p, \\\"://\\\") {\\n    20→\\t\\trequestURL = p\\n    21→\\t} else if isGraphQL {\\n    22→\\t\\trequestURL = ghinstance.GraphQLEndpoint(hostname)\\n    23→\\t} else {\\n    24→\\t\\trequestURL = ghinstance.RESTPrefix(hostname) + strings.TrimPrefix(p, \\\"/\\\")\\n    25→\\t}\\n    26→\\n    27→\\tvar body io.Reader\\n    28→\\tvar bodyIsJSON bool\\n    29→\\n    30→\\tswitch pp := params.(type) {\\n    31→\\tcase map[string]interface{}:\\n    32→\\t\\tif strings.EqualFold(method, \\\"GET\\\") {\\n    33→\\t\\t\\trequestURL = addQuery(requestURL, pp)\\n    34→\\t\\t} else {\\n    35→\\t\\t\\tif isGraphQL {\\n    36→\\t\\t\\t\\tpp = groupGraphQLVariables(pp)\\n    37→\\t\\t\\t}\\n    38→\\t\\t\\tb, err := json.Marshal(pp)\\n    39→\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n    40→\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"error serializing parameters: %w\\\", err)\\n    41→\\t\\t\\t}\\n    42→\\t\\t\\tbody = bytes.NewBuffer(b)\\n    43→\\t\\t\\tbodyIsJSON = true\\n    44→\\t\\t}\\n    45→\\tcase io.Reader:\\n    46→\\t\\tbody = pp\\n    47→\\tcase nil:\\n    48→\\t\\tbody = nil\\n    49→\\tdefault:\\n    50→\\t\\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"unrecognized parameters type: %v\\\", params)\\n    51→\\t}\\n    52→\\n    53→\\treq, err := http.NewRequest(strings.ToUpper(method), requestURL, body)\\n    54→\\tif err != nil {\\n    55→\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n    56→\\t}\\n    57→\\n    58→\\tfor _, h := range headers {\\n    59→\\t\\tidx := strings.IndexRune(h, ':')\\n    60→\\t\\tif idx == -1 {\\n    61→\\t\\t\\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"header %q requires a value separated by ':'\\\", h)\\n    62→\\t\\t}\\n    63→\\t\\tname, value := h[0:idx], strings.TrimSpace(h[idx+1:])\\n    64→\\t\\tif strings.EqualFold(name, \\\"Content-Length\\\") {\\n    65→\\t\\t\\tlength, err := strconv.ParseInt(value, 10, 0)\\n    66→\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n    67→\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n    68→\\t\\t\\t}\\n    69→\\t\\t\\treq.ContentLength = length\\n    70→\\t\\t} else {\\n    71→\\t\\t\\treq.Header.Add(name, value)\\n    72→\\t\\t}\\n    73→\\t}\\n    74→\\tif bodyIsJSON && req.Header.Get(\\\"Content-Type\\\") == \\\"\\\" {\\n    75→\\t\\treq.Header.Set(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"application/json; charset=utf-8\\\")\\n    76→\\t}\\n    77→\\tif req.Header.Get(\\\"Accept\\\") == \\\"\\\" {\\n    78→\\t\\treq.Header.Set(\\\"Accept\\\", \\\"*/*\\\")\\n    79→\\t}\\n    80→\\n    81→\\treturn client.Do(req)\\n    82→}\\n    83→\\n    84→func groupGraphQLVariables(params map[string]interface{}) map[string]interface{} {\\n    85→\\ttopLevel := make(map[string]interface{})\\n    86→\\tvariables := make(map[string]interface{})\\n    87→\\n    88→\\tfor key, val := range params {\\n    89→\\t\\tswitch key {\\n    90→\\t\\tcase \\\"query\\\", \\\"operationName\\\":\\n    91→\\t\\t\\ttopLevel[key] = val\\n    92→\\t\\tdefault:\\n    93→\\t\\t\\tvariables[key] = val\\n    94→\\t\\t}\\n    95→\\t}\\n    96→\\n    97→\\tif len(variables) > 0 {\\n    98→\\t\\ttopLevel[\\\"variables\\\"] = variables\\n    99→\\t}\\n   100→\\treturn topLevel\\n   101→}\\n   102→\\n   103→func addQuery(path string, params map[string]interface{}) string {\\n   104→\\tif len(params) == 0 {\\n   105→\\t\\treturn path\\n   106→\\t}\\n   107→\\n   108→\\tquery := url.Values{}\\n   109→\\tif err := addQueryParam(query, \\\"\\\", params); err != nil {\\n   110→\\t\\tpanic(err)\\n   111→\\t}\\n   112→\\n   113→\\tsep := \\\"?\\\"\\n   114→\\tif strings.ContainsRune(path, '?') {\\n   115→\\t\\tsep = \\\"&\\\"\\n   116→\\t}\\n   117→\\treturn path + sep + query.Encode()\\n   118→}\\n   119→\\n   120→func addQueryParam(query url.Values, key string, value interface{}) error {\\n   121→\\tswitch v := value.(type) {\\n   122→\\tcase string:\\n   123→\\t\\tquery.Add(key, v)\\n   124→\\tcase []byte:\\n   125→\\t\\tquery.Add(key, string(v))\\n   126→\\tcase nil:\\n   127→\\t\\tquery.Add(key, \\\"\\\")\\n   128→\\tcase int:\\n   129→\\t\\tquery.Add(key, fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%d\\\", v))\\n   130→\\tcase bool:\\n   131→\\t\\tquery.Add(key, fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%v\\\", v))\\n   132→\\tcase map[string]interface{}:\\n   133→\\t\\tfor subkey, value := range v {\\n   134→\\t\\t\\t// support for nested subkeys can be added here if that is ever necessary\\n   135→\\t\\t\\tif err := addQueryParam(query, subkey, value); err != nil {\\n   136→\\t\\t\\t\\treturn err\\n   137→\\t\\t\\t}\\n   138→\\t\\t}\\n   139→\\tcase []interface{}:\\n   140→\\t\\tfor _, entry := range v {\\n   141→\\t\\t\\tif err := addQueryParam(query, key+\\\"[]\\\", entry); err != nil {\\n   142→\\t\\t\\t\\treturn err\\n   143→\\t\\t\\t}\\n   144→\\t\\t}\\n   145→\\tdefault:\\n   146→\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"unknown type %v\\\", v)\\n   147→\\t}\\n   148→\\treturn nil\\n   149→}\\n   150→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\\n\\n</system-reminder>\"}", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Exploring repository structure to understand codebase organization\", \"content\": \"Explore repository structure to understand codebase organization\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Creating reproduction script to confirm the issue\", \"content\": \"Create reproduction script to confirm the issue\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Locating the parseErrorResponse function and related HTTP request handling code\", \"content\": \"Locate the parseErrorResponse function and related HTTP request handling code\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Implementing fix to handle HEAD requests properly in error responses\", \"content\": \"Implement fix to handle HEAD requests properly in error responses\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix with reproduction script\", \"content\": \"Test the fix with reproduction script\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Running existing tests to ensure no regressions\", \"content\": \"Run existing tests to ensure no regressions\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\", \"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I have a complete understanding of the issue. Let me mark the first todo as completed and move to the next step:\n\nThe issue is in the `processResponse` function in api.go at lines 465-470:\n\n```go\nvar serverError string\nif isJSON && (opts.RequestPath == \"graphql\" || resp.StatusCode >= 400) {\n    responseBody, serverError, err = parseErrorResponse(responseBody, resp.StatusCode)\n    if err != nil {\n        return\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe problem is that for HEAD requests:\n1. The response has status code 404 (for non-existent resources)\n2. The Content-Type header is \"application/json\"\n3. But the response body is empty (as per HTTP HEAD specification)\n4. The `parseErrorResponse` function tries to parse the empty body as JSON, causing \"unexpected end of JSON input\" error\n\nI need to modify this code to handle HEAD requests properly. Let me first create a reproduction script to confirm the issue."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The todos have been successfully updated. Make sure to track your progress with the todo list and, if appropriate, proceed with the current tasks.", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"ls -la | grep -E \\\"(Makefile|go\\\\.mod)\\\"\", \"description\": \"Check build files\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I need to create a reproduction script. I need to understand how the gh CLI can be tested. Let me check if there's a build process or if I can test the CLI directly:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "OUTPUT_TEXT: '-rw-r--r-- 1 test_user test_user  3402 Sep 29 23:22 Makefile\n\n  -rw-r--r-- 1 test_user test_user  7937 Sep 29 23:22 go.mod'", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/Makefile\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Let me check the Makefile to understand how to build the CLI:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "     1→CGO_CPPFLAGS ?= ${CPPFLAGS}\n     2→export CGO_CPPFLAGS\n     3→CGO_CFLAGS ?= ${CFLAGS}\n     4→export CGO_CFLAGS\n     5→CGO_LDFLAGS ?= $(filter -g -L% -l% -O%,${LDFLAGS})\n     6→export CGO_LDFLAGS\n     7→\n     8→EXE =\n     9→ifeq ($(shell go env GOOS),windows)\n    10→EXE = .exe\n    11→endif\n    12→\n    13→## The following tasks delegate to `script/build.go` so they can be run cross-platform.\n    14→\n    15→.PHONY: bin/gh$(EXE)\n    16→bin/gh$(EXE): script/build$(EXE)\n    17→\t@script/build$(EXE) $@\n    18→\n    19→script/build$(EXE): script/build.go\n    20→ifeq ($(EXE),)\n    21→\tGOOS= GOARCH= GOARM= GOFLAGS= CGO_ENABLED= go build -o $@ $<\n    22→else\n    23→\tgo build -o $@ $<\n    24→endif\n    25→\n    26→.PHONY: clean\n    27→clean: script/build$(EXE)\n    28→\t@$< $@\n    29→\n    30→.PHONY: manpages\n    31→manpages: script/build$(EXE)\n    32→\t@$< $@\n    33→\n    34→.PHONY: completions\n    35→completions: bin/gh$(EXE)\n    36→\tmkdir -p ./share/bash-completion/completions ./share/fish/vendor_completions.d ./share/zsh/site-functions\n    37→\tbin/gh$(EXE) completion -s bash > ./share/bash-completion/completions/gh\n    38→\tbin/gh$(EXE) completion -s fish > ./share/fish/vendor_completions.d/gh.fish\n    39→\tbin/gh$(EXE) completion -s zsh > ./share/zsh/site-functions/_gh\n    40→\n    41→# just convenience tasks around `go test`\n    42→.PHONY: test\n    43→test:\n    44→\tgo test ./...\n    45→\n    46→# For more information, see https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/acceptance/README.md\n    47→.PHONY: acceptance\n    48→acceptance:\n    49→\tgo test -tags acceptance ./acceptance\n    50→\n    51→## Site-related tasks are exclusively intended for use by the GitHub CLI team and for our release automation.\n    52→\n    53→site:\n    54→\tgit clone https://github.com/github/cli.github.com.git \"$@\"\n    55→\n    56→.PHONY: site-docs\n    57→site-docs: site\n    58→\tgit -C site pull\n    59→\tgit -C site rm 'manual/gh*.md' 2>/dev/null || true\n    60→\tgo run ./cmd/gen-docs --website --doc-path site/manual\n    61→\trm -f site/manual/*.bak\n    62→\tgit -C site add 'manual/gh*.md'\n    63→\tgit -C site commit -m 'update help docs' || true\n    64→\n    65→.PHONY: site-bump\n    66→site-bump: site-docs\n    67→ifndef GITHUB_REF\n    68→\t$(error GITHUB_REF is not set)\n    69→endif\n    70→\tsed -i.bak -E 's/(assign version = )\".+\"/\\1\"$(GITHUB_REF:refs/tags/v%=%)\"/' site/index.html\n    71→\trm -f site/index.html.bak\n    72→\tgit -C site commit -m '$(GITHUB_REF:refs/tags/v%=%)' index.html\n    73→\n    74→## Install/uninstall tasks are here for use on *nix platform. On Windows, there is no equivalent.\n    75→\n    76→DESTDIR :=\n    77→prefix  := /usr/local\n    78→bindir  := ${prefix}/bin\n    79→datadir := ${prefix}/share\n    80→mandir  := ${datadir}/man\n    81→\n    82→.PHONY: install\n    83→install: bin/gh manpages completions\n    84→\tinstall -d ${DESTDIR}${bindir}\n    85→\tinstall -m755 bin/gh ${DESTDIR}${bindir}/\n    86→\tinstall -d ${DESTDIR}${mandir}/man1\n    87→\tinstall -m644 ./share/man/man1/* ${DESTDIR}${mandir}/man1/\n    88→\tinstall -d ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/bash-completion/completions\n    89→\tinstall -m644 ./share/bash-completion/completions/gh ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/bash-completion/completions/gh\n    90→\tinstall -d ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/fish/vendor_completions.d\n    91→\tinstall -m644 ./share/fish/vendor_completions.d/gh.fish ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/fish/vendor_completions.d/gh.fish\n    92→\tinstall -d ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/zsh/site-functions\n    93→\tinstall -m644 ./share/zsh/site-functions/_gh ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/zsh/site-functions/_gh\n    94→\n    95→.PHONY: uninstall\n    96→uninstall:\n    97→\trm -f ${DESTDIR}${bindir}/gh ${DESTDIR}${mandir}/man1/gh.1 ${DESTDIR}${mandir}/man1/gh-*.1\n    98→\trm -f ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/bash-completion/completions/gh\n    99→\trm -f ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/fish/vendor_completions.d/gh.fish\n   100→\trm -f ${DESTDIR}${datadir}/zsh/site-functions/_gh\n   101→\n   102→.PHONY: macospkg\n   103→macospkg: manpages completions\n   104→ifndef VERSION\n   105→\t$(error VERSION is not set. Use `make macospkg VERSION=vX.Y.Z`)\n   106→endif\n   107→\t./script/release --local \"$(VERSION)\" --platform macos\n   108→\t./script/pkgmacos $(VERSION)\n   109→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"make bin/gh\", \"description\": \"Build the gh CLI binary\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I need to build the CLI to create a test. Let me try building it first:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "GOOS= GOARCH= GOARM= GOFLAGS= CGO_ENABLED= go build -o script/build script/build.go\ngo build -trimpath -ldflags \"-X github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/build.Date=2025-09-29 -X github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/build.Version=v2.66.1-103-gdb9dbfa4c \" -o bin/gh ./cmd/gh", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Write:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/reproduce_issue.go\", \"content\": \"package main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"context\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os/exec\\\"\\n\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\t// Test the issue described in the GitHub issue\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Testing HEAD request issue with gh api...\\\")\\n\\n\\t// Create a context with timeout to prevent hanging\\n\\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 60*time.Second)\\n\\tdefer cancel()\\n\\n\\t// Test case 1: HEAD request to non-existent release (should reproduce the issue)\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"\\\\n1. Testing HEAD request to non-existent release:\\\")\\n\\tcmd1 := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \\\"./bin/gh\\\", \\\"api\\\", \\\"-X\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\", \\\"repos/cli/cli/releases/tags/nonexistent\\\")\\n\\toutput1, err1 := cmd1.CombinedOutput()\\n\\texitCode1 := 0\\n\\tif err1 != nil {\\n\\t\\tif exitError, ok := err1.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\\n\\t\\t\\texitCode1 = exitError.ExitCode\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Error running command: %v\\\\n\\\", err1)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Output: %s\\\\n\\\", strings.TrimSpace(string(output1)))\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Exit code: %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode1)\\n\\n\\tif strings.Contains(string(output1), \\\"unexpected end of JSON input\\\") {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"❌ BUG REPRODUCED: Found 'unexpected end of JSON input' error\\\")\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Println(\\\"✅ No 'unexpected end of JSON input' error found\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t// Test case 2: HEAD request to existing release (should work fine)\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"\\\\n2. Testing HEAD request to existing release:\\\")\\n\\tcmd2 := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \\\"./bin/gh\\\", \\\"api\\\", \\\"-X\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\", \\\"repos/cli/cli/releases/tags/v2.62.0\\\")\\n\\toutput2, err2 := cmd2.CombinedOutput()\\n\\texitCode2 := 0\\n\\tif err2 != nil {\\n\\t\\tif exitError, ok := err2.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\\n\\t\\t\\texitCode2 = exitError.ExitCode\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Error running command: %v\\\\n\\\", err2)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Output: %s\\\\n\\\", strings.TrimSpace(string(output2)))\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Exit code: %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode2)\\n\\n\\t// Test case 3: Regular GET request to non-existent release (for comparison)\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"\\\\n3. Testing GET request to non-existent release (for comparison):\\\")\\n\\tcmd3 := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \\\"./bin/gh\\\", \\\"api\\\", \\\"repos/cli/cli/releases/tags/nonexistent\\\")\\n\\toutput3, err3 := cmd3.CombinedOutput()\\n\\texitCode3 := 0\\n\\tif err3 != nil {\\n\\t\\tif exitError, ok := err3.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\\n\\t\\t\\texitCode3 = exitError.ExitCode\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Error running command: %v\\\\n\\\", err3)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Output: %s\\\\n\\\", strings.TrimSpace(string(output3)))\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"Exit code: %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode3)\\n\\n\\t// Summary\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"\\\\n=== SUMMARY ===\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"HEAD non-existent: exit code %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode1)\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"HEAD existing: exit code %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode2)\\n\\tfmt.Printf(\\\"GET non-existent: exit code %d\\\\n\\\", exitCode3)\\n\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"\\\\nExpected behavior:\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"- HEAD requests should return exit code 0 even for 404 responses\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"- No 'unexpected end of JSON input' errors should occur\\\")\\n}\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Great! Now I have a working CLI binary. Let me create a reproduction script to test the current behavior:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "textresult = File created successfully at: /workspace/cli/reproduce_issue.go\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "Write:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"go run reproduce_issue.go\", \"description\": \"Run reproduction script to confirm the issue\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now let me compile and run the reproduction script to confirm the issue:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# command-line-arguments\n./reproduce_issue.go:6:2: \"os\" imported and not used\n./reproduce_issue.go:27:16: cannot use exitError.ExitCode (value of type func() int) as int value in assignment\n./reproduce_issue.go:50:16: cannot use exitError.ExitCode (value of type func() int) as int value in assignment\n./reproduce_issue.go:67:16: cannot use exitError.ExitCode (value of type func() int) as int value in assignment", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/reproduce_issue.go\", \"old_string\": \"import (\\n\\t\\\"context\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os/exec\\\"\\n\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n\\t\\\"t