"arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api/api.go\", \"old_string\": \"\\tvar serverError string\\n\\tif isJSON && (opts.RequestPath == \\\"graphql\\\" || resp.StatusCode >= 400) {\\n\\t\\tresponseBody, serverError, err = parseErrorResponse(responseBody, resp.StatusCode)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\", \"new_string\": \"\\tvar serverError string\\n\\tif isJSON && (opts.RequestPath == \\\"graphql\\\" || resp.StatusCode >= 400) && resp.Request.Method != \\\"HEAD\\\" {\\n\\t\\tresponseBody, serverError, err = parseErrorResponse(responseBody, resp.StatusCode)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I'll implement the fix. I need to modify the condition on line 465 to exclude HEAD requests from JSON error parsing. The fix should check if the request method is not HEAD:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"The file /workspace/cli/pkg/cmd/api/api.go has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\\n   460→\\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\\n   461→\\n   462→\\tisJSON, _ := regexp.MatchString(`[/+]json(;|$)`, resp.Header.Get(\\\"Content-Type\\\"))\\n   463→\\n   464→\\tvar serverError string\\n   465→\\tif isJSON && (opts.RequestPath == \\\"graphql\\\" || resp.StatusCode >= 400) && resp.Request.Method != \\\"HEAD\\\" {\\n   466→\\t\\tresponseBody, serverError, err = parseErrorResponse(responseBody, resp.StatusCode)\\n   467→\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n   468→\\t\\t\\treturn\\n   469→\\t\\t}\\n   470→\\t}\\n   471→\\n   472→\\tvar bodyCopy *bytes.Buffer\\n   473→\\tisGraphQLPaginate := isJSON && resp.StatusCode == 200 && opts.Paginate && opts.RequestPath == \\\"graphql\\\"\\n   474→\\tif isGraphQLPaginate {\"}", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\