"\\ntype Couple {\\n  Couple(l: Int, r: Int)\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() {\\n  let c1 = Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\n  let c2 = Couple(..c1, r: 1)\\n}\\n\\\"#;\\n\\n    println!(\\\"Checking specific positions:\\\");\\n    println!(\\\"Position 65-67: '{}'\\\", &src[65..67]); // Should be \\\"c1\\\" from \\\"let c1\\\"\\n    println!(\\\"Position 95-97: '{}'\\\", &src[95..97]); // Should be \\\"c2\\\" from \\\"let c2\\\"\\n    println!(\\\"Position 109-111: '{}'\\\", &src[109..111]); // Should be \\\"c1\\\" from \\\"..c1\\\"\\n\\n    println!(\\\"\\\\nFull string with positions marked:\\\");\\n    let chars: Vec<char> = src.chars().collect();\\n    for (i, c) in chars.iter().enumerate() {\\n        if i == 65 || i == 95 || i == 109 {\\n            print!(\\\"[{}]\\\", c);\\n        } else {\\n            print!(\\\"{}\\\", c);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    println!();\\n}\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "CONTENT: File created successfully at: /workspace/gleam/debug_positions2.rs", "name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "Write:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"rustc debug_positions2.rs && ./debug_positions2\", \"description\": \"Check exact characters at the positions\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"RESULT_TEXT\": \"Checking specific positions:\\nPosition 65-67: 'c1'\\nPosition 95-97: 'c2'\\nPosition 109-111: 'c1'\\n\\nFull string with positions marked:\\n\\ntype Couple {\\n  Couple(l: Int, r: Int)\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() {\\n  let [c]1 = Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\n  let [c]2 = Couple(..[c]1, r: 1)\\n}\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\\n\\n</system-reminder>\"}", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I see! Position 109 is indeed the `c1` inside `..c1`. But the debug output shows that this same position is being visited both as:\n\n1. `visit_typed_expr_var` (referring to the usage of `c1` in `..c1`) \n2. `visit_typed_pattern_variable` (which should be for the `c2` pattern, but it's showing the same position)\n\nThis suggests there's something wrong with how the AST is structured or how the visitor is being called. The position 109-111 should only be visited as an expression variable (the usage of `c1`), not as a pattern variable.\n\nI suspect this might be related to how record update syntax is parsed and represented in the AST. Let me focus on the original issue and create a simpler fix that doesn't rely on understanding the exact AST structure.\n\nThe key insight is that the problem described in the issue is that multiple \"Inline variable\" actions are being offered. The original issue says there should be only one correct action, but there are 2-3 actions being offered with some having malformed replacements.\n\nInstead of trying to track definitions, let me take a different approach: ensure we only create one action per variable per position range. Let me revert the debug prints and implement a simpler fix:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/code_action.rs\", \"oldString\": \"pub struct InlineVariable<'a> {\\n    module: &'a Module,\\n    params: &'a CodeActionParams,\\n    edits: TextEdits<'a>,\\n    actions: Vec<CodeAction>,\\n    processed_definition_locations: HashSet<SrcSpan>,\\n}\", \"NEW_STRING\": \"pub struct InlineVariable<'a> {\\n    module: &'a Module,\\n    params: &'a CodeActionParams,\\n    edits: TextEdits<'a>,\\n    actions: Vec<CodeAction>,\\n    processed_combinations: HashSet<(SrcSpan, SrcSpan)>, // (usage_location, definition_location)\\n}\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "type: text\ntext: The file /workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/code_action.rs has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n  4692→}\n  4693→\n  4694→/// Builder for code action to inline a variable.\n  4695→///\n  4696→pub struct InlineVariable<'a> {\n  4697→    module: &'a Module,\n  4698→    params: &'a CodeActionParams,\n  4699→    edits: TextEdits<'a>,\n  4700→    actions: Vec<CodeAction>,\n  4701→    processed_combinations: HashSet<(SrcSpan, SrcSpan)>, // (usage_location, definition_location)\n  4702→}\n  4703→\n  4704→impl<'a> InlineVariable<'a> {\n  4705→    pub fn new(\n  4706→        module: &'a Module,", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/code_action.rs\", \"oldString\": \"    pub fn new(\\n        module: &'a Module,\\n        line_numbers: &'a LineNumbers,\\n        params: &'a CodeActionParams,\\n    ) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            module,\\n            params,\\n            edits: TextEdits::new(line_numbers),\\n            actions: Vec::new(),\\n            processed_definition_locations: HashSet::new(),\\n        }\\n    }\", \"NEW_STRING\": \"    pub fn new(\\n        module: &'a Module,\\n        line_numbers: &'a LineNumbers,\\n        params: &'a CodeActionParams,\\n    ) -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n            module,\\n            params,\\n            edits: TextEdits::new(line_numbers),\\n            actions: Vec::new(),\\n            processed_combinations: HashSet::new(),\\n        }\\n    }\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/code_action.rs has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n  4701→    processed_combinations: HashSet<(SrcSpan, SrcSpan)>, // (usage_location, definition_location)\n  4702→}\n  4703→\n  4704→impl<'a> InlineVariable<'a> {\n  4705→    pub fn new(\n  4706→        module: &'a Module,\n  4707→        line_numbers: &'a LineNumbers,\n  4708→        params: &'a CodeActionParams,\n  4709→    ) -> Self {\n  4710→        Self {\n  4711→            module,\n  4712→            params,\n  4713→            edits: TextEdits::new(line_numbers),\n  4714→            actions: Vec::new(),\n  4715→            processed_combinations: HashSet::new(),\n  4716→        }\n  4717→    }\n  4718→\n  4719→    pub fn code_actions(mut self) -> Vec<CodeAction> {\n  4720→        self.visit_typed_module(&self.module.ast);\n  4721→", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me update the `maybe_inline` method to track combinations of usage and definition locations:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/code_action.rs\", \"oldString\": \"    fn maybe_inline(&mut self, location: SrcSpan) {\\n        // Check if we've already processed this variable definition to avoid duplicates\\n        if !self.processed_definition_locations.insert(location) {\\n            eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: Skipping duplicate definition at {:?}\\\", location);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: Processing definition at {:?}\\\", location);\\n\\n        let variable_location =\\n            match find_variable_references(&self.module.ast, location).as_slice() {\\n                [only_reference] => *only_reference,\\n                _ => {\\n                    eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: Not exactly one reference, skipping\\\");\\n                    return;\\n                },\\n            };\\n\\n        let Some(ast::Statement::Assignment(assignment)) =\\n            self.module.ast.find_statement(location.start)\\n        else {\\n            eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: No assignment found\\\");\\n            return;\\n        };\\n\\n        // If the assignment does not simple bind a variable, for example:\\n        // ```gleam\\n        // let #(first, second, third)\\n        // io.println(first)\\n        // //         ^ Inline here\\n        // ```\\n        // We can't inline it.\\n        if !matches!(assignment.pattern, Pattern::Variable { .. }) {\\n            eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: Pattern is not a variable\\\");\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        let value_location = assignment.value.location();\\n        let value = self\\n            .module\\n            .code\\n            .get(value_location.start as usize..value_location.end as usize)\\n            .expect(\\\"Span is valid\\\");\\n\\n        eprintln!(\\\"DEBUG: Creating inline action for value: {}\\\", value);\\n\\n        self.edits.replace(variable_location, value.into());\\n\\n        let mut location = assignment.location;\\n\\n        let chars = self.module.code.chars();\\n        let mut chars = chars.skip(assignment.location.end as usize);\\n        // Delete any whitespace after the removed statement\\n        while chars.next().is_some_and(char::is_whitespace) {\\n            location.end += 1;\\n        }\\n\\n        self.edits.delete(location);\\n\\n        CodeActionBuilder::new(\\\"Inline variable\\\")\\n            .kind(CodeActionKind::REFACTOR_INLINE)\\n            .changes(\\n                self.params.text_document.uri.clone(),\\n                std::mem::take(&mut self.edits.edits),\\n            )\\n            .preferred(false)\\n            .push_to(&mut self.actions);\\n    }\", \"NEW_STRING\": \"    fn maybe_inline(&mut self, usage_location: SrcSpan, definition_location: SrcSpan) {\\n        // Check if we've already processed this combination to avoid duplicates\\n        if !self.processed_combinations.insert((usage_location, definition_location)) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        let variable_location =\\n            match find_variable_references(&self.module.ast, definition_location).as_slice() {\\n                [only_reference] => *only_reference,\\n                _ => return,\\n            };\\n\\n        let Some(ast::Statement::Assignment(assignment)) =\\n            self.module.ast.find_statement(definition_location.start)\\n        else {\\n            return;\\n        };\\n\\n        // If the assignment does not simple bind a variable, for example:\\n        // ```gleam\\n        // let #(first, second, third)\\n        // io.println(first)\\n        // //         ^ Inline here\\n        // ```\\n        // We can't inline it.\\n        if !matches!(assignment.pattern, Pattern::Variable { .. }) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        let value_location = assignment.value.location();\\n        let value = self\\n            .module\\n            .code\\n            .get(value_location.start as usize..value_location.end as usize)\\n            .expect(\\\"Span is valid\\\");\\n\\n        self.edits.replace(variable_location, value.into());\\n\\n        let mut location = assignment.location;\\n\\n        let chars = self.module.code.chars();\\n        let mut chars = chars.skip(assignment.location.end as usize);\\n        // Delete any whitespace after the removed statement\\n        while chars.next().is_some_and(char::is_whitespace) {\\n            location.end += 1;\\n        }\\n\\n        self.edits.delete(location);\\n\\n        CodeActionBuilder::new(\\\"Inline variable\\\")\\n            .kind(CodeActionKind::REFACTOR_INLINE)\\n            .changes(\\n                self.params.text_document.uri.clone(),\\n                std::mem::take(&mut self.edits.edits),\\n            )\\n            .preferred(false)\\n            .push_to(&mut self.actions);\\n    }\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "RESULT: \"The file /workspa