*\"Found 1 inline variable actions\"** instead of 2. The fix is working! The remaining action is the correct one that replaces `c1` with `Couple(l: 1, r: 1)` and deletes the `c1` definition.\n\nLet me now create a proper test and verify it works:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/tests/action.rs\", \"oldString\": \"#[test]\\nfn inline_variable_in_record_update_actions_inspection() {\\n    let src = r#\\\"\\ntype Couple {\\n  Couple(l: Int, r: Int)\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() {\\n  let c1 = Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\n  let c2 = Couple(..c1, r: 1)\\n}\\n\\\"#;\\n    let project = TestProject::for_source(src);\\n    let range = find_position_of(\\\"c1\\\").nth_occurrence(2).to_selection().find_range(src);\\n    let actions = code_actions(project, range).unwrap_or_default();\\n\\n    println!(\\\"All actions available:\\\");\\n    for (i, action) in actions.iter().enumerate() {\\n        println!(\\\"Action {}: {}\\\", i, action.title);\\n        if let Some(edit) = &action.edit {\\n            if let Some(changes) = &edit.changes {\\n                for (uri, edits) in changes {\\n                    println!(\\\"  URI: {}\\\", uri);\\n                    for edit in edits {\\n                        println!(\\\"    Edit: {:?} -> {:?}\\\", edit.range, edit.new_text);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    let inline_actions: Vec<_> = actions.into_iter()\\n        .filter(|action| action.title == INLINE_VARIABLE)\\n        .collect();\\n\\n    println!(\\\"Found {} inline variable actions\\\", inline_actions.len());\\n    for (i, action) in inline_actions.iter().enumerate() {\\n        println!(\\\"Inline action {}: {:?}\\\", i, action);\\n    }\\n\\n    // This test is for inspection - it will currently fail but shows us what's happening\\n    // assert_eq!(inline_actions.len(), 1, \\\"Expected exactly 1 inline variable action, got {}\\\", inline_actions.len());\\n}\", \"NEW_STRING\": \"#[test]\\nfn inline_variable_in_record_update_single_action() {\\n    let src = r#\\\"\\ntype Couple {\\n  Couple(l: Int, r: Int)\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() {\\n  let c1 = Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\n  let c2 = Couple(..c1, r: 1)\\n}\\n\\\"#;\\n    let project = TestProject::for_source(src);\\n    let range = find_position_of(\\\"c1\\\").nth_occurrence(2).to_selection().find_range(src);\\n    let actions = code_actions(project, range).unwrap_or_default();\\n    let inline_actions: Vec<_> = actions.into_iter()\\n        .filter(|action| action.title == INLINE_VARIABLE)\\n        .collect();\\n\\n    // Should only have exactly 1 inline variable action, not multiple\\n    assert_eq!(inline_actions.len(), 1, \\\"Expected exactly 1 inline variable action, got {}\\\", inline_actions.len());\\n\\n    // Verify the action is correct - it should replace c1 with Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\n    let action = &inline_actions[0];\\n    let edit = action.edit.as_ref().unwrap();\\n    let changes = edit.changes.as_ref().unwrap();\\n    let text_edits: Vec<_> = changes.values().flatten().collect();\\n\\n    // Should have exactly 2 text edits: replace the usage and delete the definition\\n    assert_eq!(text_edits.len(), 2);\\n\\n    // Find the replacement edit (the one that replaces c1 with the value)\\n    let replacement_edit = text_edits.iter()\\n        .find(|edit| edit.new_text == \\\"Couple(l: 1, r: 1)\\\")\\n        .expect(\\\"Should have replacement edit\\\");\\n\\n    // Verify it replaces at the correct position (c1 in ..c1)\\n    assert_eq!(replacement_edit.range.start.line, 7);\\n    assert_eq!(replacement_edit.range.start.character, 20);\\n}\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/gleam/compiler-core/src/language_server/tests/action.rs has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n  5715→        find_position_of(\"message\").nth_occur