e context around that to see where to add c_char16_t:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "   360→ctype_wrapper!(c_int, \"c_int\", \"Newtype wrapper for an int\");\n   361→ctype_wrapper!(c_uchar, \"c_uchar\", \"Newtype wrapper for an unsigned char\");\n   362→\n   363→/// Newtype wrapper for a C void. Only useful as a `*c_void`\n   364→#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n   365→#[repr(transparent)]\n   366→pub struct c_void(pub ::std::os::raw::c_void);\n   367→\n   368→/// # Safety\n   369→///\n   370→/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\n   371→/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\n   372→unsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_void {\n   373→    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_void);\n   374→    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\n   375→}\n   376→\n   377→/// autocxx couldn't generate these bindings.\n   378→/// If you come across a method, type or function which refers to this type,\n   379→/// it indicates that autocxx couldn't generate that binding. A documentation\n   380→/// comment should be attached indicating the reason.\n   381→pub struct BindingGenerationFailure {\n   382→    _unallocatable: [*const u8; 0],\n   383→    _pinned: core::marker::PhantomData<core::marker::PhantomPinned>,\n   384→}\n   385→\n   386→/// Tools to export Rust code to C++.\n   387→// These are in a mod to avoid shadowing the definitions of the\n   388→// directives above, which, being macro_rules, are unavoidably\n   389→// in the crate root but must be function-style macros to keep\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/autocxx/src/lib.rs\", \"oldstring\": \"/// Newtype wrapper for a C void. Only useful as a `*c_void`\\n#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\\n#[repr(transparent)]\\npub struct c_void(pub ::std::os::raw::c_void);\\n\\n/// # Safety\\n///\\n/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\\n/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\\nunsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_void {\\n    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_void);\\n    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\\n}\\n\\n/// autocxx couldn't generate these bindings.\", \"newstring\": \"/// Newtype wrapper for a C void. Only useful as a `*c_void`\\n#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\\n#[repr(transparent)]\\npub struct c_void(pub ::std::os::raw::c_void);\\n\\n/// # Safety\\n///\\n/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\\n/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\\nunsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_void {\\n    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_void);\\n    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\\n}\\n\\n/// A C++ `char16_t`\\n#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\\n#[repr(transparent)]\\npub struct c_char16_t(pub u16);\\n\\n/// # Safety\\n///\\n/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\\n/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\\nunsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_char16_t {\\n    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_char16_t);\\n    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\\n}\\n\\n/// autocxx couldn't generate these bindings.\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Perfect! I'll add the c_char16_t type right after the c_void type. Let me add it:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/autocxx/src/lib.rs has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n   359→ctype_wrapper!(c_uint, \"c_uint\", \"Newtype wrapper for an unsigned int\");\n   360→ctype_wrapper!(c_int, \"c_int\", \"Newtype wrapper for an int\");\n   361→ctype_wrapper!(c_uchar, \"c_uchar\", \"Newtype wrapper for an unsigned char\");\n   362→\n   363→/// Newtype wrapper for a C void. Only useful as a `*c_void`\n   364→#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n   365→#[repr(transparent)]\n   366→pub struct c_void(pub ::std::os::raw::c_void);\n   367→\n   368→/// # Safety\n   369→///\n   370→/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\n   371→/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\n   372→unsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_void {\n   373→    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_void);\n   374→    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\n   375→}\n   376→\n   377→/// A C++ `char16_t`\n   378→#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n   379→#[repr(transparent)]\n   380→pub struct c_char16_t(pub u16);\n   381→\n   382→/// # Safety\n   383→///\n   384→/// We assert that the namespace and type ID refer to a C++\n   385→/// type which is equivalent to this Rust type.\n   386→unsafe impl cxx::ExternType for c_char16_t {\n   387→    type Id = cxx::type_id!(c_char16_t);\n   388→    type Kind = cxx::kind::Trivial;\n   389→}\n   390→\n   391→/// autocxx couldn't generate these bindings.\n   392→/// If you come across a method, type or function which refers to this type,\n   393→/// it indicates that autocxx couldn't generate that binding. A documentation\n   394→/// comment should be attached indicating the reason.\n   395→pub struct BindingGenerationFailure {", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Understanding char16_t handling\", \"content\": \"Understand how char16_t is currently handled by bindgen and autocxx\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Checking existing fix\", \"content\": \"Check if existing fix is applied\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Adding c_char16_t to known_types.rs\", \"content\": \"Add c_char16_t to known_types database\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Defining c_char16_t type in src/lib.rs\", \"content\": \"Define c_char16_t type in src/lib.rs\", \"status\": \