oc, \"cannot decompose class type %qT without non-static \"\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n |", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "grep:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "grep", "arguments": "{\"-n\": true, \"Outputmode\": \"content\", \"path\": \"/home/gcc/gcc/cp/decl.cc\", \"pattern\": \"^start_cleanup_fn \\\\(\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "I need to find the `start_cleanup_fn` function. Let me search for it more specifically:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "10374:start_cleanup_fn (tree decl, bool ob_parm)", "name": "grep", "tool_call_id": "grep:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/home/gcc/gcc/cp/decl.cc\", \"Limit\": 80, \"OFFSET\": 10374}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Found it! Let me read it:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"contentResult\": \"10374→start_cleanup_fn (tree decl, bool ob_parm)\\n 10375→{\\n 10376→  push_to_top_level ();\\n 10377→\\n 10378→  /* No need to mangle this.  */\\n 10379→  push_lang_context (lang_name_c);\\n 10380→\\n 10381→  /* Build the name of the function.  */\\n 10382→  gcc_checking_assert (HAS_DECL_ASSEMBLER_NAME_P (decl));\\n 10383→  const char *dname = IDENTIFIER_POINTER (DECL_ASSEMBLER_NAME (decl));\\n 10384→  dname = targetm.strip_name_encoding (dname);\\n 10385→  char *name = ACONCAT ((\\\"__tcf\\\", dname, NULL));\\n 10386→\\n 10387→  tree fntype = TREE_TYPE (ob_parm ? get_cxa_atexit_fn_ptr_type ()\\n 10388→\\t\\t\\t\\t   : get_atexit_fn_ptr_type ());\\n 10389→  /* Build the function declaration.  */\\n 10390→  tree fndecl = build_lang_decl (FUNCTION_DECL, get_identifier (name), fnt