tfound := false\r\n\tfor _, name := range HelpFlag.Names() {  // !!!!!!!!!  PANIC here\r\n\t\tif cCtx.Bool(name) {\r\n```\r\n\r\n## To reproduce\r\n\r\n```golang\r\npackage main\r\n\r\nimport (\r\n\t\"github.com/urfave/cli/v2\"\r\n\t\"os\"\r\n)\r\n\r\nfunc main() {\r\n\tcli.HelpFlag = nil\r\n\tapp := cli.NewApp()\r\n\t_ = app.Run(os.Args)\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen panic:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/go/pkg/mod/github.com/urfave/cli/v2@v2.25.7/help.go:419 \r\n```\n\n</github_issue>\n\nCan you help me implement the necessary changes is this repository to fix the <github_issue>?\nYour task is to make the minimal changes to non-tests files to ensure the <github_issue> is satisfied. You MUST NOT modify the testing logic or any of the test files in any way!\n\nIMPORTANT TIP:\nFollow these steps to resolve the issue:\n1. As a first step, it might be a good idea to explore the repo to familiarize yourself with its structure.\n2. Create a script (e.g., 'reproduce_issue.go') to reproduce the error and execute it to confirm the error\n  2.1 reproduce_issue.go script finishes quickly after checking the error, fix etc. There no long running background servers for django for instance etc. It should be a quick script which checks the error and fix to provide a visible response.\n  2.2 SUPER IMPORTANT: to ensure this reproduce_issue.go must have a timeout logic. If the script runs for more than 60 seconds, it should output a timeout message and you can interpret accordingly.\n  2.3 SUPER IMPORTANT: It's a good idea to mock heavy services, only focus on the main logic of the issue.\n3. Edit the sourcecode of the repo to resolve the issue\n4. Rerun your reproduce script and confirm that the error is fixed!\n5. Think about edgecases and make sure your fix handles them as well\n6. Remember to clean up the repo, delete unrelated files you wrote (e.g. reproduce script)\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: each response must include both reasoning and function call to solve the task.\nYou are being told a million times, e