ory structure to understand the codebase\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Creating a reproduction script to confirm the panic issue\", \"content\": \"Create a reproduction script to confirm the panic issue\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Analyzing the help.go file and identifying the root cause\", \"content\": \"Analyze the help.go file and identify the root cause\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Implementing the fix to handle nil HelpFlag\", \"content\": \"Implement the fix to handle nil HelpFlag\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix with the reproduction script\", \"content\": \"Test the fix with the reproduction script\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Checking edge cases and running existing tests\", \"content\": \"Check edge cases and run existing tests\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\", \"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "type=text\ntext=The todos were changed successfully. It's important to continue using the todo list for progress tracking. Proceed with your current tasks if they are still applicable.", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"go test -run TestHelpFlagNilPanic -v\", \"description\": \"Run test to verify the fix works\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "=== RUN   TestHelpFlagNilPanic\n=== RUN   TestHelpFlagNilPanic/Direct_checkHelp_call\n=== RUN   TestHelpFlagNilPanic/Full_app_run\nIncorrect Usage: flag: help requested\n\nNAME:\n   cli.test - A new cli application\n\nUSAGE:\n   cli.test  command [command options] [arguments...]\n\nCOMMANDS:\n   help, h  Shows a list of commands or help for one command\n--- PASS: TestHelpFlagNilPanic (0.00s)\n    --- PASS: TestHelpFlagNilPanic/Direct_checkHelp_call (0.00s)\n    --- PASS: TestHelpFlagNilPanic/Full_app_run (0.00s)\nPASS\nok  \tgithub.com/urfave/cli/v2\t0.054s", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent! The fix works. Both the direct `checkHelp` call and the full app run now pass without panicking. Let me also test the existing test that was already in the codebase:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"go test -run TestAppNoHelpFlag -v\", \"description\": \"Ensure existing test still passes\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Output_Text==== RUN   TestAppNoHelpFlag\n--- PASS: TestAppNoHelpFlag (0.00s)\nPASS\nok  \tgithub.com/urfave/cli/v2\t0.003s", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me also add a test for VersionFlag = nil to make sure the same fix works there:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/cli/reproduce_issue_test.go\", \"OLDString\": \"func TestHelpFlagNilPanic(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t// Store the original HelpFlag\\n\\toriginalHelpFlag := HelpFlag\\n\\n\\t// Restore it after the test\\n\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\tHelpFlag = originalHelpFlag\\n\\t}()\\n\\n\\t// Test 1: Direct call to checkHelp function\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"Direct checkHelp call\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t\\tpanicOccurred := false\\n\\n\\t\\tfunc() {\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif r := recover(); r != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tpanicOccurred = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tt.Logf(\\\"PANIC REPRODUCED in direct checkHelp call: %v\\\", r)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Set HelpFlag to nil as described in the issue\\n\\t\\t\\tHelpFlag = nil\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Create a minimal context and call checkHelp directly\\n\\t\\t\\tapp := NewApp()\\n\\t\\t\\tcCtx := NewContext(app, nil, nil)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This should cause the panic\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = checkHelp(cCtx)\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tif panicOccurred {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Error(\\\"Panic occurred when calling checkHelp with HelpFlag=nil\\\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\t// Test 2: Full app run\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"Full app run\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t\\tpanicOccurred := false\\n\\n\\t\\tfunc() {\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif r := recover(); r != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tpanicOccurred = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tt.Logf(\\\"PANIC REPRODUCED in app run: %v\\\", r)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Set HelpFlag to nil as described in the issue\\n\\t\\t\\tHelpFlag = nil\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Create a new app exactly as in the issue report\\n\\t\\t\\tapp := NewApp()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This should trigger the panic\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = app.Run([]string{\\\"test-app\\\", \\\"--help\\\"})\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tif panicOccurred {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Error(\\\"Panic occurred when running app with HelpFlag=nil\\\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t})\\n}\", \"NewString\": \"func TestHelpFlagNilPanic(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t// Store the original HelpFlag\\n\\toriginalHelpFlag := HelpFlag\\n\\n\\t// Restore it after the test\\n\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\tHelpFlag = originalHelpFlag\\n\\t}()\\n\\n\\t// Test 1: Direct call to checkHelp function\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"Direct checkHelp call\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t\\tpanicOccurred := false\\n\\n\\t\\tfunc() {\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif r := recover(); r != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tpanicOccurred = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tt.Logf(\\\"PANIC REPRODUCED in direct checkHelp call: %v\\\", r)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Set HelpFlag to nil as described in the issue\\n\\t\\t\\tHelpFlag = nil\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Create a minimal context and call checkHelp directly\\n\\t\\t\\tapp := NewApp()\\n\\t\\t\\tcCtx := NewContext(app, nil, nil)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This should cause the panic\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = checkHelp(cCtx)\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tif panicOccurred {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Error(\\\"Panic occurred when calling checkHelp with HelpFlag=nil\\\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\t// Test 2: Full app run\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"Full app run\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t\\tpanicOccurred := false\\n\\n\\t\\tfunc() {\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif r := recover(); r != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tpanicOccurred = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tt.Logf(\\\"PANIC REPRODUCED in app run: %v\\\", r)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Set HelpFlag to nil as described in the issue\\n\\t\\t\\tHelpFlag = nil\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Create a new app exactly as in the issue report\\n\\t\\t\\tapp := NewApp()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This should trigger the panic\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = app.Run([]string{\\\"test-app\\\", \\\"--help\\\"})\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tif panicOccurred {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Error(\\\"Panic occurred when running app with HelpFlag=nil\\\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t})\\n}\\n\\nfunc TestVersionFlagNilPanic(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t// Store the original VersionFlag\\n\\toriginalVersionFlag := VersionFlag\\n\\n\\t// Restore it after the test\\n\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\tVersionFlag = originalVersionFlag\\n\\t}()\\n\\n\\t// Test: Direct call to checkVersion function\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"Direct checkVersion call\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\t\\tpanicOccurred := false\\n\\n\\t\\tfunc() {\\n\\t\\t\\tdefer func() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif r := recover(); r != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tpanicOccurred = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tt.Logf(\\\"PANIC REPRODUCED in direct checkVersion call: %v\\\", r)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Set VersionFlag to nil for consistency with HelpFlag pattern\\n\\t\\t\\tVersionFlag = nil\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// Create a minimal context and call checkVersion directly\\n\\t\\t\\tapp := NewApp()\\n\\t\\t\\tcCtx := NewContext(app, nil, nil)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// This should not cause a panic\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = checkVersion(cCtx)\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tif panicOccurred {\\n\\t\\t\\tt.Error(\\\"Panic occurred when calling checkVersion with VersionFlag=nil\\\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t})\\n}\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "CONTENT: \"The file /workspace/cli/reproduce_issue_test.go has be