  data.urlIndex(i);\\n        } else if (!isHttpAnnotation) {\\n          checkState(data.formParams().isEmpty(),\\n              \\\"Body parameters cannot be used with form parameters.\\\");\\n          checkState(data.bodyIndex() == null, \\\"Method has too many Body parameters: %s\\\", method);\\n          data.bodyIndex(i);\\n          data.bodyType(Types.resolve(targetType, targetType, genericParameterTypes[i]));\\n        }\\n      }\", \"new-string\": \"      Annotation[][] parameterAnnotations = method.getParameterAnnotations();\\n      int count = parameterAnnotations.length;\\n      for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n        boolean isHttpAnnotation = false;\\n        if (parameterAnnotations[i] != null) {\\n          isHttpAnnotation = processAnnotationsOnParameter(data, parameterAnnotations[i], i);\\n        }\\n        if (parameterTypes[i] == URI.class) {\\n          data.urlIndex(i);\\n        } else if (parameterTypes[i] == Request.Options.class) {\\n          data.optionsIndex(i);\\n        } else if (!isHttpAnnotation) {\\n          checkState(data.formParams().isEmpty(),\\n              \\\"Body parameters cannot be used with form parameters.\\\");\\n          checkState(data.bodyIndex() == null, \\\"Method has too many Body parameters: %s\\\", method);\\n          data.bodyIndex(i);\\n          data.bodyType(Types.resolve(targetType, targetType, genericParameterTypes[i]));\\n        }\\n      }\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I need to modify the Contract.BaseContract to detect Request.Options parameters. Looking at lines 102-121 in Contract.java, I need to add logic to detect when a parameter is of type Request.Options and set the optionsIndex.\n\nThe logic should be similar to how URI.class is detected:\n- If parameterTypes[i] == Request.Options.class, then set data.optionsIndex(i)\n- This should be checked before other checks, and marked as isHttpAnnotation so it's not treated as a body parameter"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"TEXT_RESULT\": \"The file /workspace/feign/core/src/main/java/feign/Contract.java has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\\n   101→          method.getName());\\n   102→      Class<?>[] parameterTypes = method.getParameterTypes();\\n   103→      Type[] genericParameterTypes = method.getGenericParameterTypes();\\n   104→\\n   105→      Annotation[][] parameterAnnotations = method.getParameterAnnotations();\\n   106→      int count = parameterAnnotations.length;\\n   107→      for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n   108→        boolean isHttpAnnotation = false;\\n   109→        if (parameterAnnotations[i] != null) {\\n   110→          isHttpAnnotation = processAnnotationsOnParameter(data, parameterAnnotations[i], i);\\n   111→        }\\n   112→        if (parameterTypes[i] == URI.class) {\\n   113→          data.urlIndex(i);\\n   114→        } else if (parameterTypes[i] == Request.Options.class) {\\n   115→          data.optionsIndex(i);\\n   116→        } else if (!isHttpAnnotation) {\\n   117→          checkState(data.formParams().isEmpty(),\\n   118→              \\\"Body parameters cannot be used with form parameters.\\\");\\n   119→          checkState(data.bodyIndex() == null, \\\"Method has too many Body parameters: %s\\\", method);\\n   120→          data.bodyIndex(i);\\n   121→          data.bodyType(Types.resolve(targetType, targetType, genericParameterTypes[i]));\\n   122→        }\\n   123→      }\\n   124→\\n   125→      if (data.headerMapIndex() != null) {\\n   126→        checkMapString(\\\"HeaderMap\\\", parameterTypes[data.headerMapIndex()],\\n   127→            genericParameterTypes[data.headerMapIndex()]);\"}", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Adding optionsIndex field to MethodMetadata\", \"content\": \"Add optionsIndex field to MethodMetadata\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Modifying Contract to detect Request.Options parameters\", \"content\": \"Modify Contract to detect Request.Options parameters\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Updating BuildTemplateByResolvingArgs to track Options\", \"content\": \"Update BuildTemplateByResolvingArgs to track Options\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Modifying SynchronousMethodHandler to use per-request options\", \"content\": \"Modify SynchronousMethodHandler to use per-request options\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the implementation\", \"content\": \"Test the implementation\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Good! Now let me mark this task as completed and move on to the next one. Now I need to modify the BuildTemplateByResolvingArgs to track the options from the method arguments.\n\nActually, looking back at the architecture, I realize that BuildTemplateByResolvingArgs creates RequestTemplates, but the options need to be passed to the SynchronousMethodHandler.executeAndDecode method. \n\nThe flow is:\n1. SynchronousMethodHandler.invoke(Object[] argv) is called\n2. It calls buildTemplateFromArgs.create(argv) to create a RequestTemplate\n3. It calls executeAndDecode(template) which uses the instance-level `options` field\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Make SynchronousMethodHandler.invoke extract the options from argv if optionsIndex is set\n2. Pass those options to executeAndDecode\n3. Modify executeAndDecode to accept options as a parameter\n\nLet me look at SynchronousMethodHandler again to understand the flow better."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Having successfully modified the todos, please proceed with current tasks if they are relevant and continue to utilize the todo list to monitor your progress.", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function":