is to:\n\n1. Store the MethodMetadata in SynchronousMethodHandler (it's already there - line 34)\n2. In the invoke method, check if metadata.optionsIndex() is set\n3. If it is, extract the options from argv[metadata.optionsIndex()]\n4. Use those options instead of the default options when calling executeAndDecode\n\nLet me modify SynchronousMethodHandler:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/feign/core/src/main/java/feign/SynchronousMethodHandler.java has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    68→    this.closeAfterDecode = closeAfterDecode;\n    69→    this.propagationPolicy = propagationPolicy;\n    70→  }\n    71→\n    72→  @Override\n    73→  public Object invoke(Object[] argv) throws Throwable {\n    74→    RequestTemplate template = buildTemplateFromArgs.create(argv);\n    75→    Options options = this.options;\n    76→    if (metadata.optionsIndex() != null) {\n    77→      options = (Options) argv[metadata.optionsIndex()];\n    78→    }\n    79→    Retryer retryer = this.retryer.clone();\n    80→    while (true) {\n    81→      try {\n    82→        return executeAndDecode(template, options);\n    83→      } catch (RetryableException e) {\n    84→        try {\n    85→          retryer.continueOrPropagate(e);\n    86→        } catch (RetryableException th) {\n    87→          Throwable cause = th.getCause();\n    88→          if (propagationPolicy == UNWRAP && cause != null) {\n    89→            throw cause;\n    90→          } else {\n    91→            throw th;\n    92→          }\n    93→        }\n    94→        if (logLevel != Logger.Level.NONE) {\n    95→          logger.logRetry(metadata.configKey(), logLevel);\n    96→        }\n    97→        continue;\n    98→      }\n    99→    }\n   100→  }\n   101→\n   102→  Object executeAndDecode(RequestTemplate template) throws Throwable {\n   103→    Request request = targetRequest(template);\n   104→", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit: