ent work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\\n\\n</system-reminder>\"}", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/vue-router/src/util/params.js\", \"Old_String\": \"export function fillParams (\\n  path: string,\\n  params: ?Object,\\n  routeMsg: string\\n): string {\\n  try {\\n    const filler =\\n      regexpCompileCache[path] ||\\n      (regexpCompileCache[path] = Regexp.compile(path))\\n    return filler(params || {}, { pretty: true })\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {\\n      warn(false, `missing param for ${routeMsg}: ${e.message}`)\\n    }\\n    return ''\\n  }\\n}\", \"newstring\": \"export function fillParams (\\n  path: string,\\n  params: ?Object,\\n  routeMsg: string\\n): string {\\n  // Normalize asterisk to named parameter to avoid unnamed param issues\\n  const normalizedPath = path.replace(/\\\\*/g, ':pathMatch(.*)')\\n  try {\\n    const filler =\\n      regexpCompileCache[normalizedPath] ||\\n      (regexpCompileCache[normalizedPath] = Regexp.compile(normalizedPath))\\n    return filler(params || {}, { pretty: true })\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {\\n      warn(false, `missing param for ${routeMsg}: ${e.message}`)\\n    }\\n    return ''\\n  }\\n}\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now let me modify the approach. Since the path is stored with `*`, I need to normalize it when it's used with fillParams. Let me modify the fillParams function to normalize asterisks before compiling."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/vue-router/src/util/params.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n     7→const regexpCompileCache: {\n     8→  [key: string]: Function\n     9→} = Object.create(null)\n    10→\n    11→export function fillParams (\n   