guments": "{\"todos\": [{\"content\": \"Explore the repository to understand its structure\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"activeForm\": \"Exploring the repository\"}, {\"content\": \"Create reproduce_issue.js script to confirm the bug\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"activeForm\": \"Creating reproduce_issue.js script\"}, {\"content\": \"Understand how parseArray works and where scoping happens\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"activeForm\": \"Understanding parseArray implementation\"}, {\"content\": \"Fix the scoping issue in array environments\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"activeForm\": \"Fixing scoping issue\"}, {\"content\": \"Test the fix with reproduce script\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix\"}, {\"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\"}]}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Good! I found the test. Let me read around line 3146-3160 to see the TODO comment."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "  3145→\n  3146→    it(\"array cells generate groups\", () => {\n  3147→        expect`\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\x&\\def\\x{2}\\x&\\x\\end{matrix}`\n  3148→            .toParseLike`\\begin{matrix}1&2&1\\end{matrix}`;\n  3149→    });\n  3150→\n  3151→    // TODO: This doesn't yet work; before the environment gets called,\n  3152→    // {matrix} gets consumed which means that the \\def gets executed, before\n  3153→    // we can create a group. :-(  Issue #1989\n  3154→    /*\n  3155→    it(\"array cells generate groups\", () => {\n  3156→        expect`\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}`\n  3157→            .toParseLike`\\begin{matrix}&1\\end{matrix}`;\n  3158→    });\n  3159→    */\n  3160→\n  3161→    it(\"\\\\gdef changes settings.macros\", () => {\n  3162→        const macros = {};\n  3163→        expect`\\gdef\\foo{1}`.toParse(new Settings({macros}));\n  3164→        expect(macros[\"\\\\foo\"]).toBeTruthy();\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Your todos were successfully changed. In applicable cases, proceed with your current tasks, and make sure to maintain your use of the todo list for progress tracking.", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me create a reproduce script to confirm the issue:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Write:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/reproduce_issue.js\", \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env node\\n\\n// Reproduce script for the array scoping issue\\n// This script will timeout after 60 seconds\\n\\nconst katex = require('./katex.js');\\n\\n// Set a timeout to prevent infinite loops\\nconst timeout = setTimeout(() => {\\n    console.log('\\\\n[TIMEOUT] Script ran for more than 60 seconds. Exiting...');\\n    process.exit(1);\\n}, 60000);\\n\\nconsole.log('=== Testing Array Scoping Issue ===\\\\n');\\n\\n// Test case from the GitHub issue\\nconst testCase = '\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{1}\\\\\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{2}&\\\\\\\\x\\\\\\\\end{matrix}\\\\\\\\x';\\nconsole.log('Test case:', testCase);\\nconsole.log('Expected rendering: \\\"2\\\" in first cell, \\\"1\\\" in second cell, \\\"1\\\" after matrix');\\nconsole.log('Expected output: should render as if it were \\\"\\\\\\\\begin{matrix}2&1\\\\\\\\end{matrix}1\\\"\\\\n');\\n\\ntry {\\n    const result = katex.renderToString(testCase);\\n    console.log('Successfully rendered!');\\n    console.log('\\\\nHTML output (truncated):');\\n    // Extract just the text content to see what it renders\\n    const textMatch = result.match(/>([^<]+)</g);\\n    if (textMatch) {\\n        const texts = textMatch.map(m => m.replace(/[><]/g, '')).filter(t => t.trim());\\n        console.log('Rendered values:', texts.join(', '));\\n    }\\n\\n    // More detailed analysis - let's parse to check the values\\n    const parsed = katex.__parse(testCase);\\n    console.log('\\\\nParsed tree (simplified):');\\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(parsed, null, 2).substring(0, 500) + '...');\\n\\n} catch (error) {\\n    console.log('Error rendering:', error.message);\\n}\\n\\nconsole.log('\\\\n=== Testing simpler case ===\\\\n');\\n\\n// Simpler test to understand the current behavior\\nconst simpleCase = '\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{1}\\\\\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{2}\\\\\\\\x&\\\\\\\\x\\\\\\\\end{matrix}\\\\\\\\x';\\nconsole.log('Test case:', simpleCase);\\nconsole.log('Expected: \\\"2\\\" in first cell, \\\"1\\\" in second cell (scoped), \\\"1\\\" after matrix');\\n\\ntry {\\n    const result = katex.renderToString(simpleCase);\\n    console.log('Successfully rendered!');\\n\\n    // Extract text content\\n    const textMatch = result.match(/>([^<]+)</g);\\n    if (textMatch) {\\n        const texts = textMatch.map(m => m.replace(/[><]/g, '')).filter(t => t.trim() && /^[0-9]$/.test(t));\\n        console.log('Rendered values:', texts.join(''));\\n        console.log('Expected values: 211');\\n        if (texts.join('') === '211') {\\n            console.log('✓ PASS: Scoping works correctly!');\\n        } else {\\n            console.log('✗ FAIL: Got', texts.join(''), 'but expected 211');\\n        }\\n    }\\n} catch (error) {\\n    console.log('Error rendering:', error.message);\\n}\\n\\nconsole.log('\\\\n=== Testing the commented test case ===\\\\n');\\n\\n// The commented test case from katex-spec.js\\nconst commentedCase = '\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{1}\\\\\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\\\\\def\\\\\\\\x{2}&\\\\\\\\x\\\\\\\\end{matrix}';\\nconsole.log('Test case:', commentedCase);\\nconsole.log('Expected: First cell empty (just has \\\\\\\\def), second cell shows \\\"1\\\" (original definition)');\\n\\ntry {\\n    const result = katex.renderToString(commentedCase);\\n    console.log('Successfully rendered!');\\n\\n    const textMatch = result.match(/>([^<]+)</g);\\n    if (textMatch) {\\n        const texts = textMatch.map(m => m.replace(/[><]/g, '')).filter(t => t.trim() && /^[0-9]$/.test(t));\\n        console.log('Rendered values in cells:', texts);\\n        if (texts.length === 1 && texts[0] === '1') {\\n            console.log('✓ PASS: Second cell correctly shows 1 from original definition');\\n        } else {\\n            console.log('✗ FAIL: Expected only \\\"1\\\" in second cell, got:', texts);\\n        }\\n    }\\n} catch (error) {\\n    console.log('Error rendering:', error.message);\\n}\\n\\n// Clear timeout\\nclearTimeout(timeout);\\nconsole.log('\\\\n=== Script completed successfully ===');\\n\"}"}}, {"id": "Bash:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"node reproduce_issue.js\", \"description\": \"Run the reproduce script to confirm the issue\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Perfect! I found the TODO. This is exactly the issue described in the GitHub issue. The test case is commented out and there's a TODO explaining the problem.\n\nThe expected behavior is:\n- `\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\\x` should render as '111' where:\n  - First '1' is from the outer definition outside the matrix\n  - '2' is from the redefinition inside the first cell\n  - Second '1' (after &) is from the original definition being restored in the second cell\n  - Final '1' (after \\end{matrix}) is from the original definition outside the matrix\n\nBut currently it renders as '22' because the `\\def\\x{2}` in the first cell leaks to the second cell and outside.\n\nNow let me create a reproduce script to confirm the issue:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"result_text\": \"<?xml version=\\\"1.0\\\" ?>\\n<result>\\n  <CONTENT_RESULT>File created successfully at: /workspace/KaTeX/reproduce_issue.js</CONTENT_RESULT>\\n</result>\"}", "name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "Write:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"OUTPUT-TEXT\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/katex.js:11\\nimport ParseError from \\\"./src/ParseError\\\";\\n^^^^^^\\n\\nSyntaxError: Cannot use import statement outside a module\\n    at internalCompileFunction (node:internal/vm:76:18)\\n    at wrapSafe (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1283:20)\\n    at Module._compile (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1328:27)\\n    at Module._extensions..js (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1422:10)\\n    at Module.load (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1203:32)\\n    at Module._load (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1019:12)\\n    at Module.require (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1231:19)\\n    at require (node:internal/modules/helpers:177:18)\\n    at Object.<anonymous> (/workspace/KaTeX/reproduce_issue.js:6:15)\\n    at Module._compile (node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1364:14)\\n\\nNode.js v18.20.8\"}", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me check the available built files and adjust the script:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"ls -la /workspace/KaTeX/dist/ 2>/dev/null || ls -la /workspace/KaTeX/ | grep -E \\\"katex|dist\\\"\", \"description\": \"Check for built files\"}"}}, {"id": "Bash:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm run build 2>&1 | head -50\", \"description\": \"Build KaTeX\", \"timeout\": 120000}"}}], "reasoning_content": "I need to build KaTeX first and use the dist version. Let me check what's available in the dist folder or build the project first."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "TEXT-RESULT: '-rw-r--r--   1 test_user test_user   6277 Oct  2 07:18 katex.js\n\n  -rw-r--r--   1 test_user test_user    398 Oct  2 07:18 katex.webpack.js'", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "> katex@0.12.0-pre build\n> yarn prestart &&