x\\end{matrix}\\x\nExpected: \"2\" in first cell, \"1\" in second cell (scoped), \"1\" after matrix\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values: 222222\nExpected values: 211\n✗ FAIL: Got 222222 but expected 211\n\n=== Testing the commented test case ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\nExpected: First cell empty (just has \\def), second cell shows \"1\" (original definition)\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values in cells: [ '2', '2' ]\n✗ FAIL: Expected only \"1\" in second cell, got: [ '2', '2' ]\n\n=== Script completed successfully ===\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see the issue - by the time `parseArray` is called, the `\\def` has already been executed during lookahead. I need to capture the macro state earlier, in the `\\begin` handler before any argument parsing. Let me modify the environment handler:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/functions/environment.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"        if (funcName === \\\"\\\\\\\\begin\\\") {\\n            // begin...end is similar to left...right\\n            if (!environments.hasOwnProperty(envName)) {\\n                throw new ParseError(\\n                    \\\"No such environment: \\\" + envName, nameGroup);\\n            }\\n            // Build the environment object. Arguments and other information will\\n            // be made available to the begin and end methods using properties.\\n            const env = environments[envName];\\n            const {args, optArgs} =\\n                parser.parseArguments(\\\"\\\\\\\\begin{\\\" + envName + \\\"}\\\", env);\\n            const context = {\\n                mode: parser.mode,\\n                envName,\\n                parser,\\n            };\\n            const result = env.handler(context, args, optArgs);\", \"Newstring\": \"        if (funcName === \\\"\\\\\\\\begin\\\") {\\n            // begin...end is similar to left...right\\n            if (!environments.hasOwnProperty(envName)) {\\n                throw new ParseError(\\n                    \\\"No such environment: \\\" + envName, nameGroup);\\n            }\\n            // Build the environment object. Arguments and other information will\\n            // be made available to the begin and end methods using properties.\\n            const env = environments[envName];\\n\\n            // Save the current macro names before parsing environment arguments.\\n            // This is needed for issue #1989: macros expanded during token\\n            // lookahead (like \\\\def at the start of array cells) need to be\\n            // properly scoped to the cell, not leak to other cells.\\n            const preLookaheadMacros = Object.keys(parser.gullet.macros.current);\\n\\n            const {args, optArgs} =\\n                parser.parseArguments(\\\"\\\\\\\\begin{\\\" + envName + \\\"}\\\", env);\\n            const context = {\\n                mode: parser.mode,\\n                envName,\\n                parser,\\n                preLookaheadMacros,\\n            };\\n            const result = env.handler(context, args, optArgs);\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Hmm, still failing. The macros that were added during lookahead are still leaking. Let me think about why my fix isn't working...\n\nOh! I think I see the issue. When I save `preCellMacroKeys` at the start of parseArray, `\\def\\x{2}` has already been executed (during token lookahead after `{matrix}`). So `preCellMacroKeys` includes `\\x` already!\n\nLet me check by adding some debug logging:\n- If `\\def\\x{1}` was executed before `\\begin{matrix}`, then `preCellMacroKeys` would include `\\\\x`\n- If `\\def\\x{2}` was executed during lookahead (after `{matrix}`), then `preCellMacroKeys` would also include `\\\\x`\n\nSo `preCellMacroKeys` can't distinguish between macros from before the environment and macros added during lookahead!\n\nI need to save the macro keys BEFORE the environment's argument parsing, not at the start of parseArray.\n\nThe right place to save the state is in the `\\begin` handler, before it calls `env.handler`.\n\nLet me modify the environment.js file to pass this information to the environment handler:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/functions/environment.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    23→        for (let i = 0; i < nameGroup.body.length; ++i) {\n    24→            envName += assertNodeType(nameGroup.body[i], \"textord\").text;\n    25→        }\n    26→\n    27→        if (funcName === \"\\\\begin\") {\n    28→            // begin...end is similar to left...right\n    29→            if (!environments.hasOwnProperty(envName)) {\n    30→                throw new ParseError(\n    31→                    \"No such environment: \" + envName, nameGroup);\n    32→            }\n    33→            // Build the environment object. Arguments and other information will\n    34→            // be made available to the begin and end methods using properties.\n    35→            const env = environments[envName];\n    36→\n    37→            // Save the current macro names before parsing environment arguments.\n    38→            // This is needed for issue #1989: macros expanded during token\n    39→            // lookahead (like \\def at the start of array cells) need to be\n    40→            // properly scoped to the cell, not leak to other cells.\n    41→            const preLookaheadMacros = Object.keys(parser.gullet.macros.current);\n    42→\n    43→            const {args, optArgs} =\n    44→                parser.parseArguments(\"\\\\begin{\" + envName + \"}\", env);\n    45→            const context = {\n    46→                mode: parser.mode,\n    47→                envName,\n    48→                parser,\n    49→                preLookaheadMacros,\n    50→            };\n    51→            const result = env.handler(context, args, optArgs);\n    52→            parser.expect(\"\\\\end\", false);\n    53→            const endNameToken = parser.nextToken;\n    54→            const end = assertNodeType(parser.parseFunction(), \"environment\");\n    55→            if (end.name !== envName) {", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now update parseArray to use the macro list from the context:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\\n    // Save the current set of macro names to detect macros that were\\n    // expanded during token lookahead (before cell groups are created).\\n    // This fixes issue #1989 where \\\\def at the start of a cell would leak\\n    // to other cells.\\n    const preCellMacroKeys = Object.keys(parser.gullet.macros.current);\\n\\n    // Parse body of array with \\\\\\\\ temporarily mapped to \\\\cr\\n    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\", \"Newstring\": \"    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\\n    // Parse body of array with \\\\\\\\ temporarily mapped to \\\\cr\\n    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\"}"}}, {"id": "Read:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"limit\": 40, \"offset\": 605}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Good! Now I need to update parseArray to us