re and use the preLookaheadMacros:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"function parseArray(\\n    parser: Parser,\\n    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType}: {|\\n        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\\n        addJot?: boolean,\\n        cols?: AlignSpec[],\\n        arraystretch?: number,\\n        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\\n    |},\\n    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\\n    // Parse body of array with \\\\\\\\ temporarily mapped to \\\\cr\\n    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\", \"Newstring\": \"function parseArray(\\n    parser: Parser,\\n    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType, preLookaheadMacros}: {|\\n        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\\n        addJot?: boolean,\\n        cols?: AlignSpec[],\\n        arraystretch?: number,\\n        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\\n        preLookaheadMacros?: string[],\\n    |},\\n    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\\n    // Parse body of array with \\\\\\\\ temporarily mapped to \\\\cr\\n    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\"}"}}, {"id": "Edit:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"    // Register any macros that were defined during token lookahead\\n    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\\n    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\\n    const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\\n        parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\\n    for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n        if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n            !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n            preCellMacroKeys.indexOf(name) === -1) {\\n            // This macro was added during lookahead. Register it in the\\n            // undo stack so it gets removed when the cell group ends.\\n            topUndo[name] = undefined;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    let row = [];\", \"Newstring\": \"    // Register any macros that were defined during token lookahead\\n    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\\n    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\\n    if (preLookaheadMacros) {\\n        const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\\n            parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\\n        for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n            if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n                !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n                preLookaheadMacros.indexOf(name) === -1) {\\n                // This macro was added during lookahead. Register it in the\\n                // undo stack so it gets removed when the cell group ends.\\n                topUndo[name] = undefined;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    let row = [];\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Now I need to update the parseArray function signature to accept and use preLookaheadMacros:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "RESULT=The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    49→ * columns delimited by &, and create a nested list in row-major order\n    50→ * with one group per cell.  If given an optional argument style\n    51→ * (\"text\", \"display\", etc.), then each cell is cast into that style.\n    52→ */\n    53→function parseArray(\n    54→    parser: Parser,\n    55→    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType, preLookaheadMacros}: {|\n    56→        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\n    57→        addJot?: boolean,\n    58→        cols?: AlignSpec[],\n    59→        arraystretch?: number,\n    60→        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\n    61→        preLookaheadMacros?: string[],\n    62→    |},\n    63→    style: StyleStr,\n    64→): ParseNode<\"array\"> {\n    65→    // Parse body of array with \\\\ temporarily mapped to \\cr\n    66→    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\n    67→    parser.gullet.macros.set(\"\\\\\\\\\", \"\\\\cr\");\n    68→\n    69→    // Get current arraystretch if it's not set by the environment\n    70→    if (!arraystretch) {", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    82→\n    83→    // Start group for first cell\n    84→    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\n    85→\n    86→    // Register any macros that were defined during token lookahead\n    87→    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\n    88→    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\n    89→    if (preLookaheadMacros) {\n    90→        const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\n    91→            parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\n    92→        for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\n    93→            if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\n    94→                !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\n    95→                preLookaheadMacros.indexOf(name) === -1) {\n    96→                // This macro was added during lookahead. Register it in the\n    97→                // undo stack so it gets removed when the cell group ends.\n    98→                topUndo[name] = undefined;\n    99→            }\n   100→        }\n   101→    }\n   102→\n   103→    let row = [];\n   104→    const body = [row];\n   105→    const rowGaps = [];\n   106→    const hLinesBeforeRow = [];\n   107→\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm run build 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"(created|error|Error)\\\" | head -10\", \"description\": \"Rebuild KaTeX\", \"timeout\": 120000}"}}, {"id": "Bash:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"node reproduce_issue.mjs\", \"description\": \"Test the fix\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Good! Now let me rebuild and test:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"result\": \"created dist/katex.mjs in 2.3s\\ncreated dist/contrib/auto-render.mjs in 29ms\\ncreated dist/contrib/mhchem.mjs in 185ms\\ncreated dist/contrib/copy-tex.mjs in 31ms\\ncreated dist/contrib/mathtex-script-type.mjs in 30ms\\ncreated dist/contrib/render-a11y-string.mjs in 57ms\\nError: error:0308010C:digital envelope routines::unsupported\\n    at handleParseError (/workspace/KaTeX/node_modules/webpack/lib/NormalModule.js:449:10)\\n  opensslErrorStack: [ 'error:03000086:digital envelope routines::initialization error' ],\"}", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "result==== Testing Array Scoping Issue ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\\x\nExpected rendering: \"2\" in first cell, \"1\" in second cell, \"1\" after matrix\nExpected output: should render as if it were \"\\begin{matrix}2&1\\end{matrix}1\"\n\nSuccessfully rendered!\n\nHTML output (truncated):\nRendered values: 2, 2, \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&amp;\\x\\end{matrix}\\x, ​, 2, ​, 2\n\nParsed tree (simplified):\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"array\",\n    \"mode\": \"math\",\n    \"arraystretch\": 1,\n    \"body\": [\n      [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"styling\",\n          \"mode\": \"math\",\n          \"style\": \"text\",\n          \"body\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ordgroup\",\n              \"mode\": \"math\",\n              \"body\": []\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"styling\",\n          \"mode\": \"math\",\n          \"style\": \"text\",\n          \"body\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ordgrou...\n\n=== Testing simpler case ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}\\x&\\x\\end{matrix}\\x\nExpected: \"2\" in first cell, \"1\" in second cell (scoped), \"1\" after matrix\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values: 222222\nExpected values: 211\n✗ FAIL: Got 222222 but expected 211\n\n=== Testing the commented test case ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\nExpected: First cell empty (just has \\def), second cell shows \"1\" (original definition)\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values in cells: [ '2', '2' ]\n✗ FAIL: Expected only \"1\" in second cell, got: [ '2', '2' ]\n\n=== Script completed successfully ===", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I see - I'm checking if the macro name is new, but `\\x` was already defined (as 1) before the environment. I need to check if the macro VALUE changed. Let me update the fix to compare values:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Edit:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/functions/environment.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"            // Save the current macro names before parsing environment arguments.\\n            // This is needed for issue #1989: macros expanded during token\\n            // lookahead (like \\\\def at the start of array cells) need to be\\n            // properly scoped to the cell, not leak to other cells.\\n            const preLookaheadMacros = Object.keys(parser.gullet.macros.current);\\n\\n            const {args, optArgs} =\\n                parser.parseArguments(\\\"\\\\\\\\begin{\\\" + envName + \\\"}\\\", env);\\n            const context = {\\n                mode: parser.mode,\\n                envName,\\n                parser,\\n                preLookaheadMacros,\\n            };\", \"Newstring\": \"            // Save the current macro state before parsing environment arguments.\\n            // This is needed for issue #1989: macros expanded during token\\n            // lookahead (like \\\\def at the start of array cells) need to be\\n            // properly scoped to the cell, not leak to other cells.\\n            const preLookaheadMacros = {};\\n            for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n                if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name)) {\\n                    preLookaheadMacros[name] = parser.gullet.macros.current[name];\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            const {args, optArgs} =\\n                parser.parseArguments(\\\"\\\\\\\\begin{\\\" + envName + \\\"}\\\", env);\\n            const context = {\\n                mode: parser.mode,\\n                envName,\\n                parser,\\n                preLookaheadMacros,\\n            };\"}"}}, {"id": "Edit:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"function parseArray(\\n    parser: Parser,\\n    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType, preLookaheadMacros}: {|\\n        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\\n        addJot?: boolean,\\n        cols?: AlignSpec[],\\n        arraystretch?: number,\\n        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\\n        preLookaheadMacros?: string[],\\n    |},\\n    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\", \"Newstring\": \"function parseArray(\\n    parser: Parser,\\n    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType, preLookaheadMacros}: {|\\n        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\\n        addJot?: boolean,\\n        cols?: AlignSpec[],\\n        arraystretch?: number,\\n        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\\n        preLookaheadMacros?: {[string]: any},\\n    |},\\n    style: StyleStr,\\n): ParseNode<\\\"array\\\"> {\"}"}}, {"id": "Edit:2", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\", \"OLD-STRING\": \"    // Register any macros that were defined during token lookahead\\n    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\\n    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\\n    if (preLookaheadMacros) {\\n        const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\\n            parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\\n        for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n            if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n                !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n                preLookaheadMacros.indexOf(name) === -1) {\\n                // This macro was added during lookahead. Register it in the\\n                // undo stack so it gets removed when the cell group ends.\\n                topUndo[name] = undefined;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    let row = [];\", \"Newstring\": \"    // Register any macros that were defined or modified during token lookahead\\n    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\\n    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\\n    if (preLookaheadMacros) {\\n        const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\\n            parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\\n        for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n            if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\\n                !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name)) {\\n                const currentValue = parser.gullet.macros.current[name];\\n                const oldValue = preLookaheadMacros[name];\\n                // Check if this macro is new or was modified during lookahead\\n                if (!preLookaheadMacros.hasOwnProperty(name) ||\\n                    currentValue !== oldValue) {\\n                    // This macro was added or modified during lookahead.\\n                    // Register its pre-lookahead value (or undefined if new)\\n                    // in the undo stack so it gets restored/removed when the\\n                    // cell group ends.\\n                    topUndo[name] = oldValue;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    let row = [];\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Still failing! Let me add some debug logging to understand what's happening. Actually, let me think about this more carefully.\n\nThe test case is: `\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}`\n\nExpected output: first cell empty, second cell shows 1\n\nLet me trace through what happens with my fix:\n1. `\\def\\x{1}` is executed - `\\\\x` is in the macros\n2. `\\begin{matrix}` is encountered\n3. In environment.js, line 41: `preLookaheadMacros` = `[\"\\\\x\"]` (includes `\\\\x` defined in step 1)\n4. Environment name `{matrix}` is parsed\n5. parseArguments is called (returns immediately for matrix)\n6. But before parseArguments, the closing `}` was consumed, which called `expandNextToken()`\n7. `\\def\\x{2}` is expanded - now `\\\\x` = 2\n8. parseArray is called with `preLookaheadMacros = [\"\\\\x\"]`\n9. parseArray creates array group\n10. parseArray creates first cell group\n11. My fix code checks: is `\\\\x` in current? Yes. Is it in builtins? No. Is it in preLookaheadMacros? YES!\n12. So my code does NOT add it to the undo stack!\n13. That's the bug!\n\nThe problem is that `\\\\x` WAS in preLookaheadMacros (from step 1), but it was MODIFIED during lookahead (in step 7).\n\nSo I need to check not just if the macro NAME is new, but also if its VALUE changed.\n\nLet me fix this by saving not just the names, but also the values:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"OUTPUT-TEXT\": \"The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/functions/environment.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\\n    33→            // Build the environment object. Arguments and other information will\\n    34→            // be made available to the begin and end methods using properties.\\n    35→            const env = environments[envName];\\n    36→\\n    37→            // Save the current macro state before parsing environment arguments.\\n    38→            // This is needed for issue #1989: macros expanded during token\\n    39→            // lookahead (like \\\\def at the start of array cells) need to be\\n    40→            // properly scoped to the cell, not leak to other cells.\\n    41→            const preLookaheadMacros = {};\\n    42→            for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\\n    43→                if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name)) {\\n    44→                    preLookaheadMacros[name] = parser.gullet.macros.current[name];\\n    45→                }\\n    46→            }\\n    47→\\n    48→            const {args, optArgs} =\\n    49→                parser.parseArguments(\\\"\\\\\\\\begin{\\\" + envName + \\\"}\\\", env);\\n    50→            const context = {\\n    51→                mode: parser.mode,\\n    52→                envName,\\n    53→                parser,\\n    54→                preLookaheadMacros,\\n    55→            };\\n    56→            const result = env.handler(context, args, optArgs);\\n    57→            parser.expect(\\\"\\\\\\\\end\\\", false);\\n    58→            const endNameToken = parser.nextToken;\\n    59→            const end = assertNodeType(parser.parseFunction(), \\\"environment\\\");\"}", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    49→ * columns delimited by &, and create a nested list in row-major order\n    50→ * with one group per cell.  If given an optional argument style\n    51→ * (\"text\", \"display\", etc.), then each cell is cast into that style.\n    52→ */\n    53→function parseArray(\n    54→    parser: Parser,\n    55→    {hskipBeforeAndAfter, addJot, cols, arraystretch, colSeparationType, preLookaheadMacros}: {|\n    56→        hskipBeforeAndAfter?: boolean,\n    57→        addJot?: boolean,\n    58→        cols?: AlignSpec[],\n    59→        arraystretch?: number,\n    60→        colSeparationType?: ColSeparationType,\n    61→        preLookaheadMacros?: {[string]: any},\n    62→    |},\n    63→    style: StyleStr,\n    64→): ParseNode<\"array\"> {\n    65→    // Parse body of array with \\\\ temporarily mapped to \\cr\n    66→    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\n    67→    parser.gullet.macros.set(\"\\\\\\\\\", \"\\\\cr\");\n    68→", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:1"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "The file /workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js has been updated. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of the edited file:\n    82→\n    83→    // Start group for first cell\n    84→    parser.gullet.beginGroup();\n    85→\n    86→    // Register any macros that were defined or modified during token lookahead\n    87→    // (between environment start and first cell group creation) in the\n    88→    // cell's undo stack so they get properly scoped to this cell.\n    89→    if (preLookaheadMacros) {\n    90→        const topUndo = parser.gullet.macros.undefStack[\n    91→            parser.gullet.macros.undefStack.length - 1];\n    92→        for (const name in parser.gullet.macros.current) {\n    93→            if (parser.gullet.macros.current.hasOwnProperty(name) &&\n    94→                !parser.gullet.macros.builtins.hasOwnProperty(name)) {\n    95→                const currentValue = parser.gullet.macros.current[name];\n    96→                const oldValue = preLookaheadMacros[name];\n    97→                // Check if this macro is new or was modified during lookahead\n    98→                if (!preLookaheadMacros.hasOwnProperty(name) ||\n    99→                    currentValue !== oldValue) {\n   100→                    // This macro was added or modified during lookahead.\n   101→                    // Register its pre-lookahead value (or undefined if new)\n   102→                    // in the undo stack so it gets restored/removed when the\n   103→                    // cell group ends.\n   104→                    topUndo[name] = oldValue;\n   105→                }\n   106→            }\n   107→        }\n   108→    }\n   109→\n   110→    let row = [];\n   111→    const body = [row];\n   112→    const rowGaps = [];\n   113→    const hLinesBeforeRow = [];\n   114→\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Edit", "tool_call_id": "Edit:2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent! Now let's rebuild and test this improved fix:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Exploring the repository\", \"content\": \"Explore the repository to understand its structure\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Creating reproduce_issue.js script\", \"content\": \"Create reproduce_issue.js script to confirm the bug\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Understanding parseArray implementation\", \"content\": \"Understand how parseArray works and where scoping happens\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Fixing scoping issue\", \"content\": \"Fix the scoping issue in array environments\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix\", \"content\": \"Test the fix with reproduce script\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\", \"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}, {"id": "Bash:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm run build 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"(created|error|Error)\\\" | head -10\", \"description\": \"Rebuild KaTeX\", \"timeout\": 120000}"}}, {"id": "Bash:2", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"node reproduce_issue.mjs\", \"description\": \"Test the comprehensive fix\"}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Perfect! Now let me rebuild and test:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "OutputText: The todos have been modified successfully. Please proceed with your current tasks if they are applicable, and continue to utilize the todo list for progress tracking.", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "created dist/katex.mjs in 2.3s\ncreated dist/contrib/auto-render.mjs in 32ms\ncreated dist/contrib/mhchem.mjs in 198ms\ncreated dist/contrib/copy-tex.mjs in 34ms\ncreated dist/contrib/mathtex-script-type.mjs in 33ms\ncreated dist/contrib/render-a11y-string.mjs in 62ms\nError: error:0308010C:digital envelope routines::unsupported\n    at handleParseError (/workspace/KaTeX/node_modules/webpack/lib/NormalModule.js:449:10)\n  opensslErrorStack: [ 'error:03000086:digital envelope routines::initialization error' ],", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "=== Testing Array Scoping Issue ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\\x\nExpected rendering: \"2\" in first cell, \"1\" in second cell, \"1\" after matrix\nExpected output: should render as if it were \"\\begin{matrix}2&1\\end{matrix}1\"\n\nSuccessfully rendered!\n\nHTML output (truncated):\nRendered values: 2, 2, \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&amp;\\x\\end{matrix}\\x, ​, 2, ​, 2\n\nParsed tree (simplified):\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"array\",\n    \"mode\": \"math\",\n    \"arraystretch\": 1,\n    \"body\": [\n      [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"styling\",\n          \"mode\": \"math\",\n          \"style\": \"text\",\n          \"body\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ordgroup\",\n              \"mode\": \"math\",\n              \"body\": []\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"styling\",\n          \"mode\": \"math\",\n          \"style\": \"text\",\n          \"body\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ordgrou...\n\n=== Testing simpler case ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}\\x&\\x\\end{matrix}\\x\nExpected: \"2\" in first cell, \"1\" in second cell (scoped), \"1\" after matrix\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values: 222222\nExpected values: 211\n✗ FAIL: Got 222222 but expected 211\n\n=== Testing the commented test case ===\n\nTest case: \\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}\nExpected: First cell empty (just has \\def), second cell shows \"1\" (original definition)\nSuccessfully rendered!\nRendered values in cells: [ '2', '2' ]\n✗ FAIL: Expected only \"1\" in second cell, got: [ '2', '2' ]\n\n=== Script completed successfully ===", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The tests are still failing. Let me add some debug output to understand what's happening. Let me check if the test case in the test file gives us more clues:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/KaTeX/test/katex-spec.js\", \"limit\": 25, \"offset\": 3145}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Still failing! Let me think about what's happening...\n\nThe test case `\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}` still shows `['2', '2']` instead of the expected behavior.\n\nLet me trace through what happens with my current fix:\n\n1. `\\def\\x{1}` executed - `current[\"\\\\x\"]` = {tokens: \"1\", ...}\n2. `\\begin{matrix}` encountered\n3. Line 41-46 in environment.js: save `preLookaheadMacros[\"\\\\x\"]` = {tokens: \"1\", ...}\n4. Parse `{matrix}`\n5. Consume `}`, which calls `expandNextToken()`\n6. `\\def\\x{2}` is expanded - `current[\"\\\\x\"]` = {tokens: \"2\", ...}\n7. parseArray is called\n8. Line 84: first cell group created\n9. Line 92-107: my fix code runs\n10. Line 95: `currentValue` = {tokens: \"2\", ...}\n11. Line 96: `oldValue` = {tokens: \"1\", ...}\n12. Line 98-99: check if not in preLookaheadMacros OR currentValue !== oldValue\n13. currentValue !== oldValue is TRUE (different objects!)\n14. Line 104: `topUndo[\"\\\\x\"]` = {tokens: \"1\", ...}\n15. Cell is parsed (empty, because `\\def\\x{2}` was already consumed)\n16. Line 117: endGroup() called\n17. Namespace.endGroup() restores `current[\"\\\\x\"]` = {tokens: \"1\", ...}\n18. Line 118: beginGroup() for second cell\n19. Second cell parsed: `\\x` should expand to 1!\n\nThis SHOULD work! But it's not working. Let me check if there's an issue with the comparison `currentValue !== oldValue`.\n \nIn JavaScript, object references matter critically. When comparing objects, `!==` checks if they are different memory references, not their content. Even if two objects look identical, they might be distinct instances. This means my comparison could be misleading - two macro objects with the same tokens might still trigger as \"different\" due to being separate object instances.\n\nThe potential complexity lies in how macro definitions are stored and referenced. If each `\\def` creates a new object rather than modifying an existing one, my current comparison strategy might inadvertently treat seemingly similar macros as fundamentally different.\n\nI need to verify precisely how macro references are managed during definition and storage to ensure my comparison logic accurately captures the intended semantic differences.\n\nThe key insight involves tracking object references when macros are redefined. When `\\def\\x{2}` executes, it should create a distinct object reference separate from previous macro definitions. My current understanding suggests the references should differ, which means object inequality comparison should function correctly.\n\nI'll implement targeted logging to illuminate the actual object reference behavior during macro redefinition and comparison."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"content_result\": \"  3145→\\n  3146→    it(\\\"array cells generate groups\\\", () => {\\n  3147→        expect`\\\\def\\\\x{1}\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\x&\\\\def\\\\x{2}\\\\x&\\\\x\\\\end{matrix}`\\n  3148→            .toParseLike`\\\\begin{matrix}1&2&1\\\\end{matrix}`;\\n  3149→    });\\n  3150→\\n  3151→    // TODO: This doesn't yet work; before the environment gets called,\\n  3152→    // {matrix} gets consumed which means that the \\\\def gets executed, before\\n  3153→    // we can create a group. :-(  Issue #1989\\n  3154→    /*\\n  3155→    it(\\\"array cells generate groups\\\", () => {\\n  3156→        expect`\\\\def\\\\x{1}\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\def\\\\x{2}&\\\\x\\\\end{matrix}`\\n  3157→            .toParseLike`\\\\begin{matrix}&1\\\\end{matrix}`;\\n  3158→    });\\n  3159→    */\\n  3160→\\n  3161→    it(\\\"\\\\\\\\gdef changes settings.macros\\\", () => {\\n  3162→        const macros = {};\\n  3163→        expect`\\\\gdef\\\\foo{1}`.toParse(new Settings({macros}));\\n  3164→        expect(macros[\\\"\\\\\\\\foo\\\"]).toBeTruthy();\\n  3165→    });\\n  3166→\\n  3167→    it(\\\"\\\\\\\\def doesn't change settings.macros\\\", () => {\\n  3168→        const macros = {};\\n  3169→        expect`