n=== Testing the commented test case ===\\n\\nTest case: \\\\def\\\\x{1}\\\\begin{matrix}\\\\def\\\\x{2}&\\\\x\\\\end{matrix}\\nExpected: First cell empty (just has \\\\def), second cell shows \\\"1\\\" (original definition)\\nSuccessfully rendered!\\nRendered values in cells: [ '1', '1' ]\\n✗ FAIL: Expected only \\\"1\\\" in second cell, got: [ '1', '1' ]\\n\\n=== Script completed successfully ===\"}", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great progress! The fix is working - I can see \"211\" in the output (though duplicated due to my crude regex). Let me run the actual test suite to verify the fix properly:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Exploring the repository\", \"content\": \"Explore the repository to understand its structure\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Creating reproduce_issue.js script\", \"content\": \"Create reproduce_issue.js script to confirm the bug\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Understanding parseArray implementation\", \"content\": \"Understand how parseArray works and where scoping happens\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Fixing scoping issue\", \"content\": \"Fix the scoping issue in array environments\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix\", \"content\": \"Test the fix with reproduce script\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Running test suite\", \"content\": \"Run the actual test suite to verify the fix\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\", \"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}, {"id": "Bash:1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm test 2>&1 | grep -A 5 \\\"array cells generate groups\\\"\", \"description\": \"Run the specific test for array cell scoping\", \"timeout\": 120000}"}}], "reasoning_content": "Excellent progress! The third test case is now working correctly! It's showing ['1', '1'] which means:\n- First cell: empty (1 is not shown because the cell body is empty, the \\def was consumed during lookahead)\n- Second cell: 1 (correctly restored from the original definition)\n\nWait, actually, the test says \"Expected only \"1\" in second cell\", so it expects only ONE '1', but we're getting TWO '1's. Let me look at the test case more carefully...\n\nActually, looking at the test output, it says \"Rendered values in cells: [ '1', '1' ]\". This means TWO cells, each showing '1'. But the expected output is \"First cell empty (just has \\def), second cell shows '1'\". So it should be ['', '1'] or just ['1'] if the empty cell isn't counted.\n\nHmm, but my reproduce script might be extracting the values incorrectly. Let me look at the actual test case again:\n\nTest case: `\\def\\x{1}\\begin{matrix}\\def\\x{2}&\\x\\end{matrix}`\n\nThis has:\n- First cell: `\\def\\x{2}` (which gets consumed during lookahead, so the cell is empty)\n- Second cell: `\\x` (which should expand to 1)\n\nSo the output should have an empty first cell and '1' in the second cell.\n\nThe test says it expects to parse like `\\begin{matrix}&1\\end{matrix}`, which is:\n- First cell: empty (just `&`)\n- Second cell: 1\n\nSo there should be TWO cells, one empty and one with 1.\n\nBut my script says it found `['1', '1']`, which means two cells both with 1. That's weird!\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the first test case output, it says \"Rendered values: 1, 1, ...\" which suggests it's finding '1' multiple times. \n\nI'll investigate the regex pattern in my reproduce script. The current pattern `/>([^<]+)</g` captures text between tags, which might be matching duplicated content or unintended labels. This could explain the unexpected multiple '1' values.\n\nThe core issue seems to be with how the script extracts rendered values, potentially picking up multiple instances of the same text. A more precise extraction method is needed to accurately capture the expected cell contents.\n\nThe test case reveals a critical insight: the values are being duplicated (211211 instead of 211), but crucially, the scoping mechanism appears to be functioning correctly. This suggests the fix is partially successful, with the core logic working but the output processing needing refinement."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"Result\": \"Your todos have been changed successfully. Remember to use the todo list to track your progress and continue with the current tasks if relevant.\"}", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"Text\": \"\"}", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me run the test suite more comprehensively:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm test -- --testNamePattern=\\\"array cells\\\" 2>&1 | tail -50\", \"description\": \"Run specific test for array cells\", \"timeout\": 120000}"}}], "reasoning_content": "The test didn't produce output. Let me try running the test suite more directly:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "> katex@0.12.0-pre test\n> yarn prestart && yarn test:lint && yarn test:flow && yarn test:jest --testNamePattern=array cells\n\nyarn run v1.22.22\n$ node src/unicodeMake.js\nDone in 0.09s.\nyarn run v1.22.22\n$ yarn test:lint:js && yarn test:lint:css\n$ eslint *.js src static test contrib dockers website\n\n/workspace/KaTeX/src/environments/array.js\n  55:1  error  Line 55 exceeds the maximum line length of 84  max-len\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n\nerror Command failed with exit code 1.\ninfo Visit https://yarnpkg.com/en/docs/cli/run for documentation about this command.\nerror Command failed with exit code 1.\ninfo Visit https://yarnpkg.com/en/docs/cli/run for documentation about this command.", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assis