, "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me examine the key files to understand how Jotai works and identify the issue:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/src/core/atom.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Output_Text:      1→import {\n     2→  Read,\n     3→  Write,\n     4→  Atom,\n     5→  WritableAtom,\n     6→  WithInitialValue,\n     7→  PrimitiveAtom,\n     8→} from './types'\n     9→\n    10→type AnyFunction = (...args: any[]) => any\n    11→\n    12→let keyCount = 0 // global key count for all atoms\n    13→\n    14→// writable derived atom\n    15→export function atom<Value, Update>(\n    16→  read: Read<Value>,\n    17→  write: Write<Update>\n    18→): WritableAtom<Value, Update>\n    19→\n    20→// write-only derived atom\n    21→export function atom<Value, Update>(\n    22→  read: Value,\n    23→  write: Write<Update>\n    24→): Value extends AnyFunction\n    25→  ? never\n    26→  : WritableAtom<Value, Update> & WithInitialValue<Value>\n    27→\n    28→// read-only derived atom\n    29→export function atom<Value>(read: Read<Value>): Atom<Value>\n    30→\n    31→// invalid read-only derived atom\n    32→export function atom(read: AnyFunction): never\n    33→\n    34→// primitive atom\n    35→export function atom<Value>(\n    36→  initialValue: Value\n    37→): PrimitiveAtom<Value> & WithInitialValue<Value>\n    38→\n    39→export function atom<Value, Update>(\n    40→  read: Value | Read<Value>,\n    41→  write?: Write<Update>\n    42→) {\n    43→  const key = `atom${++keyCount}`\n    44→  const config = {\n    45→    toString: () => key,\n    46→  } as WritableAtom<Value, Update> & { init?: Value }\n    47→  if (typeof read === 'function') {\n    48→    config.read = read as Read<Value>\n    49→  } else {\n    50→    config.init = read\n    51→    config.read = (get) => get(config)\n    52→    config.write = (get, set, update) => {\n    53→      set(config, typeof update === 'function' ? update(get(config)) : update)\n    54→    }\n    55→  }\n    56→  if (write) {\n    57→    config.write = write\n    58→  }\n    59→  return config\n    60→}\n    61→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/src/core/useAtom.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "textresult = 1→import { useContext, useCallback, useDebugValue } from 'react'\n     2→\n     3→import { getStoreContext } from './contexts'\n     4→import { readAtom, subscribeAtom } from './vanilla'\n     5→import type { State } from './vanilla'\n     6→import type { Atom, WritableAtom, SetAtom } from './types'\n     7→import { useMutableSource } from './useMutableSource'\n     8→\n     9→const isWritable = <Value, Update>(\n    10→  atom: Atom<Value> | WritableAtom<Value, Update>\n    11→): atom is WritableAtom<Value, Update> =>\n    12→  !!(atom as WritableAtom<Value, Update>).write\n    13→\n    14→export function useAtom<Value, Update>(\n    15→  atom: WritableAtom<Value, Update>\n    16→): [Value, SetAtom<Update>]\n    17→\n    18→export function useAtom<Value>(atom: Atom<Value>): [Value, never]\n    19→\n    20→export function useAtom<Value, Update>(\n    21→  atom: Atom<Value> | WritableAtom<Value, Update>\n    22→) {\n    23→  const getAtomValue = useCallback(\n    24→    (state: State) => {\n    25→      const atomState = readAtom(state, atom)\n    26→      if (atomState.e) {\n    27→        throw atomState.e // read error\n    28→      }\n    29→      if (atomState.p) {\n    30→        throw atomState.p // read promise\n    31→      }\n    32→      if (atomState.w) {\n    33→        throw atomState.w // write promise\n    34→      }\n    35→      if ('v' in atomState) {\n    36→        return atomState.v as Value\n    37→      }\n    38→      throw new Error('no atom value')\n    39→    },\n    40→    [atom]\n    41→  )\n    42→\n    43→  const subscribe = useCallback(\n    44→    (state: State, callback: () => void) =>\n    45→      subscribeAtom(state, atom, callback),\n    46→    [atom]\n    47→  )\n    48→\n    49→  const StoreContext = getStoreContext(atom.scope)\n    50→  const [mutableSource, updateAtom] = useContext(StoreContext)\n    51→  const value: Value = useMutableSource(mutableSource, getAtomValue, subscribe)\n    52→\n    53→  const setAtom = useCallback(\n    54→    (update: Update) => {\n    55→      if (isWritable(atom)) {\n    56→        return updateAtom(atom, update)\n    57→      } else {\n    58→        throw new Error('not writable atom')\n    59→      }\n    60→    },\n    61→    [updateAtom, atom]\n    62→  )\n    63→\n    64→  useDebugValue(value)\n    65→  return [value, setAtom]\n    66→}\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me examine the vanilla.ts file which contains the core state management logic:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/src/core/vanilla.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "     1→import type {\n     2→  Atom,\n     3→  WritableAtom,\n     4→  WithInitialValue,\n     5→  AnyAtom,\n     6→  AnyWritableAtom,\n     7→  Getter,\n     8→  Setter,\n     9→  OnUnmount,\n    10→} from './types'\n    11→\n    12→const hasInitialValue = <T extends Atom<unknown>>(\n    13→  atom: T\n    14→): atom is T &\n    15→  (T extends Atom<infer Value> ? WithInitialValue<Value> : never) =>\n    16→  'init' in atom\n    17→\n    18→type Revision = number\n    19→type InvalidatedRevision = number\n    20→type ReadDependencies = Map<AnyAtom, Revision>\n    21→\n    22→// immutable atom state\n    23→export type AtomState<Value = unknown> = {\n    24→  e?: Error // read error\n    25→  p?: Promise<void> // read promise\n    26→  w?: Promise<void> // write promise\n    27→  v?: Value\n    28→  r: Revision\n    29→  i?: InvalidatedRevision\n    30→  d: ReadDependencies\n    31→}\n    32→\n    33→type AtomStateMap = WeakMap<AnyAtom, AtomState>\n    34→\n    35→type Listeners = Set<() => void>\n    36→type Dependents = Set<AnyAtom>\n    37→type Mounted = {\n    38→  l: Listeners\n    39→  d: Dependents\n    40→  u: OnUnmount | void\n    41→}\n    42→\n    43→type MountedMap = WeakMap<AnyAtom, Mounted>\n    44→\n    45→export type NewAtomReceiver = (newAtom: AnyAtom) => void\n    46→\n    47→type StateVersion = number\n    48→\n    49→type PendingAtoms = Set<AnyAtom>\n    50→\n    51→// mutable state\n    52→export type State = {\n    53→  n?: NewAtomReceiver\n    54→  v: StateVersion\n    55→  a: AtomStateMap\n    56→  m: MountedMap\n    57→  p: PendingAtoms\n    58→}\n    59→\n    60→export const createState = (\n    61→  initialValues?: Iterable<readonly [AnyAtom, unknown]>,\n    62→  newAtomReceiver?: NewAtomReceiver\n    63→): State => {\n    64→  const state: State = {\n    65→    n: newAtomReceiver,\n    66→    v: 0,\n    67→    a: new WeakMap(),\n    68→    m: new WeakMap(),\n    69→    p: new Set(),\n    70→  }\n    71→  if (initialValues) {\n    72→    for (const [atom, value] of initialValues) {\n    73→      const atomState: AtomState = { v: value, r: 0, d: new Map() }\n    74→      if (\n    75→        typeof process === 'object' &&\n    76→        process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n    77→      ) {\n    78→        Object.freeze(atomState)\n    79→      }\n    80→      state.a.set(atom, atomState)\n    81→    }\n    82→  }\n    83→  return state\n    84→}\n    85→\n    86→const getAtomState = <Value>(state: State, atom: Atom<Value>) =>\n    87→  state.a.get(atom) as AtomState<Value> | undefined\n    88→\n    89→const wipAtomState = <Value>(\n    90→  state: State,\n    91→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n    92→  dependencies?: Set<AnyAtom>\n    93→): [AtomState<Value>, ReadDependencies | undefined] => {\n    94→  const atomState = getAtomState(state, atom)\n    95→  const nextAtomState = {\n    96→    r: 0,\n    97→    ...atomState,\n    98→    d: dependencies\n    99→      ? new Map(\n   100→          Array.from(dependencies).map((a) => [\n   101→            a,\n   102→            getAtomState(state, a)?.r ?? 0,\n   103→          ])\n   104→        )\n   105→      : atomState\n   106→      ? atomState.d\n   107→      : new Map(),\n   108→  }\n   109→  if (!atomState && hasInitialValue(atom)) {\n   110→    nextAtomState.v = atom.init\n   111→  }\n   112→  return [nextAtomState, atomState?.d]\n   113→}\n   114→\n   115→const setAtomValue = <Value>(\n   116→  state: State,\n   117→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   118→  value: Value,\n   119→  dependencies?: Set<AnyAtom>,\n   120→  promise?: Promise<void>\n   121→): void => {\n   122→  const [atomState, prevDependencies] = wipAtomState(state, atom, dependencies)\n   123→  if (promise && promise !== atomState?.p) {\n   124→    // newer async read is running, not updating\n   125→    return\n   126→  }\n   127→  delete atomState.e // read error\n   128→  delete atomState.p // read promise\n   129→  delete atomState.i // invalidated revision\n   130→  if (!('v' in atomState) || !Object.is(atomState.v, value)) {\n   131→    atomState.v = value\n   132→    ++atomState.r // increment revision\n   133→  }\n   134→  commitAtomState(state, atom, atomState)\n   135→  mountDependencies(state, atom, atomState, prevDependencies)\n   136→}\n   137→\n   138→const setAtomReadError = <Value>(\n   139→  state: State,\n   140→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   141→  error: Error,\n   142→  dependencies: Set<AnyAtom>,\n   143→  promise?: Promise<void>\n   144→): void => {\n   145→  const [atomState, prevDependencies] = wipAtomState(state, atom, dependencies)\n   146→  if (promise && promise !== atomState?.p) {\n   147→    // newer async read is running, not updating\n   148→    return\n   149→  }\n   150→  delete atomState.p // read promise\n   151→  delete atomState.i // invalidated revision\n   152→  atomState.e = error // read error\n   153→  commitAtomState(state, atom, atomState)\n   154→  mountDependencies(state, atom, atomState, prevDependencies)\n   155→}\n   156→\n   157→const setAtomReadPromise = <Value>(\n   158→  state: State,\n   159→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   160→  promise: Promise<void>,\n   161→  dependencies: Set<AnyAtom>\n   162→): void => {\n   163→  const [atomState, prevDependencies] = wipAtomState(state, atom, dependencies)\n   164→  atomState.p = promise // read promise\n   165→  commitAtomState(state, atom, atomState)\n   166→  mountDependencies(state, atom, atomState, prevDependencies)\n   167→}\n   168→\n   169→const setAtomInvalidated = <Value>(state: State, atom: Atom<Value>): void => {\n   170→  const [atomState] = wipAtomState(state, atom)\n   171→  atomState.i = atomState.r // invalidated revision\n   172→  commitAtomState(state, atom, atomState)\n   173→}\n   174→\n   175→const setAtomWritePromise = <Value>(\n   176→  state: State,\n   177→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   178→  promise?: Promise<void>\n   179→): void => {\n   180→  const [atomState] = wipAtomState(state, atom)\n   181→  if (promise) {\n   182→    atomState.w = promise\n   183→  } else {\n   184→    delete atomState.w // write promise\n   185→  }\n   186→  commitAtomState(state, atom, atomState)\n   187→}\n   188→\n   189→const scheduleReadAtomState = <Value>(\n   190→  state: State,\n   191→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   192→  promise: Promise<unknown>\n   193→): void => {\n   194→  promise.then(() => {\n   195→    readAtomState(state, atom, true)\n   196→  })\n   197→}\n   198→\n   199→const readAtomState = <Value>(\n   200→  state: State,\n   201→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   202→  force?: boolean\n   203→): AtomState<Value> => {\n   204→  if (!force) {\n   205→    const atomState = getAtomState(state, atom)\n   206→    if (atomState) {\n   207→      atomState.d.forEach((_, a) => {\n   208→        if (a !== atom) {\n   209→          const aState = getAtomState(state, a)\n   210→          if (\n   211→            aState &&\n   212→            !aState.e && // no read error\n   213→            !aState.p && // no read promise\n   214→            aState.r === aState.i // revision is invalidated\n   215→          ) {\n   216→            readAtomState(state, a, true)\n   217→          }\n   218→        }\n   219→      })\n   220→      if (\n   221→        Array.from(atomState.d.entries()).every(([a, r]) => {\n   222→          const aState = getAtomState(state, a)\n   223→          return (\n   224→            aState &&\n   225→            !aState.e && // no read error\n   226→            !aState.p && // no read promise\n   227→            aState.r !== aState.i && // revision is not invalidated\n   228→            aState.r === r // revision is equal to the last one\n   229→          )\n   230→        })\n   231→      ) {\n   232→        return atomState\n   233→      }\n   234→    }\n   235→  }\n   236→  let error: Error | undefined\n   237→  let promise: Promise<void> | undefined\n   238→  let value: Value | undefined\n   239→  const dependencies = new Set<AnyAtom>()\n   240→  try {\n   241→    const promiseOrValue = atom.read(((a: AnyAtom) => {\n   242→      dependencies.add(a)\n   243→      if (a !== atom) {\n   244→        const aState = readAtomState(state, a)\n   245→        if (aState.e) {\n   246→          throw aState.e // read error\n   247→        }\n   248→        if (aState.p) {\n   249→          throw aState.p // read promise\n   250→        }\n   251→        return aState.v // value\n   252→      }\n   253→      // a === atom\n   254→      const aState = getAtomState(state, a)\n   255→      if (aState) {\n   256→        if (aState.p) {\n   257→          throw aState.p // read promise\n   258→        }\n   259→        return aState.v // value\n   260→      }\n   261→      if (hasInitialValue(a)) {\n   262→        return a.init\n   263→      }\n   264→      throw new Error('no atom init')\n   265→    }) as Getter)\n   266→    if (promiseOrValue instanceof Promise) {\n   267→      promise = promiseOrValue\n   268→        .then((value) => {\n   269→          setAtomValue(\n   270→            state,\n   271→            atom,\n   272→            value,\n   273→            dependencies,\n   274→            promise as Promise<void>\n   275→          )\n   276→          flushPending(state)\n   277→        })\n   278→        .catch((e) => {\n   279→          if (e instanceof Promise) {\n   280→            scheduleReadAtomState(state, atom, e)\n   281→            return e\n   282→          }\n   283→          setAtomReadError(\n   284→            state,\n   285→            atom,\n   286→            e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(e),\n   287→            dependencies,\n   288→            promise as Promise<void>\n   289→          )\n   290→          flushPending(state)\n   291→        })\n   292→    } else {\n   293→      value = promiseOrValue\n   294→    }\n   295→  } catch (errorOrPromise) {\n   296→    if (errorOrPromise instanceof Promise) {\n   297→      scheduleReadAtomState(state, atom, errorOrPromise)\n   298→      promise = errorOrPromise\n   299→    } else if (errorOrPromise instanceof Error) {\n   300→      error = errorOrPromise\n   301→    } else {\n   302→      error = new Error(errorOrPromise)\n   303→    }\n   304→  }\n   305→  if (error) {\n   306→    setAtomReadError(state, atom, error, dependencies)\n   307→  } else if (promise) {\n   308→    setAtomReadPromise(state, atom, promise, dependencies)\n   309→  } else {\n   310→    setAtomValue(state, atom, value, dependencies)\n   311→  }\n   312→  return getAtomState(state, atom) as AtomState<Value>\n   313→}\n   314→\n   315→export const readAtom = <Value>(\n   316→  state: State,\n   317→  readingAtom: Atom<Value>\n   318→): AtomState<Value> => {\n   319→  const atomState = readAtomState(state, readingAtom)\n   320→  state.p.delete(readingAtom)\n   321→  flushPending(state)\n   322→  return atomState\n   323→}\n   324→\n   325→const addAtom = (state: State, addingAtom: AnyAtom): Mounted => {\n   326→  let mounted = state.m.get(addingAtom)\n   327→  if (!mounted) {\n   328→    mounted = mountAtom(state, addingAtom)\n   329→  }\n   330→  flushPending(state)\n   331→  return mounted\n   332→}\n   333→\n   334→// XXX doesn't work with mutally dependent atoms\n   335→const canUnmountAtom = (atom: AnyAtom, mounted: Mounted) =>\n   336→  !mounted.l.size &&\n   337→  (!mounted.d.size || (mounted.d.size === 1 && mounted.d.has(atom)))\n   338→\n   339→const delAtom = (state: State, deletingAtom: AnyAtom): void => {\n   340→  const mounted = state.m.get(deletingAtom)\n   341→  if (mounted && canUnmountAtom(deletingAtom, mounted)) {\n   342→    unmountAtom(state, deletingAtom)\n   343→  }\n   344→  flushPending(state)\n   345→}\n   346→\n   347→const invalidateDependents = <Value>(state: State, atom: Atom<Value>): void => {\n   348→  const mounted = state.m.get(atom)\n   349→  mounted?.d.forEach((dependent) => {\n   350→    if (dependent === atom) {\n   351→      return\n   352→    }\n   353→    setAtomInvalidated(state, dependent)\n   354→    invalidateDependents(state, dependent)\n   355→  })\n   356→}\n   357→\n   358→const writeAtomState = <Value, Update>(\n   359→  state: State,\n   360→  atom: WritableAtom<Value, Update>,\n   361→  update: Update,\n   362→  pendingPromises?: Promise<void>[]\n   363→): void => {\n   364→  const atomState = getAtomState(state, atom)\n   365→  if (\n   366→    atomState &&\n   367→    atomState.w // write promise\n   368→  ) {\n   369→    const promise = atomState.w.then(() => {\n   370→      writeAtomState(state, atom, update)\n   371→      flushPending(state)\n   372→    })\n   373→    if (pendingPromises) {\n   374→      pendingPromises.push(promise)\n   375→    }\n   376→    return\n   377→  }\n   378→  try {\n   379→    const promiseOrVoid = atom.write(\n   380→      ((a: AnyAtom) => {\n   381→        const aState = readAtomState(state, a)\n   382→        if (aState.e) {\n   383→          throw aState.e // read error\n   384→        }\n   385→        if (aState.p) {\n   386→          if (\n   387→            typeof process === 'object' &&\n   388→            process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   389→          ) {\n   390→            console.warn(\n   391→              'Reading pending atom state in write operation. We throw a promise for now.',\n   392→              a\n   393→            )\n   394→          }\n   395→          throw aState.p // read promise\n   396→        }\n   397→        if ('v' in aState) {\n   398→          return aState.v // value\n   399→        }\n   400→        if (\n   401→          typeof process === 'object' &&\n   402→          process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   403→        ) {\n   404→          console.warn(\n   405→            '[Bug] no value found while reading atom in write operation. This probably a bug.',\n   406→            a\n   407→          )\n   408→        }\n   409→        throw new Error('no value found')\n   410→      }) as Getter,\n   411→      ((a: AnyWritableAtom, v: unknown) => {\n   412→        if (a === atom) {\n   413→          setAtomValue(state, a, v)\n   414→          invalidateDependents(state, a)\n   415→        } else {\n   416→          writeAtomState(state, a, v)\n   417→        }\n   418→      }) as Setter,\n   419→      update\n   420→    )\n   421→    if (promiseOrVoid instanceof Promise) {\n   422→      if (pendingPromises) {\n   423→        pendingPromises.push(promiseOrVoid)\n   424→      }\n   425→      setAtomWritePromise(\n   426→        state,\n   427→        atom,\n   428→        promiseOrVoid.then(() => {\n   429→          setAtomWritePromise(state, atom)\n   430→          flushPending(state)\n   431→        })\n   432→      )\n   433→    }\n   434→  } catch (e) {\n   435→    if (pendingPromises && pendingPromises.length) {\n   436→      pendingPromises.push(\n   437→        new Promise((_resolve, reject) => {\n   438→          reject(e)\n   439→        })\n   440→      )\n   441→    } else {\n   442→      throw e\n   443→    }\n   444→  }\n   445→}\n   446→\n   447→export const writeAtom = <Value, Update>(\n   448→  state: State,\n   449→  writingAtom: WritableAtom<Value, Update>,\n   450→  update: Update\n   451→): void | Promise<void> => {\n   452→  const pendingPromises: Promise<void>[] = []\n   453→\n   454→  writeAtomState(state, writingAtom, update, pendingPromises)\n   455→  flushPending(state)\n   456→\n   457→  if (pendingPromises.length) {\n   458→    return new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {\n   459→      const loop = () => {\n   460→        const len = pendingPromises.length\n   461→        if (len === 0) {\n   462→          resolve()\n   463→        } else {\n   464→          Promise.all(pendingPromises)\n   465→            .then(() => {\n   466→              pendingPromises.splice(0, len)\n   467→              loop()\n   468→            })\n   469→            .catch(reject)\n   470→        }\n   471→      }\n   472→      loop()\n   473→    })\n   474→  }\n   475→}\n   476→\n   477→const isActuallyWritableAtom = (atom: AnyAtom): atom is AnyWritableAtom =>\n   478→  !!(atom as AnyWritableAtom).write\n   479→\n   480→const mountAtom = <Value>(\n   481→  state: State,\n   482→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   483→  initialDependent?: AnyAtom\n   484→): Mounted => {\n   485→  // mount dependencies beforehand\n   486→  const atomState = getAtomState(state, atom)\n   487→  if (atomState) {\n   488→    atomState.d.forEach((_, a) => {\n   489→      if (a !== atom) {\n   490→        // check if not mounted\n   491→        if (!state.m.has(a)) {\n   492→          mountAtom(state, a, atom)\n   493→        }\n   494→      }\n   495→    })\n   496→  } else if (\n   497→    typeof process === 'object' &&\n   498→    process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   499→  ) {\n   500→    console.warn('[Bug] could not find atom state to mount', atom)\n   501→  }\n   502→  // mount self\n   503→  const mounted: Mounted = {\n   504→    d: new Set(initialDependent && [initialDependent]),\n   505→    l: new Set(),\n   506→    u: undefined,\n   507→  }\n   508→  state.m.set(atom, mounted)\n   509→  if (isActuallyWritableAtom(atom) && atom.onMount) {\n   510→    const setAtom = (update: unknown) => writeAtom(state, atom, update)\n   511→    mounted.u = atom.onMount(setAtom)\n   512→  }\n   513→  return mounted\n   514→}\n   515→\n   516→const unmountAtom = <Value>(state: State, atom: Atom<Value>): void => {\n   517→  // unmount self\n   518→  const onUnmount = state.m.get(atom)?.u\n   519→  if (onUnmount) {\n   520→    onUnmount()\n   521→  }\n   522→  state.m.delete(atom)\n   523→  // unmount dependencies afterward\n   524→  const atomState = getAtomState(state, atom)\n   525→  if (atomState) {\n   526→    if (\n   527→      atomState.p && // read promise\n   528→      typeof process === 'object' &&\n   529→      process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   530→    ) {\n   531→      console.warn('[Bug] deleting atomState with read promise', atom)\n   532→    }\n   533→    atomState.d.forEach((_, a) => {\n   534→      if (a !== atom) {\n   535→        const mounted = state.m.get(a)\n   536→        if (mounted) {\n   537→          mounted.d.delete(atom)\n   538→          if (canUnmountAtom(a, mounted)) {\n   539→            unmountAtom(state, a)\n   540→          }\n   541→        }\n   542→      }\n   543→    })\n   544→  } else if (\n   545→    typeof process === 'object' &&\n   546→    process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   547→  ) {\n   548→    console.warn('[Bug] could not find atom state to unmount', atom)\n   549→  }\n   550→}\n   551→\n   552→const mountDependencies = <Value>(\n   553→  state: State,\n   554→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   555→  atomState: AtomState<Value>,\n   556→  prevDependencies?: ReadDependencies\n   557→): void => {\n   558→  if (prevDependencies !== atomState.d) {\n   559→    const dependencies = new Set(atomState.d.keys())\n   560→    if (prevDependencies) {\n   561→      prevDependencies.forEach((_, a) => {\n   562→        const mounted = state.m.get(a)\n   563→        if (dependencies.has(a)) {\n   564→          // not changed\n   565→          dependencies.delete(a)\n   566→        } else if (mounted) {\n   567→          mounted.d.delete(atom)\n   568→          if (canUnmountAtom(a, mounted)) {\n   569→            unmountAtom(state, a)\n   570→          }\n   571→        } else if (\n   572→          typeof process === 'object' &&\n   573→          process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'\n   574→        ) {\n   575→          console.warn('[Bug] a dependency is not mounted', a)\n   576→        }\n   577→      })\n   578→    }\n   579→    dependencies.forEach((a) => {\n   580→      const mounted = state.m.get(a)\n   581→      if (mounted) {\n   582→        const dependents = mounted.d\n   583→        dependents.add(atom)\n   584→      } else {\n   585→        mountAtom(state, a, atom)\n   586→      }\n   587→    })\n   588→  }\n   589→}\n   590→\n   591→const commitAtomState = <Value>(\n   592→  state: State,\n   593→  atom: Atom<Value>,\n   594→  atomState: AtomState<Value>\n   595→): void => {\n   596→  if (typeof process === 'object' && process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {\n   597→    Object.freeze(atomState)\n   598→  }\n   599→  const isNewAtom = state.n && !state.a.has(atom)\n   600→  state.a.set(atom, atomState)\n   601→  if (isNewAtom) {\n   602→    ;(state.n as NewAtomReceiver)(atom)\n   603→  }\n   604→  ++state.v\n   605→  state.p.add(atom)\n   606→}\n   607→\n   608→const flushPending = (state: State): void => {\n   609→  state.p.forEach((atom) => {\n   610→    const mounted = state.m.get(atom)\n   611→    mounted?.l.forEach((listener) => listener())\n   612→  })\n   613→  state.p.clear()\n   614→}\n   615→\n   616→export const subscribeAtom = (\n   617→  state: State,\n   618→  atom: AnyAtom,\n   619→  callback: () => void\n   620→) => {\n   621→  const mounted = addAtom(state, atom)\n   622→  const listeners = mounted.l\n   623→  listeners.add(callback)\n   624→  return () => {\n   625→    listeners.delete(callback)\n   626→    delAtom(state, atom)\n   627→  }\n   628→}\n   629→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me examine the Provider component to understand how the state is managed:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/src/core/Provider.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "type=text\ntext=     1→import React, { createElement, useCallback, useRef, useDebugValue } from 'react'\n     2→\n     3→import type { AnyAtom, Scope } from './types'\n     4→import { subscribeAtom } from './vanilla'\n     5→import type { AtomState, State } from './vanilla'\n     6→import { createStore, getStoreContext } from './contexts'\n     7→import type { Store } from './contexts'\n     8→import { useMutableSource } from './useMutableSource'\n     9→\n    10→export const Provider: React.FC<{\n    11→  initialValues?: Iterable<readonly [AnyAtom, unknown]>\n    12→  scope?: Scope\n    13→}> = ({ initialValues, scope, children }) => {\n    14→  const storeRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof createStore> | null>(null)\n    15→\n    16→  if (\n    17→    typeof process === 'object' &&\n    18→    process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production' &&\n    19→    process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'test'\n    20→  ) {\n    21→    /* eslint-disable react-hooks/rules-of-hooks */\n    22→    const atomsRef = useRef<AnyAtom[]>([])\n    23→    if (storeRef.current === null) {\n    24→      // lazy initialization\n    25→      storeRef.current = createStore(initialValues, (newAtom) => {\n    26→        atomsRef.current.push(newAtom)\n    27→      })\n    28→    }\n    29→    useDebugState(\n    30→      storeRef.current as ReturnType<typeof createStore>,\n    31→      atomsRef.current\n    32→    )\n    33→    /* eslint-enable react-hooks/rules-of-hooks */\n    34→  } else {\n    35→    if (storeRef.current === null) {\n    36→      // lazy initialization\n    37→      storeRef.current = createStore(initialValues)\n    38→    }\n    39→  }\n    40→\n    41→  const StoreContext = getStoreContext(scope)\n    42→  return createElement(\n    43→    StoreContext.Provider,\n    44→    { value: storeRef.current as ReturnType<typeof createStore> },\n    45→    children\n    46→  )\n    47→}\n    48→\n    49→const atomToPrintable = (atom: AnyAtom) => atom.debugLabel || atom.toString()\n    50→\n    51→const stateToPrintable = ([state, atoms]: [State, AnyAtom[]]) =>\n    52→  Object.fromEntries(\n    53→    atoms.flatMap((atom) => {\n    54→      const mounted = state.m.get(atom)\n    55→      if (!mounted) {\n    56→        return []\n    57→      }\n    58→      const dependents = mounted.d\n    59→      const atomState = state.a.get(atom) || ({} as AtomState)\n    60→      return [\n    61→        [\n    62→          atomToPrintable(atom),\n    63→          {\n    64→            value: atomState.e || atomState.p || atomState.w || atomState.v,\n    65→            dependents: Array.from(dependents).map(atomToPrintable),\n    66→          },\n    67→        ],\n    68→      ]\n    69→    })\n    70→  )\n    71→\n    72→const getState = (state: State) => ({ ...state }) // shallow copy\n    73→\n    74→// We keep a reference to the atoms in Provider's atomsRef in dev mode,\n    75→// so atoms aren't garbage collected by the WeakMap of mounted atoms\n    76→const useDebugState = (store: Store, atoms: AnyAtom[]) => {\n    77→  const subscribe = useCallback(\n    78→    (state: State, callback: () => void) => {\n    79→      // FIXME we don't need to resubscribe, just need to subscribe for new one\n    80→      const unsubs = atoms.map((atom) => subscribeAtom(state, atom, callback))\n    81→      return () => {\n    82→        unsubs.forEach((unsub) => unsub())\n    83→      }\n    84→    },\n    85→    [atoms]\n    86→  )\n    87→  const state = useMutableSource(store[0], getState, subscribe)\n    88→  useDebugValue([state, atoms], stateToPrintable)\n    89→}\n    90→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me look at the contexts to understand how stores are created:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Read:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/src/core/contexts.ts\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "resulttext = 1→import { createContext } from 'react'\n     2→import type { Context } from 'react'\n     3→\n     4→import type { AnyAtom, WritableAtom, Scope } from './types'\n     5→import { createState, writeAtom } from './vanilla'\n     6→import type { NewAtomReceiver } from './vanilla'\n     7→import { createMutableSource } from './useMutableSource'\n     8→\n     9→type MutableSource = ReturnType<typeof createMutableSource>\n    10→\n    11→export type Store = [\n    12→  mutableSource: MutableSource,\n    13→  updateAtom: <Value, Update>(\n    14→    atom: WritableAtom<Value, Update>,\n    15→    update: Update\n    16→  ) => void | Promise<void>\n    17→]\n    18→\n    19→export const createStore = (\n    20→  initialValues?: Iterable<readonly [AnyAtom, unknown]>,\n    21→  newAtomReceiver?: NewAtomReceiver\n    22→): Store => {\n    23→  const state = createState(initialValues, newAtomReceiver)\n    24→  const mutableSource = createMutableSource(state, () => state.v)\n    25→  const updateAtom = <Value, Update>(\n    26→    atom: WritableAtom<Value, Update>,\n    27→    update: Update\n    28→  ) => writeAtom(state, atom, update)\n    29→  return [mutableSource, updateAtom]\n    30→}\n    31→\n    32→type StoreContext = Context<Store>\n    33→\n    34→const StoreContextMap = new Map<Scope | undefined, StoreContext>()\n    35→\n    36→export const getStoreContext = (scope?: Scope) => {\n    37→  if (!StoreContextMap.has(scope)) {\n    38→    StoreContextMap.set(scope, createContext(createStore()))\n    39→  }\n    40→  return StoreContextMap.get(scope) as StoreContext\n    41→}\n    42→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe TodoWrite tool hasn't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using the TodoWrite tool to track progress. Also consider cleaning up the todo list if has become stale and no longer matches what you are working on. Only use it if it's relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>", "name": "Read", "tool_call_id": "Read:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now let me complete the first task and start analyzing the issue. Let me create a reproduction script to understand the problem:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "TodoWrite:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "TodoWrite", "arguments": "{\"todos\": [{\"activeForm\": \"Exploring the repository structure\", \"content\": \"Explore the repository structure to understand Jotai\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Creating a reproduction script\", \"content\": \"Create a reproduction script to confirm the issue\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Analyzing the problem in source code\", \"content\": \"Analyze the problem in the Jotai source code\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Implementing the fix\", \"content\": \"Implement the fix for the atom update issue\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Testing the fix\", \"content\": \"Test the fix with the reproduction script\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Running existing tests\", \"content\": \"Run existing tests to ensure no regressions\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"activeForm\": \"Cleaning up temporary files\", \"content\": \"Clean up temporary files\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"result\": \"Successful modification of the todos is hereby confirmed. Please ensure your continued use of the todo list for progress tracking and proceed with current tasks where appropriate.\"}", "name": "TodoWrite", "tool_call_id": "TodoWrite:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Write:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/reproduce_issue.ts\", \"content\": \"import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\\nimport { render, act } from '@testing-library/react';\\nimport { atom, useAtom, Provider } from './src/index';\\n\\n// Mock DocumentService to simulate the user's issue\\nconst DocumentService = {\\n  findById: async (documentId: string) => {\\n    console.log(`Fetching document with ID: ${documentId}`);\\n    // Simulate async operation\\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n    return { id: documentId, name: `Document ${documentId}` };\\n  }\\n};\\n\\n// Create atoms similar to the user's issue\\nconst loading = atom(false);\\nconst document = atom(undefined);\\n\\nconst loadDocument = atom(\\n  null,\\n  (_get, set, documentId) => {\\n    const fetch = async () => {\\n      try {\\n        set(loading, true);\\n        console.log('Set loading to true');\\n        const response = await DocumentService.findById(documentId);\\n        console.log('Document fetched:', response);\\n        set(document, response);\\n        console.log('Set document to:', response);\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error(error);\\n      } finally {\\n        set(loading, false);\\n        console.log('Set loading to false');\\n      }\\n    }\\n    fetch();\\n  }\\n);\\n\\n// Test component similar to user's component\\nfunction ListPage() {\\n  const [loadingState, setLoading] = useAtom(loading);\\n  const [documentState] = useAtom(document);\\n  const [, loadDocumentAction] = useAtom(loadDocument);\\n\\n  console.log('ListPage render - loading:', loadingState, 'document:', documentState);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    console.log('useEffect triggered, calling loadDocument');\\n    loadDocumentAction('test-doc-id');\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    console.log('Document state changed:', documentState);\\n  }, [documentState]);\\n\\n  if (loadingState) {\\n    return React.createElement('h1', {}, 'Loading...');\\n  }\\n\\n  if (documentState) {\\n    return React.createElement('h1', {}, documentState.name);\\n  }\\n\\n  return React.createElement('h1', {}, 'No document');\\n}\\n\\n// Test wrapper with Provider\\nfunction TestWrapper() {\\n  return React.createElement(\\n    Provider,\\n    {},\\n    React.createElement(ListPage)\\n  );\\n}\\n\\n// Test runner with timeout\\nasync function runTest() {\\n  console.log('Starting reproduction test...');\\n\\n  let timeoutReached = false;\\n  const timeout = setTimeout(() => {\\n    timeoutReached = true;\\n    console.log('TIMEOUT: Test took longer than 60 seconds');\\n  }, 60000);\\n\\n  try {\\n    // Initial render\\n    const { container, rerender } = render(React.createElement(TestWrapper));\\n    console.log('Initial render:', container.textContent);\\n\\n    // Wait for async operations\\n    await act(async () => {\\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 500));\\n    });\\n\\n    console.log('After async operations:', container.textContent);\\n\\n    // Check if the issue exists\\n    const finalText = container.textContent;\\n    if (finalText === 'Loading...') {\\n      console.log('❌ ISSUE REPRODUCED: Component stuck in loading state');\\n      console.log('The document atom was not updated properly, causing the component to not re-render');\\n    } else if (finalText === 'Document test-doc-id') {\\n      console.log('✅ Issue not present: Component updated correctly');\\n    } else {\\n      console.log('🤔 Unexpected state:', finalText);\\n    }\\n\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error('Test failed with error:', error);\\n  } finally {\\n    clearTimeout(timeout);\\n    if (!timeoutReached) {\\n      console.log('Test completed within timeout');\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Run the test\\nrunTest().then(() => {\\n  console.log('Reproduction test finished');\\n}).catch((error) => {\\n  console.error('Test runner failed:', error);\\n});\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Output: File created successfully at: /workspace/jotai/reproduce_issue.ts\"}", "name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "Write:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll confirm the issue by running the reproduction script now:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npx ts-node reproduce_issue.ts\", \"description\": \"Run the reproduction script to confirm the issue\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "After 2m 0.0s, the command timed out.", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me try a different approach with a simpler script using the compiled JS version:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"npm run build\", \"description\": \"Build Jotai to generate the distribution files\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "resulttext: [Request interrupted by user for tool use]\n\nsrc/index.ts → dist...\ncreated dist in 27.8s\n\nsrc/index.ts → dist/index.js...\nbabelHelpers: 'bundled' option was used by default. It is recommended to configure this option explicitly, read more here: https://github.com/rollup/plugins/tree/master/packages/babel#babelhelpers\nKilled\n\n\n> jotai@0.15.3 prebuild\n> shx rm -rf dist\n\n\n> jotai@0.15.3 build\n> rollup -c && rollup -c --config-utils && rollup -c --config-devtools && rollup -c --config-immer && rollup -c --config-optics && rollup -c --config-query && rollup -c --config-xstate", "name": "Bash", "tool_call_id": "Bash:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Let me create a simpler test with just basic JavaScript to reproduce the issue:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Write:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Write", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/jotai/simple_test.js\", \"content\": \"// Simple test to reproduce the atom update issue\\nconst { atom } = require('./src/index');\\n\\nconsole.log('Creating atoms...');\\n\\n// Create the same pattern from the issue\\nconst loading = atom(false);\\nconst document = atom(undefined);\\n\\nconsole.log('Loading atom:', loading);\\nconsole.log('Document atom:', document);\\n\\nconst loadDocument = atom(\\n  null,\\n  (get, set, documentId) => {\\n    console.log('loadDocument called with:', documentId);\\n\\n    const fetch = async () => {\\n      try {\\n        console.log('Setting loading to true');\\n        set(loading, true);\\n\\n        // Mock async fetch\\n        console.log('Simulating async fetch...');\\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n        const response = { id: documentId, name: `Document ${documentId}` };\\n        console.log('Fetch completed with response:', response);\\n\\n        console.log('Setting document to response');\\n        set(document, response);\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('Error during fetch:', error);\\n      } finally {\\n        console.log('Setting loading to false');\\n        set(loading, false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    fetch();\\n  }\\n);\\n\\nconsole.log('LoadDocument atom created:', loadDocument);\\n\\n// Test timeout protection\\nsetTimeout(() => {\\n  console.log('TIMEOUT: Script running longer than expected');\\n  process.exit(1);\\n}, 5000);\\n\\nconsole.log('Basic atom creation test completed successfully');\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File created successfully at: /workspace/jotai/simple_test.js", "name": "Write", "tool_call_id": "Write:0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "Bash:0", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"node simple_test.js\", \"description\": \"Run simple atom creation test\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" ?>\n<result>\n  <OUTPUTText>node:internal/modules/cjs/loader:1215\n  throw err;\n  ^\n\nError: Cannot find modul