have VLA (Variable Length Array) data, the column data is of type `_VLF` (Variable Length Form), and when we try to do `arra != arrb` on such arrays, it fails because numpy doesn't know how to handle the comparison of arrays containing variable-length arrays.\n\nThe issue is in the TableDataDiff._diff method around line 1463. The code is:\n\n```python\nelse:\n    diffs = np.where(arra != arrb)\n```\n\nBut when `arra` and `arrb` are VLA columns, the `!=` operation fails because each element in the array is itself an array, and numpy can't determine the truth value of the comparison.\n\nLooking at the code, I can see there's already special handling for \"P\" format columns (lines 1452-1461), but the issue is that the format check is `if \"P\" in col.format` but in our case the format is \"QD\" which contains \"D\" but not \"P\". Let me check what the actual format should be for VLA data.\n\nLet me look at how VLA formats are handled in the FITS module."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Execution output of [search]:\nFound 27 matches for \"VLA\" in /testbed/astropy/io/fits:\n./astropy/io/fits/column.py (2 matches)\n./astropy/io/fits/fitsrec.py (4 matches)\n./astropy/io/fits/tests/test_table.py (11 matches)\n./astropy/io/fits/hdu/table.py (10 matches)\nEnd of matches for \"VLA\" in /testbed/astropy/io/fits", "name": "search", "tool_call_id": "call_function_0524280082_1"}, {"content": "\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_6631571759_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"path\": \"/testbed/astropy/io/fits/column.py\", \"search_term\": \"VLA\"}", "name": "search"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "reasoning_content": "Let me check the column.py file to understand VLA formats better:"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Execution output of [search]:\nMatches for \"VLA\" in /testbed/astropy/io/fits/column.py:\n1199:                    # TDIMs have different meaning for VLA format,\n1705:                # Note: VLA array descriptors should not be reshaped", 