*20:20–20:25** | Break.\n- **20:25–20:50** | History: source linking practice (1 paragraph).\n- **20:50–21:15** | Anki review (20 min max).\n- **21:15–21:30** | Light prep.\n\n### Saturday, Jan 10\n- **WORLD HISTORY FINAL: Sat Jan 10, 10:00**.\n- **Morning** (08:00–09:30): timeline sweep, ID cards, thesis structure review.\n- **10:00–13:00** | **WORLD HISTORY FINAL**.\n- **Post-exam**: rest, light Algorithms review (15 min).\n\n### Sunday, Jan 11\n- **15-minute micro-review only** — Algorithms cards only, keep DP/flow fresh.\n\n---\n\n## Week 7 (Jan 12–13)\n\n### Monday, Jan 12\n- **19:00–19:25** | New Anki: 5 cards Algorithms (new cards reduced 50%).\n- **19:25–19:30** | Break.\n- **19:30–19:55** | Algorithms: DP + flow + amortized (2 problems, keep fresh).\n- **19:55–20:20** | Light review of past Algorithms problems (review only, no new hard problems).\n- **20:20–20:30** | Break.\n- **20:30–21:00** | Anki review (20 min max).\n- **21:00–21:30** | Final prep: pseudocode patterns, key theorems.\n\n### Tuesday, Jan 13\n- **ALGORITHMS FINAL: Tue Jan 13, 09:00**.\n- **Morning** (07:30–08:30): quick review of DP recurrence templates, flow theorem statements, amortized proof outlines.\n- **09:00–12:00** | **ALGORITHMS FINAL**.\n- **Post-exam**: celebration — you're done!\n\n---\n\n## Taper Summary\n\n- **T–10 days (around Dec 27)**: Reduce new Anki cards by 50% (from ~40 to ~20/day).\n- **T–5 days (around Jan 1)**: Freeze all new cards. Review-only mode.\n- **Mock exams**:\n  - Algorithms mock: Week 6 Thu (Jan 8) 18:00–21:00 (after Organic final, but before History).\n  - Calculus mock: Week 7 Sat (Jan 10) 09:00–12:00 (before History final, note scheduling conflict — if needed, move Calculus mock to Week 6 Sat Dec 28 09:00–12:00 and keep Week 6 Thu for Algorithms light review). **Recommend: Calculus mock Week 6 Sat Dec 28 09:00–12:00** (fits better with taper and avoids conflict with Organic final).\n- **Week 5 Saturday event**: Front-load to Fri evening + Sat morning 0