{"data_index": 74, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I need to prioritize our sales leads using recent activity and how well they fit our ICP. Can you help design a scoring approach?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. To set this up, please share:\n- The absolute path and format of your lead dataset and key column names.\n- Which activity signals you track (e.g., email opens/replies, site visits) and the timeframe to consider.\n- Your ICP criteria (industries, company size, revenue, regions).\n- Weighting between activity and fit, desired top-k, and output format/path.\nOnce I have these, I’ll score and rank in one pass.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a lead scoring framework combining recent activity and ICP fit. I will first gather the data source, schema, timeframe, weighting, and output preferences. Once parameters are clear, I plan to run a single tool call to a lead prioritization function with the dataset path, weights, lookback, ICP profile, and output settings."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We have a CSV at /data/lead_activity_2025-10.csv. Columns: lead_id, company, domain, industry, employees, region, annual_revenue_usd, email_opens_7d, email_replies_30d, site_visits_14d, last_activity_at (ISO 8601), created_at (ISO 8601)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Proposed approach:\n- Total score = w_activity × activity_score + w_fit × fit_score.\n- Activity: normalize email_opens_7d, email_replies_30d, site_visits_14d, and apply time-decay to last_activity_at.\n- Fit: compare industry, employees, annual_revenue_usd, and region against your ICP.\nPlease confirm:\n- Weights for activity vs fit.\n- Lookback window and decay half-life.\n- ICP details: target industries, employee range, minimum revenue, target regions.\n- Normalization method (min-max or z-score) and any per-signal weights (e.g., replies > opens > visits).\n- Tie-breaker order for equal scores.\n- Missing values policy (zero, drop, or constant) and dedup strategy.\n- Desired top-k and output path/format plus fields to include.", "reasoning_content": "Now I know the data location and schema. I’ll propose a scoring formula and ask for the remaining parameters: weights, lookback, time-decay, ICP details, normalization, tie-breakers, missing-value handling, dedup, output fields/path. With those, I can execute one call to the lead prioritization tool."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Weights: activity 0.6, fit 0.4. Lookback: 30 days. Decay half-life: 7 days. ICP: industries SaaS, Fintech, Healthcare IT; employees 50–1000; minimum revenue $5M; regions US and CA. Return the top 50 leads with a short reason for fit. Timezone is America/Los_Angeles."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. A few final details:\n- Normalization: min-max or z-score?\n- Per-signal weights for activity (e.g., replies, opens, visits)?\n- Tie-breakers when scores tie (e.g., more replies, then site visits, then most recent activity).\n- Missing values policy (treat as zero, drop, or use a constant).\n- Deduplication (none, by lead_id, by company domain) and keep all or highest score.\n- Output: confirm CSV path and which fields to include (rank, lead_id, company, total_score, activity_score, fit_score, fit_reasons, last_activity_at).", "reasoning_content": "We have the core settings: weights, lookback, decay, ICP, top-k, timezone. I need tie-breakers, missing-value policy, dedup strategy, normalization method, per-signal weights, and the exact output path/fields. Then I can run a single prioritize_leads call with those parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Use min-max normalization. Activity signal weights: replies 0.5, opens 0.3, visits 0.2. Tie-breakers: more email_replies_30d, then more site_visits_14d, then most recent last_activity_at. Treat missing values as zero. No dedup—keep all rows. Save CSV to /reports/top_leads_2025-11.csv with fields rank, lead_id, company, total_score, activity_score, fit_score, fit_reasons, last_activity_at."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Configuration confirmed. Ready to score and rank in one pass and write the CSV report. Would you like me to include summary statistics in the response (averages and percentiles)? If yes, specify which metrics and percentile cutoffs.", "reasoning_content": "All parameters are specified. I will perform one tool call to prioritize_leads using: source_path=/data/lead_activity_2025-10.csv, source_format=csv, weights activity=0.6 fit=0.4, lookback=30 days, half-life=7 days, timezone America/Los_Angeles, activity_signals mapping and weights, min-max normalization, ICP profile, tie-breakers, missing policy zero, no dedup, and output config top_k=50 to /reports/top_leads_2025-11.csv with the requested fields. I’ll also be ready to include summary stats if the user wants them."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes. Run it now with these settings: source_format=csv; source_path=/data/lead_activity_2025-10.csv; activity_lookback_days=30; timezone=America/Los_Angeles; time_decay_half_life_days=7; weights.activity=0.6; weights.fit=0.4; activity_signals.email_opens_field=email_opens_7d; activity_signals.email_replies_field=email_replies_30d; activity_signals.site_visits_field=site_visits_14d; activity_signals.last_activity_at_field=last_activity_at; activity_signals.normalization_method=min_max; activity_signals.signal_weights.email_replies=0.5; activity_signals.signal_weights.email_opens=0.3; activity_signals.signal_weights.site_visits=0.2; fit_profile.industries=[\"SaaS\",\"Fintech\",\"Healthcare IT\"]; fit_profile.employee_range.min=50; fit_profile.employee_range.max=1000; fit_profile.revenue_min_usd=5000000; fit_profile.regions=[\"US\",\"CA\"]; tie_breakers=[\"email_replies\",\"site_visits\",\"last_activity_at\"]; missing_values.policy=zero; deduplication.strategy=none; output.format=csv; output.destination_path=/reports/top_leads_2025-11.csv; output.fields=[\"rank\",\"lead_id\",\"company\",\"total_score\",\"activity_score\",\"fit_score\",\"fit_reasons\",\"last_activity_at\"]; output.top_k=50; output.include_summary=true; output.summary_metrics=[\"total_score\",\"activity_score\",\"fit_score\"]; output.summary_percentiles=[10,25,50,75,90]."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "prioritize_leads", "description": "Score and rank leads by recent activity and ICP fit, applying optional time-decay and normalization, then output a report with reasons and summary stats.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to the lead dataset file"}, "source_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Input format", "enum": ["csv", "json"]}, "activity_lookback_days": {"type": "integer", "description": "Days to consider activity", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 365}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone for parsing timestamps (e.g., America/Los_Angeles)"}, "time_decay_half_life_days": {"type": "integer", "description": "Half-life used to decay older activity", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 90}, "weights": {"type": "object", "properties": {"activity": {"type": "number", "description": "Weight for activity score (0–1)", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "fit": {"type": "number", "description": "Weight for fit score (0–1)", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}}, "required": ["activity", "fit"]}, "activity_signals": {"type": "object", "properties": {"email_opens_field": {"type": "string", "description": "Column name for email opens count within lookback"}, "email_replies_field": {"type": "string", "description": "Column name for email replies count within lookback"}, "site_visits_field": {"type": "string", "description": "Column name for site visits count within lookback"}, "last_activity_at_field": {"type": "string", "description": "Column name for last activity timestamp (ISO 8601)"}, "normalization_method": {"type": "string", "description": "Normalization method for activity metrics", "enum": ["min_max", "z_score"]}, "signal_weights": {"type": "object", "properties": {"email_replies": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "email_opens": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "site_visits": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}}, "required": ["email_replies", "email_opens", "site_visits"]}}, "required": ["email_opens_field", "email_replies_field", "site_visits_field", "last_activity_at_field", "normalization_method", "signal_weights"]}, "fit_profile": {"type": "object", "properties": {"industries": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "description": "Target industries for ICP"}, "employee_range": {"type": "object", "properties": {"min": {"type": "integer"}, "max": {"type": "integer"}}, "required": ["min", "max"]}, "revenue_min_usd": {"type": "number", "description": "Minimum annual revenue in USD for ICP fit"}, "regions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "description": "Target regions/countries"}}, "required": ["industries", "employee_range", "revenue_min_usd", "regions"]}, "tie_breakers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["email_replies", "site_visits", "email_opens", "last_activity_at"]}, "description": "Priority order when scores tie"}, "missing_values": {"type": "object", "properties": {"policy": {"type": "string", "enum": ["zero", "drop", "constant"]}, "fill_value": {"type": "number"}}, "required": ["policy"]}, "deduplication": {"type": "object", "properties": {"strategy": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "by_key", "by_company_domain"]}, "key_field": {"type": "string"}, "keep": {"type": "string", "enum": ["all", "highest_score"]}}, "required": ["strategy"]}, "output": {"type": "object", "properties": {"format": {"type": "string", "enum": ["csv", "json"]}, "destination_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to write the prioritized leads report"}, "fields": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["rank", "lead_id", "company", "total_score", "activity_score", "fit_score", "fit_reasons", "last_activity_at"]}, "minItems": 1}, "top_k": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 1000}, "include_summary": {"type": "boolean"}, "summary_metrics": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["total_score", "activity_score", "fit_score"]}}, "summary_percentiles": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 99}}}, "required": ["format", "destination_path", "fields", "top_k"]}}, "required": ["source_path", "source_format", "activity_lookback_days", "timezone", "time_decay_half_life_days", "weights", "activity_signals", "fit_profile", "output"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "0645005803582500a6490bc72b4b2f9e", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to run the prioritization with all the parameters specified. Let me construct the complete request with all the parameters they've provided.\n\nI need to call the prioritize_leads function with all the parameters:\n- source_format: csv\n- source_path: /data/lead_activity_2025-10.csv\n- activity_lookback_days: 30\n- timezone: America/Los_Angeles\n- time_decay_half_life_days: 7\n- weights: activity=0.6, fit=0.4\n- activity_signals: email_opens_field, email_replies_field, site_visits_field, last_activity_at_field, normalization_method=min_max, signal_weights\n- fit_profile: industries, employee_range, revenue_min_usd, regions\n- tie_breakers: email_replies, site_visits, last_activity_at\n- missing_values: policy=zero\n- deduplication: strategy=none\n- output: format, destination_path, fields, top_k, include_summary, summary_metrics, summary_percentiles\n\nThis is a straightforward function call with all the parameters provided by the user. Let me make the call now.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_9aapk685a35a_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"source_format\": \"csv\", \"source_path\": \"/data/lead_activity_2025-10.csv\", \"activity_lookback_days\": 30, \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"time_decay_half_life_days\": 7, \"weights\": {\"activity\": 0.6, \"fit\": 0.4}, \"activity_signals\": {\"email_opens_field\": \"email_opens_7d\", \"email_replies_field\": \"email_replies_30d\", \"site_visits_field\": \"site_visits_14d\", \"last_activity_at_field\": \"last_activity_at\", \"normalization_method\": \"min_max\", \"signal_weights\": {\"email_replies\": 0.5, \"email_opens\": 0.3, \"site_visits\": 0.2}}, \"fit_profile\": {\"industries\": [\"SaaS\", \"Fintech\", \"Healthcare IT\"], \"employee_range\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 1000}, \"revenue_min_usd\": 5000000, \"regions\": [\"US\", \"CA\"]}, \"tie_breakers\": [\"email_replies\", \"site_visits\", \"last_activity_at\"], \"missing_values\": {\"policy\": \"zero\"}, \"deduplication\": {\"strategy\": \"none\"}, \"output\": {\"format\": \"csv\", \"destination_path\": \"/reports/top_leads_2025-11.csv\", \"fields\": [\"rank\", \"lead_id\", \"company\", \"total_score\", \"activity_score\", \"fit_score\", \"fit_reasons\", \"last_activity_at\"], \"top_k\": 50, \"include_summary\": true, \"summary_metrics\": [\"total_score\", \"activity_score\", \"fit_score\"], \"summary_percentiles\": [10, 25, 50, 75, 90]}}", "name": "prioritize_leads"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716568, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 701, "prompt_tokens": 2496, "total_tokens": 3197, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 241, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 2235}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:34.405414", "duration_ms": 10691, "hash": "59ac126ad6cafde72551c447651d75f2", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 75, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I want to build a monthly budget and set up alerts if I overspend."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great — to set this up, please share: the target month (YYYY-MM) and currency, your income sources and amounts, the categories you want to track, any categories that should roll over unused budget, and the overspend alert threshold (e.g., 10% over limit or a fixed amount). Also, where are your transactions stored (CSV path or a list)?", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a monthly budget with overspend alerts. I need the month, currency, income sources, target categories, rollover rules, and alert threshold. Once I have budgets and a transaction source, I will call the analyze_monthly_budget tool with those parameters to compute the summary and flags."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Let's plan October 2025 in USD. Monthly income: Salary $5,200 and Freelance $800. Categories to budget: Rent, Groceries, Dining Out, Utilities, Insurance, Transport, Entertainment, Health, Kids, Subscriptions, Misc, Savings. Suggest reasonable limits per category and an overspend scheme."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on $6,000 total income, a practical starting point: Rent 1,800; Utilities 220; Insurance 300; Transport 160; Groceries 600; Dining Out 250; Kids 180; Health 120; Entertainment 150; Subscriptions 85; Misc 100; Savings 1,000. Does this work for you? What overspend threshold should trigger alerts (e.g., 10% over the category limit), and should any categories roll over unused amounts? Do you have your transactions in a CSV file or an export?", "reasoning_content": "They provided month, currency, incomes, and categories. I will propose baseline allocations using typical percentages and common ranges. I will then ask for confirmation of limits, overspend threshold type/value, rollover preferences, and how to ingest transactions. After confirmation, I will use the analyze_monthly_budget tool with the agreed parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Those limits look good. Use a 10% overspend threshold. Transactions are in a CSV at /home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. What are the CSV column names (e.g., date, description, category, amount, type)? For amounts: are expenses positive and refunds negative, and are incomes marked with type=income? Also, should Savings be excluded from overspend alerts?", "reasoning_content": "Budgets, threshold, and the CSV path are provided. I must confirm the CSV column names and amount/type semantics to parse correctly and whether Savings should be excluded from alerts. Once confirmed, I will prepare an analyze_monthly_budget call for 2025-10 in USD with a percentage threshold of 10 and the CSV source."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Columns are: date, description, category, amount, type. Expenses are positive amounts, refunds show up as negative but still type=expense. Incomes are positive with type=income. Yes — exclude the Savings category from overspend alerts."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Noted. Which categories should roll over unused budget into next month? Groceries is a common choice; rent, utilities, and insurance typically do not roll over.", "reasoning_content": "CSV structure and alert exclusions are clear. Before running the tool, I need rollover rules per category so the budget logic can carry forward unused amounts where applicable. I expect Groceries to roll over and fixed bills not to."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Set Groceries to roll over; all others should not. Keep the limits we discussed. The CSV path is /home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Please confirm the incomes: Salary $5,200 and Freelance $800 (total $6,000). Use per-category alerts with a 10% threshold. Month: 2025-10, currency USD. Do you want the report exported, and if so, to what path and format?", "reasoning_content": "We now have budgets, rollover rules, and the transaction source. I will confirm income sources and the alert mode (per-category at 10%) and ask about exporting the report. Then I can call analyze_monthly_budget with month=2025-10, currency=USD, the agreed budgets, overspend alert settings, and the CSV mapping."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes: Salary $5,200, Freelance $800. Use per-category 10% alerts. Add burn-rate and a mid-month projection in the summary. Currency USD. Month 2025-10. CSV path is /home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. I’ll include burn rate and a mid-month projection. Which output format do you prefer (json, csv, or markdown), and what absolute path should I use to save the report?", "reasoning_content": "All core inputs are set. I will include extra metrics: burn rate and mid-month projection. I need the desired output format and absolute path to save the report. Then I will call analyze_monthly_budget with those options."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Export JSON to /home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect — ready to run the October 2025 budget analysis and write the JSON report to /home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json. Say “Run it” or provide the final command and I’ll generate the summary.", "reasoning_content": "We have everything needed. I will call analyze_monthly_budget with: month=2025-10; currency=USD; income_sources=[Salary 5200, Freelance 800]; budget_categories with rollover for Groceries and Savings excluded from alerts; overspend_alert={threshold_type: percentage, threshold_value: 10, alert_mode: per_category}; transactions_source={type: csv_file, path: /home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv, csv_format columns}; report_format=json; output_path=/home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json; extra_metrics=[burn_rate, projection]."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Run the October 2025 budget analysis with these parameters: Month 2025-10, Currency USD. Income sources: Salary 5200, Freelance 800. Budget categories: Rent 1800; Utilities 220; Insurance 300; Transport 160; Groceries 600 (rollover true); Dining Out 250; Kids 180; Health 120; Entertainment 150; Subscriptions 85; Misc 100; Savings 1000 (exclude from alerts). Overspend alert: 10% over limit, per category. Transactions source: CSV at /home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv with columns date, description, category, amount, type. Include burn_rate and projection. Output JSON to /home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "analyze_monthly_budget", "description": "Compute a monthly budget summary from budgets, income, and transactions; flag overspending per category; optionally include extra metrics and write a report.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"month": {"type": "string", "description": "Target month in YYYY-MM", "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}$"}, "currency": {"type": "string", "description": "Currency code", "enum": ["USD", "EUR", "GBP", "JPY", "AUD", "CAD", "CNY", "INR"]}, "income_sources": {"type": "array", "description": "List of income sources and amounts for the month", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Amount in currency units"}}, "required": ["name", "amount"]}}, "budget_categories": {"type": "array", "description": "Budget limits per category", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "limit": {"type": "number", "description": "Monthly budget limit in currency units"}, "rollover": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Carry unused budget to the next month", "default": false}, "exclude_from_alerts": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Do not flag overspending for this category", "default": false}}, "required": ["name", "limit"]}}, "overspend_alert": {"type": "object", "description": "Overspending alert settings", "properties": {"threshold_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["percentage", "fixed_amount"]}, "threshold_value": {"type": "number", "description": "Percentage (e.g., 10) or fixed amount (e.g., 50)"}, "alert_mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["per_category", "overall"], "default": "per_category"}}, "required": ["threshold_type", "threshold_value"]}, "transactions_source": {"type": "object", "description": "Source of transaction data", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["inline", "csv_file"]}, "path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to CSV if type=csv_file"}, "transactions": {"type": "array", "description": "Inline transactions if type=inline", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string"}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD"}, "description": {"type": "string"}, "category": {"type": "string"}, "amount": {"type": "number"}, "type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["expense", "income", "transfer"]}}, "required": ["id", "date", "category", "amount", "type"]}}, "csv_format": {"type": "object", "description": "Column names in the CSV file", "properties": {"date_col": {"type": "string", "default": "date"}, "description_col": {"type": "string", "default": "description"}, "category_col": {"type": "string", "default": "category"}, "amount_col": {"type": "string", "default": "amount"}, "type_col": {"type": "string", "default": "type"}}}}, "required": ["type"]}, "extra_metrics": {"type": "array", "description": "Additional metrics to compute", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["burn_rate", "projection", "top_overspends", "category_trends"]}}, "report_format": {"type": "string", "enum": ["json", "csv", "markdown"], "default": "json"}, "output_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to write the summary report"}}, "required": ["month", "currency", "income_sources", "budget_categories", "overspend_alert", "transactions_source"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500565a3dd2c7310c9a98eb367283", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to run the analysis with all the parameters they've specified. Let me call the function with all the details:\n\n- month: \"2025-10\"\n- currency: \"USD\"\n- income_sources: [{\"name\": \"Salary\", \"amount\": 5200}, {\"name\": \"Freelance\", \"amount\": 800}]\n- budget_categories:\n  - Rent: 1800, rollover: false\n  - Utilities: 220, rollover: false\n  - Insurance: 300, rollover: false\n  - Transport: 160, rollover: false\n  - Groceries: 600, rollover: true\n  - Dining Out: 250, rollover: false\n  - Kids: 180, rollover: false\n  - Health: 120, rollover: false\n  - Entertainment: 150, rollover: false\n  - Subscriptions: 85, rollover: false\n  - Misc: 100, rollover: false\n  - Savings: 1000, rollover: false, exclude_from_alerts: true\n- overspend_alert: threshold_type: \"percentage\", threshold_value: 10, alert_mode: \"per_category\"\n- transactions_source: type: \"csv_file\", path: \"/home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv\", csv_format: date_col: \"date\", description_col: \"description\", category_col: \"category\", amount_col: \"amount\", type_col: \"type\"\n- extra_metrics: [\"burn_rate\", \"projection\"]\n- report_format: \"json\"\n- output_path: \"/home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json\"\n\nLet me construct this properly.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_mebm4brejwmw_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"month\": \"2025-10\", \"currency\": \"USD\", \"income_sources\": [{\"name\": \"Salary\", \"amount\": 5200}, {\"name\": \"Freelance\", \"amount\": 800}], \"budget_categories\": [{\"name\": \"Rent\", \"limit\": 1800, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Utilities\", \"limit\": 220, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Insurance\", \"limit\": 300, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Transport\", \"limit\": 160, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Groceries\", \"limit\": 600, \"rollover\": true}, {\"name\": \"Dining Out\", \"limit\": 250, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Kids\", \"limit\": 180, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Health\", \"limit\": 120, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Entertainment\", \"limit\": 150, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Subscriptions\", \"limit\": 85, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Misc\", \"limit\": 100, \"rollover\": false}, {\"name\": \"Savings\", \"limit\": 1000, \"rollover\": false, \"exclude_from_alerts\": true}], \"overspend_alert\": {\"threshold_type\": \"percentage\", \"threshold_value\": 10, \"alert_mode\": \"per_category\"}, \"transactions_source\": {\"type\": \"csv_file\", \"path\": \"/home/alex/finance/2025-10-transactions.csv\", \"csv_format\": {\"date_col\": \"date\", \"description_col\": \"description\", \"category_col\": \"category\", \"amount_col\": \"amount\", \"type_col\": \"type\"}}, \"extra_metrics\": [\"burn_rate\", \"projection\"], \"report_format\": \"json\", \"output_path\": \"/home/alex/finance/reports/2025-10-budget-report.json\"}", "name": "analyze_monthly_budget"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 835, "prompt_tokens": 1988, "total_tokens": 2823, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 354, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1787}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:33.022079", "duration_ms": 9244, "hash": "ed20b5813cba2e6e9cd37cfdf61cff40", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 76, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I've been exhausted lately and want to improve my sleep. Can you analyze my sleep tracker exports and suggest what to change?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. Which trackers do you use, what period should I analyze, and what’s your timezone? If you have export files ready, please share their absolute paths.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants analysis of sleep tracker data plus actionable suggestions. I need the tracker sources, timeframe, timezone, file paths, and target metrics to configure the analysis. Plan: for each export, call analyze_sleep_export with file_path, source_type, timezone, date_start/date_end, include_naps, metrics, summary_granularity, detect_outliers, include_annotations, output_format. Then aggregate findings into prioritized issues and actions."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I have Oura, Apple Health, and Garmin data covering the last 30 days. Main issues: frequent wake-ups and irregular bed/wake times."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. What timezone should I use, and do you want naps included? I can compute total sleep, sleep efficiency, awakenings, REM/deep proportions, HRV, resting HR, and consistency. Anything else?", "reasoning_content": "They provided sources and a rough period. I should confirm timezone, whether to include naps, and the metrics to compute. Plan: prepare analyze_sleep_export calls per source with metrics: total_sleep, sleep_efficiency, awake_count, deep_pct, rem_pct, hrv, resting_hr, consistency."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Timezone is America/Los_Angeles. Include naps. Please compute total sleep, sleep efficiency, awakenings, deep/REM %, HRV, resting heart rate, and sleep consistency."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Please provide the exact start and end dates, and the absolute paths to your Oura, Apple Health, and Garmin exports. Should I flag outliers and include annotations (notes like alcohol/caffeine)?", "reasoning_content": "We now have timezone and metrics. Next I need exact start/end dates, file paths, and preferences for outlier detection and annotations. Plan: call analyze_sleep_export per file with timezone=America/Los_Angeles, date_start/date_end, include_naps=true, metrics=[total_sleep, sleep_efficiency, awake_count, deep_pct, rem_pct, hrv, resting_hr, consistency], summary_granularity=weekly, detect_outliers and include_annotations as requested."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Start 2025-10-08, end 2025-11-06. I usually have coffee around 3 pm, rarely drink alcohol, and I do scroll my phone in bed."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. Do you prefer weekly or daily summaries, and in text or JSON? I’ll factor in your 3 pm caffeine habit and late screen use when giving recommendations. When ready, send the file paths.", "reasoning_content": "We have date range and lifestyle context. I should confirm summary granularity and output format before running analysis. Plan remains to call analyze_sleep_export with weekly summaries and later synthesize recommendations considering caffeine timing and screen use."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Weekly summaries in text are fine. Also list top 5 issues and 5 concrete actions. The files are on my server."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. Please provide absolute paths for each export and the source type for each (Oura, Apple Health, Garmin). Do you want me to include annotations and flag outliers?", "reasoning_content": "Output preferences are clear. I need absolute paths and the source type per file. Plan: run analyze_sleep_export per file with summary_granularity=weekly, output_format=text, detect_outliers and include_annotations if requested, then merge findings into prioritized issues/actions."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes, include annotations and flag outliers. I'll send the paths next."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great — send 2–5 absolute paths with their source types. I’ll analyze them in parallel and return weekly summaries plus the top issues and actions.", "reasoning_content": "We’re ready to run parallel analysis once paths arrive. I will call analyze_sleep_export for 2–5 files in parallel with timezone=America/Los_Angeles, date_start=2025-10-08, date_end=2025-11-06, include_naps=true, metrics specified, summary_granularity=weekly, detect_outliers=true, include_annotations=true, output_format=text."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Also, please note nights with alcohol use or late caffeine if metadata captures that."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Will do. I’ll tag nights with alcohol or late caffeine from the annotations. Share the file paths when ready.", "reasoning_content": "They want annotations highlighted. I will scan metadata for alcohol/caffeine keywords during analysis. Plan: include include_annotations=true and annotation_keywords to capture alcohol/late caffeine and reflect them in summaries and recommendations."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In parallel, analyze these three exports and produce weekly summaries and tailored recommendations: \n- Oura: /srv/data/sleep/oura/oura_sleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json \n- Apple Health: /srv/data/sleep/apple_health/AppleHealthSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json \n- Garmin: /srv/data/sleep/garmin/GarminSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.csv \nUse timezone America/Los_Angeles, date range 2025-10-08 to 2025-11-06, include naps, detect outliers, and include annotations. Compute total sleep, sleep efficiency, awakenings, deep/REM %, HRV, resting HR, and sleep consistency. Flag nights with alcohol or late caffeine. Return the top 5 issues and 5 concrete actions."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "analyze_sleep_export", "description": "Parse a sleep tracker export and compute metrics, weekly/daily summaries, and annotations for a given time window", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to the sleep export file"}, "source_type": {"type": "string", "description": "Sleep tracker source type", "enum": ["oura", "apple_health", "garmin", "fitbit", "withings", "generic_csv", "generic_json"]}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone, e.g., America/Los_Angeles"}, "date_start": {"type": "string", "description": "Start date (inclusive)", "format": "date"}, "date_end": {"type": "string", "description": "End date (inclusive)", "format": "date"}, "include_naps": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Whether to include naps in metrics"}, "metrics": {"type": "array", "description": "Metrics to compute", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["total_sleep", "sleep_efficiency", "awake_count", "deep_pct", "rem_pct", "hrv", "resting_hr", "consistency"]}, "minItems": 1}, "summary_granularity": {"type": "string", "description": "Summary window", "enum": ["daily", "weekly", "monthly", "overall"]}, "detect_outliers": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Flag outlier nights (e.g., unusually short/long sleep, extreme awakenings)"}, "include_annotations": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Include notes/metadata like alcohol or caffeine events"}, "annotation_keywords": {"type": "array", "description": "Keywords to scan for in annotations", "items": {"type": "string"}, "default": ["alcohol", "beer", "wine", "late caffeine", "caffeine", "coffee"]}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output format for the summary", "enum": ["json", "text", "markdown"], "default": "text"}}, "required": ["file_path", "source_type", "timezone", "date_start", "date_end"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "aggregate_sleep_results", "description": "Merge metrics from multiple sources, prioritize issues, and generate a concise action plan", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"sources": {"type": "array", "description": "Per-source metrics payloads to aggregate", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"label": {"type": "string", "description": "Source label (e.g., Oura)"}, "metrics": {"type": "object", "description": "Metrics object returned by analysis"}, "annotations": {"type": "array", "description": "Annotation events per night", "items": {"type": "object"}}}, "required": ["label", "metrics"]}, "minItems": 1}, "goals": {"type": "array", "description": "Goals to optimize for", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["reduce_awakenings", "increase_consistency", "extend_total_sleep", "improve_efficiency", "increase_deep_rem", "increase_hrv", "lower_resting_hr"]}}, "lifestyle": {"type": "object", "properties": {"caffeine_cutoff": {"type": "string", "description": "Typical caffeine cutoff time, HH:MM (24h)"}, "alcohol": {"type": "string", "description": "Alcohol frequency", "enum": ["none", "rare", "weekly", "frequent"]}, "screen_use_before_bed_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Estimated minutes of screen use before bedtime", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 300}}}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Format of the aggregated report", "enum": ["json", "text", "markdown"], "default": "text"}, "top_n_issues": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of top issues to surface", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10, "default": 5}, "top_n_actions": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of top actions to recommend", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10, "default": 5}}, "required": ["sources"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450058b0b77157ac994e107d8807e2", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to analyze three sleep tracker exports in parallel. They've provided all the necessary details:\n\n1. File paths:\n   - Oura: /srv/data/sleep/oura/oura_sleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json\n   - Apple Health: /srv/data/sleep/apple_health/AppleHealthSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json\n   - Garmin: /srv/data/sleep/garmin/GarminSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.csv\n\n2. Parameters:\n   - timezone: America/Los_Angeles\n   - date_start: 2025-10-08\n   - date_end: 2025-11-06\n   - include_naps: true\n   - detect_outliers: true\n   - include_annotations: true\n   - metrics: [\"total_sleep\", \"sleep_efficiency\", \"awake_count\", \"deep_pct\", \"rem_pct\", \"hrv\", \"resting_hr\", \"consistency\"]\n   - summary_granularity: weekly\n   - output_format: text\n   - annotation_keywords: [\"alcohol\", \"beer\", \"wine\", \"late caffeine\", \"caffeine\", \"coffee\"]\n\n3. They want:\n   - Weekly summaries\n   - Top 5 issues\n   - Top 5 concrete actions\n   - Flag nights with alcohol or late caffeine\n\nI'll make three parallel analyze_sleep_export calls, one for each source. Then I'll use aggregate_sleep_results to combine the results and generate the issues and actions.\n\nLet me construct the calls:\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_aprabpteaxhm_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/srv/data/sleep/oura/oura_sleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json\", \"source_type\": \"oura\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"date_start\": \"2025-10-08\", \"date_end\": \"2025-11-06\", \"include_naps\": true, \"metrics\": [\"total_sleep\", \"sleep_efficiency\", \"awake_count\", \"deep_pct\", \"rem_pct\", \"hrv\", \"resting_hr\", \"consistency\"], \"summary_granularity\": \"weekly\", \"detect_outliers\": true, \"include_annotations\": true, \"annotation_keywords\": [\"alcohol\", \"beer\", \"wine\", \"late caffeine\", \"caffeine\", \"coffee\"], \"output_format\": \"text\"}", "name": "analyze_sleep_export"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}, {"id": "call_function_aprabpteaxhm_2", "function": {"arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/srv/data/sleep/apple_health/AppleHealthSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.json\", \"source_type\": \"apple_health\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"date_start\": \"2025-10-08\", \"date_end\": \"2025-11-06\", \"include_naps\": true, \"metrics\": [\"total_sleep\", \"sleep_efficiency\", \"awake_count\", \"deep_pct\", \"rem_pct\", \"hrv\", \"resting_hr\", \"consistency\"], \"summary_granularity\": \"weekly\", \"detect_outliers\": true, \"include_annotations\": true, \"annotation_keywords\": [\"alcohol\", \"beer\", \"wine\", \"late caffeine\", \"caffeine\", \"coffee\"], \"output_format\": \"text\"}", "name": "analyze_sleep_export"}, "type": "function", "index": 1}, {"id": "call_function_aprabpteaxhm_3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"/srv/data/sleep/garmin/GarminSleep_2025-10-08_to_2025-11-06.csv\", \"source_type\": \"garmin\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"date_start\": \"2025-10-08\", \"date_end\": \"2025-11-06\", \"include_naps\": true, \"metrics\": [\"total_sleep\", \"sleep_efficiency\", \"awake_count\", \"deep_pct\", \"rem_pct\", \"hrv\", \"resting_hr\", \"consistency\"], \"summary_granularity\": \"weekly\", \"detect_outliers\": true, \"include_annotations\": true, \"annotation_keywords\": [\"alcohol\", \"beer\", \"wine\", \"late caffeine\", \"caffeine\", \"coffee\"], \"output_format\": \"text\"}", "name": "analyze_sleep_export"}, "type": "function", "index": 2}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716568, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1104, "prompt_tokens": 1827, "total_tokens": 2931, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 354, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1787}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:37.370106", "duration_ms": 13507, "hash": "26d2b0dac8af9514abe13e232fae55f4", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 3}
{"data_index": 77, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I’m evaluating a couple of rentals in Brooklyn and want a fair comparison by normalizing utilities, parking, and laundry differences. Can you help?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. Please share, for each listing: source and listing ID, address and unit, rent amount and frequency, beds/baths, square footage, utilities included, parking type and fees, laundry type, pet policy, deposit and fees, heating/cooling, furnished status, availability date, commute destination/mode/minutes, and amenities. Also tell me your normalization preferences (currency, include parking cost, adjust for utilities, target rent frequency, sort key).", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a normalized comparison of rental listings. I should collect structured details and their normalization preferences, then perform a single tool call to normalize and compare. Plan: ask for listing data and options, then call normalize_compare_listings with listings and normalize_options."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Preferences: normalize to monthly USD, include parking costs, adjust for utilities, compute rent per sqft, and sort by effective monthly cost. Rounding to 2 decimals. Weights: price 0.4, size 0.2, laundry 0.1, parking 0.1, pets 0.1, commute 0.1. Monthly assumptions: electric $60, internet $70, gas $40. I have a cat and a car. We’ll compare two units."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great — I’ll include parking and utility adjustments, compute rent per sqft, and sort by effective monthly cost using your weights. Please send the two listings with: source and listing ID; address and unit; rent and frequency; lease term; beds/baths; square footage; parking details (type, included, monthly fee); laundry type; pet policy; utilities included; deposit and application/broker fees; heating/cooling; furnished; availability date; commute (destination, mode, minutes); and amenities. Since you have a cat and a car, I’ll include pet rent where allowed and parking costs.", "reasoning_content": "I have their normalization preferences and assumptions, plus tenant profile (cat and car). Next, I need full listing details to run a single tool call. Plan: collect the two listings, then call normalize_compare_listings with listings and normalize_options including currency USD, target monthly, include parking, utility adjustment, rent per sqft, rounding=2, sort_by=effective_monthly_cost, weights, assumptions, and tenant_profile."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Here are the two listings:\n\nListing A:\n- source: StreetEasy; id: SE-1345872\n- address: 241 Smith St, Apt 4B, Brooklyn, NY 11201\n- rent: $3,800 per month\n- lease term: 12 months\n- beds/baths: 2 bed, 1 bath\n- sqft: 900\n- parking: street, included, monthly fee $0\n- laundry: coin\n- pets: cats allowed, dogs not allowed\n- deposit: $3,800\n- application fee: $20\n- utilities included: water\n- heating: radiator\n- cooling: window AC\n- furnished: no\n- availability date: 2025-12-01\n- amenities: elevator, roof deck\n- commute: to 4 Times Square (New York, NY 10036), mode subway, 25 minutes\n\nListing B:\n- source: StreetEasy; id: SE-1345891\n- address: 155 Wyckoff St, Apt 2, Brooklyn, NY 11201\n- rent: $3,650 per month\n- lease term: 12 months\n- beds/baths: 2 bed, 1 bath\n- sqft: 850\n- parking: garage, not included, monthly fee $250\n- laundry: in-unit\n- pets: small dogs allowed, cats not allowed\n- deposit: $3,650\n- application fee: $25\n- utilities included: water and gas\n- heating: forced air\n- cooling: central AC\n- furnished: no\n- availability date: 2025-11-20\n- amenities: elevator, roof deck\n- commute: to 4 Times Square (New York, NY 10036), mode subway, 28 minutes"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks — these details are clear. Before I run the comparison, please confirm:\n- Is internet included for either listing?\n- Is electric included for either listing?\n- Any brokerage fee?\n\nAlso, list the exact fields you want returned (e.g., normalized rent, effective monthly cost, rent per sqft, total move‑in cost, parking and utilities effects, laundry, pets, commute, score) and whether you prefer a detailed or summary output.", "reasoning_content": "The listings look complete. I need to confirm internet/electric inclusion and any brokerage fee, plus the desired return fields and output format. Then I will make a single call to normalize_compare_listings with these two items and the user’s options (USD, monthly, include parking, adjust utilities, rent per sqft, rounding=2, sort by effective monthly cost, given weights, assumptions, tenant_profile pet=cat, car_owner=true) and requested return fields."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Internet not included for either. Electric not included for either. No brokerage fee.\n\nIn a single run, normalize and compare Listing A (SE-1345872) and Listing B (SE-1345891) with these options:\n- currency: USD\n- target rent frequency: monthly\n- include parking cost: true\n- adjust for utilities: true\n- compute rent per sqft: true\n- rounding: 2\n- sort by: effective_monthly_cost\n- weights: price 0.4, size 0.2, laundry 0.1, parking 0.1, pets 0.1, commute 0.1\n- assumptions: monthly electric $60, monthly internet $70, monthly gas $40, pet rent $25\n- tenant profile: car_owner true, pet cat\n\nReturn fields: normalized_rent, effective_monthly_cost, rent_per_sqft, total_move_in_cost, parking_effect, utilities_effect, laundry, pets, commute, score.\n\nUse the listing details I sent above."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "normalize_compare_listings", "description": "Normalize rental listings (costs and features) and produce comparison metrics including effective monthly cost, rent per sqft, score, and differences.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"listings": {"type": "array", "description": "2–5 rental listings to normalize and compare", "minItems": 2, "maxItems": 5, "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "Listing ID"}, "source": {"type": "string", "description": "Listing source", "enum": ["StreetEasy", "Zillow", "Craigslist", "MLS", "Other"]}, "address": {"type": "string", "description": "Street address including unit if not provided separately"}, "unit": {"type": "string", "description": "Unit/apartment identifier (optional)"}, "city": {"type": "string", "description": "City name (optional if included in address)"}, "state": {"type": "string", "description": "State code (e.g., NY)", "minLength": 2, "maxLength": 2}, "zip": {"type": "string", "description": "ZIP code", "pattern": "^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$"}, "rent_amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Advertised rent amount"}, "rent_frequency": {"type": "string", "description": "Advertised rent frequency", "enum": ["monthly", "weekly", "annual"]}, "currency": {"type": "string", "description": "Currency code", "enum": ["USD", "EUR", "GBP", "CAD", "AUD"]}, "lease_term_months": {"type": "integer", "description": "Lease term in months", "minimum": 1}, "beds": {"type": "number", "description": "Bedrooms", "minimum": 0}, "baths": {"type": "number", "description": "Bathrooms", "minimum": 0}, "sqft": {"type": "integer", "description": "Square footage", "minimum": 0}, "parking": {"type": "object", "description": "Parking details", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "street", "garage", "reserved"]}, "included": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Whether parking cost is included in rent"}, "monthly_fee": {"type": "number", "description": "Monthly parking fee if not included", "minimum": 0}}, "required": ["type", "included"]}, "laundry": {"type": "string", "description": "Laundry type", "enum": ["none", "coin", "shared", "in_unit"]}, "pets_policy": {"type": "object", "description": "Pet policy", "properties": {"cats": {"type": "string", "enum": ["allowed", "restricted", "not_allowed"]}, "dogs": {"type": "string", "enum": ["allowed", "restricted", "not_allowed"]}, "notes": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["cats", "dogs"]}, "deposit_amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Security deposit", "minimum": 0}, "application_fee": {"type": "number", "description": "Application fee", "minimum": 0}, "brokerage_fee": {"type": "number", "description": "Broker fee due at signing (if any)", "minimum": 0}, "utilities_included": {"type": "array", "description": "Included utilities", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["water", "gas", "electric", "trash", "internet", "heat"]}, "uniqueItems": true}, "amenities": {"type": "array", "description": "Amenities list", "items": {"type": "string"}, "uniqueItems": true}, "furnished": {"type": "string", "description": "Furnished status", "enum": ["no", "partial", "full"]}, "heating": {"type": "string", "description": "Heating type", "enum": ["radiator", "forced_air", "baseboard", "heat_pump", "steam", "none", "unknown"]}, "cooling": {"type": "string", "description": "Cooling type", "enum": ["window_ac", "central_ac", "none", "unknown"]}, "availability_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Available date (YYYY-MM-DD)", "format": "date"}, "commute": {"type": "object", "description": "Commute details", "properties": {"to_address": {"type": "string", "description": "Destination address"}, "mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["subway", "bus", "walk", "bike", "car"]}, "estimated_minutes": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0}}, "required": ["to_address", "mode", "estimated_minutes"]}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Additional notes (optional)"}}, "required": ["id", "source", "address", "currency", "rent_amount", "rent_frequency", "lease_term_months", "beds", "baths", "sqft", "laundry", "pets_policy", "deposit_amount", "application_fee", "utilities_included", "availability_date"]}}, "normalize_options": {"type": "object", "description": "Normalization settings and assumptions", "properties": {"currency": {"type": "string", "enum": ["USD", "EUR", "GBP", "CAD", "AUD"]}, "target_rent_frequency": {"type": "string", "enum": ["monthly", "annual"]}, "compute_rent_per_sqft": {"type": "boolean"}, "include_parking_cost": {"type": "boolean"}, "adjust_for_utilities": {"type": "boolean"}, "rounding_decimals": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 4, "default": 2}, "sort_by": {"type": "string", "enum": ["effective_monthly_cost", "rent_per_sqft", "score"]}, "weights": {"type": "object", "description": "Scoring weights (0–1 each; not required to sum to 1)", "properties": {"price": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "size": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "laundry": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "parking": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "pets": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "commute": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}, "amenities": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}}}, "assumptions": {"type": "object", "description": "Monthly cost assumptions used when utilities are not included", "properties": {"monthly_gas_estimate": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0}, "monthly_electric_estimate": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0}, "monthly_internet_estimate": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0}, "pet_rent_monthly": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0}}}, "tenant_profile": {"type": "object", "description": "Tenant context for applying optional costs", "properties": {"car_owner": {"type": "boolean"}, "pet": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "cat", "dog"]}}}}, "required": ["currency", "target_rent_frequency", "compute_rent_per_sqft", "include_parking_cost", "adjust_for_utilities", "sort_by"]}, "return_fields": {"type": "array", "description": "Which fields to include in the result", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["normalized_rent", "effective_monthly_cost", "rent_per_sqft", "lease_term_months", "total_move_in_cost", "parking_effect", "utilities_effect", "laundry", "pets", "amenities", "commute", "score"]}, "uniqueItems": true}, "include_differences": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Include per-field differences", "default": true}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output detail level", "enum": ["summary", "detailed"]}}, "required": ["listings", "normalize_options"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "0645005677d1f2ac20cbc2c00ade8e32", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user has provided all the necessary information to run the normalization comparison. Let me construct the function call with the two listings and the specified options.\n\nListing A (SE-1345872):\n- id: SE-1345872\n- source: StreetEasy\n- address: 241 Smith St, Apt 4B, Brooklyn, NY 11201\n- rent_amount: 3800\n- rent_frequency: monthly\n- lease_term_months: 12\n- beds: 2\n- baths: 1\n- sqft: 900\n- parking: type street, included: true, monthly_fee: 0\n- laundry: coin\n- pets_policy: cats allowed, dogs not allowed\n- deposit_amount: 3800\n- application_fee: 20\n- brokerage_fee: 0 (not mentioned, assumed 0)\n- utilities_included: water\n- heating: radiator\n- cooling: window_ac\n- furnished: no\n- availability_date: 2025-12-01\n- amenities: elevator, roof deck\n- commute: to_address: 4 Times Square, New York, NY 10036, mode: subway, estimated_minutes: 25\n\nListing B (SE-1345891):\n- id: SE-1345891\n- source: StreetEasy\n- address: 155 Wyckoff St, Apt 2, Brooklyn, NY 11201\n- rent_amount: 3650\n- rent_frequency: monthly\n- lease_term_months: 12\n- beds: 2\n- baths: 1\n- sqft: 850\n- parking: type garage, included: false, monthly_fee: 250\n- laundry: in_unit\n- pets_policy: cats not_allowed, dogs allowed (small dogs)\n- deposit_amount: 3650\n- application_fee: 25\n- brokerage_fee: 0 (not mentioned, assumed 0)\n- utilities_included: water, gas\n- heating: forced_air\n\n\n- cooling: central_ac\n- furnished: no\n- availability_date: 2025-11-20\n- amenities: elevator, roof deck\n- commute: to_address: 4 Times Square, New York, NY 10036, mode: subway, estimated_minutes: 28\n\nI'll proceed with running the normalization comparison to analyze the two rental options systematically.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_dj58j559b4tk_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"listings\": [{\"id\": \"SE-1345872\", \"source\": \"StreetEasy\", \"address\": \"241 Smith St, Apt 4B, Brooklyn, NY 11201\", \"rent_amount\": 3800, \"rent_frequency\": \"monthly\", \"lease_term_months\": 12, \"beds\": 2, \"baths\": 1, \"sqft\": 900, \"parking\": {\"type\": \"street\", \"included\": true, \"monthly_fee\": 0}, \"laundry\": \"coin\", \"pets_policy\": {\"cats\": \"allowed\", \"dogs\": \"not_allowed\"}, \"deposit_amount\": 3800, \"application_fee\": 20, \"brokerage_fee\": 0, \"utilities_included\": [\"water\"], \"heating\": \"radiator\", \"cooling\": \"window_ac\", \"furnished\": \"no\", \"availability_date\": \"2025-12-01\", \"amenities\": [\"elevator\", \"roof deck\"], \"commute\": {\"to_address\": \"4 Times Square, New York, NY 10036\", \"mode\": \"subway\", \"estimated_minutes\": 25}}, {\"id\": \"SE-1345891\", \"source\": \"StreetEasy\", \"address\": \"155 Wyckoff St, Apt 2, Brooklyn, NY 11201\", \"rent_amount\": 3650, \"rent_frequency\": \"monthly\", \"lease_term_months\": 12, \"beds\": 2, \"baths\": 1, \"sqft\": 850, \"parking\": {\"type\": \"garage\", \"included\": false, \"monthly_fee\": 250}, \"laundry\": \"in_unit\", \"pets_policy\": {\"cats\": \"not_allowed\", \"dogs\": \"allowed\"}, \"deposit_amount\": 3650, \"application_fee\": 25, \"brokerage_fee\": 0, \"utilities_included\": [\"water\", \"gas\"], \"heating\": \"forced_air\", \"cooling\": \"central_ac\", \"furnished\": \"no\", \"availability_date\": \"2025-11-20\", \"amenities\": [\"elevator\", \"roof deck\"], \"commute\": {\"to_address\": \"4 Times Square, New York, NY 10036\", \"mode\": \"subway\", \"estimated_minutes\": 28}}], \"normalize_options\": {\"currency\": \"USD\", \"target_rent_frequency\": \"monthly\", \"include_parking_cost\": true, \"adjust_for_utilities\": true, \"compute_rent_per_sqft\": true, \"rounding_decimals\": 2, \"sort_by\": \"effective_monthly_cost\", \"weights\": {\"price\": 0.4, \"size\": 0.2, \"laundry\": 0.1, \"parking\": 0.1, \"pets\": 0.1, \"commute\": 0.1}, \"assumptions\": {\"monthly_electric_estimate\": 60, \"monthly_internet_estimate\": 70, \"monthly_gas_estimate\": 40, \"pet_rent_monthly\": 25}, \"tenant_profile\": {\"car_owner\": true, \"pet\": \"cat\"}}, \"return_fields\": [\"normalized_rent\", \"effective_monthly_cost\", \"rent_per_sqft\", \"total_move_in_cost\", \"parking_effect\", \"utilities_effect\", \"laundry\", \"pets\", \"commute\", \"score\"]}", "name": "normalize_compare_listings"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1259, "prompt_tokens": 3109, "total_tokens": 4368, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 496, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 2683}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:37.339718", "duration_ms": 13387, "hash": "c9b5ce7280cb791c5dbece0e6d62b570", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": false, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 78, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I want to set up a daily mindfulness and journaling routine I can actually stick to. I tend to fall off after a week. Can you help me design something that fits my day?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Happy to help. To tailor the routine, could you share: your available time windows (morning, midday, evening), your main goals (e.g., anxiety, stress, gratitude), journaling style (questions, bullet points, affirmations), preferred mindfulness practices (breathwork, body scan, walking), your timezone, and whether you want daily reminders?", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a sustainable daily routine. I need their goals, time windows, preferred practices, journaling style, and notification preferences to tailor a plan. Once we have specifics, I will plan parallel calls to generate journaling prompts and mindfulness session scripts, and optionally schedule reminders. Tools to use later: generate_journal_prompts (themes, count, time_of_day, tone, format), compose_mindfulness_session (focus, duration, level, goal, opening/closing), and schedule_reminder (title, time, timezone, method, recurrence, dates)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I’m in America/Los_Angeles. I can do about 10–20 minutes in the morning around 7:30, 3–5 minutes midday near 12:00, and 10–15 minutes in the evening around 9:30 pm. I’m dealing with anxiety and stress. I like short breathing exercises. Journaling: bullet points or questions. Yes to phone reminders."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Here’s a simple baseline:\n- Morning (~10 min): brief breathwork + gratitude-focused journaling.\n- Midday (3–5 min): quick grounding (breath or mindful walking) + 1–3 micro questions.\n- Evening (12 min): body scan + reflective questions to offload stress.\nWould you like rotating prompts? For each slot, please confirm: themes (e.g., gratitude, anxiety processing, work reflection), prompt counts, and preferred format (bullet points vs questions).", "reasoning_content": "The user provided windows, goals, styles, and timezone. I’ll propose a simple, balanced routine with concrete durations and ask for prompt counts, themes per slot, formats, and rotation. I plan later to call generate_journal_prompts per time slot and compose_mindfulness_session per time slot, plus schedule_reminder for morning, midday, and evening alarms."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes, rotating prompts. Morning: gratitude + grounding, 5 prompts. Midday: anxiety defusion, 3 prompts. Evening: reflection with some self-compassion, 5 prompts. Midday breathing 2–3 minutes; morning breathwork 10 minutes; evening body scan 12 minutes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. A few details to finalize:\n- Tone: supportive, neutral, or slightly challenging?\n- Include one deeper prompt in each set?\n- Mediums: morning and midday on phone; evening on paper journal—does that work?\n- Do you want an opening bell and a closing note for the sessions?", "reasoning_content": "We have themes, counts, and durations. I’ll confirm tone, whether to include one deeper prompt per set, and mediums (phone vs paper) to shape the format and language. Then I can prepare to call generate_journal_prompts (theme, count, time_of_day, tone, include_deep_prompt, format) and compose_mindfulness_session (focus, duration, level, goal, opening/closing flags)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Tone supportive, include one deep prompt each. Morning and midday on phone; evening on paper. Please add simple micro-habit anchors, like right after brushing teeth in the morning, after lunch at midday, and after dinner in the evening."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Anchors noted: morning after brushing teeth, midday after lunch, evening after dinner. Do you have a start date in mind and any end date? Also, confirm: no background audio, and include an opening bell and a short closing note?", "reasoning_content": "Anchors are set. I’ll capture start date and whether they want background audio; they already prefer supportive tone and deep prompts. I will plan to include opening/closing cues and schedule reminders. Tools planned: generate_journal_prompts per slot and compose_mindfulness_session per slot in parallel, then schedule_reminder for three times with the user’s timezone."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Start next Monday, 2025-11-10, and run for a month. No background audio. Yes to opening bell and closing note. Please schedule daily reminders titled “Morning Mindfulness”, “Midday Grounding”, and “Evening Wind-down” at 07:30, 12:00, and 21:30 respectively in America/Los_Angeles."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. Should the reminders recur daily? And for delivery: push notifications for all, or calendar events for evening to avoid quiet hours conflicts?", "reasoning_content": "We have schedule times, titles, timezone, and dates. I’ll confirm recurrence, and whether push notifications are okay for all slots. Evening could also be a calendar entry to avoid quiet-hours issues. Once confirmed, I’ll plan schedule_reminder calls for each slot with recurrence daily."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Daily recurrence. Use push notifications for morning and midday. For evening, use a calendar event. If I ever shift later than 10 pm, avoid push reminders after 22:00."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Understood. Final prompt formatting preference per slot: morning (bullet points or questions), midday (bullet points or questions), evening (bullet points or questions)? Also, do you want one-liner prompts or short paragraphs?", "reasoning_content": "Delivery and recurrence are clear: push for morning/midday, calendar event for evening, with quiet-hours consideration. Next I’ll lock prompt formats. Then I can prepare parallel calls: for each time-of-day, one generate_journal_prompts and one compose_mindfulness_session, plus one schedule_reminder."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Morning: bullet points, one-liners. Midday: questions, one-liners. Evening: questions, one-liners."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great—everything is set. When you send the final request, I’ll generate the morning, midday, and evening packages in parallel and set the reminders accordingly.", "reasoning_content": "We now have full parameters for prompts (themes, counts, time_of_day, tone supportive, include_deep_prompt true, formats per slot, one-liners) and sessions (focus per slot, durations, level beginner, goal aligned to each theme, opening/closing true). Scheduling details are set with timezone, recurrence, titles, methods, and dates. I will be ready to run parallel tool calls—per slot: generate_journal_prompts and compose_mindfulness_session—plus schedule_reminder for each time."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In parallel, create three packages—morning, midday, and evening—and set the reminders:\n- Morning: prompts (theme: gratitude, count: 5, time_of_day: morning, tone: supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: bullet_points, length_style: one_line); session (focus: breathwork, duration_minutes: 10, level: beginner, goal: gratitude, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true).\n- Midday: prompts (theme: anxiety_processing, count: 3, time_of_day: midday, tone: supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: questions, length_style: one_line); session (focus: mindful_walking, duration_minutes: 5, level: beginner, goal: anxiety_grounding, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true).\n- Evening: prompts (theme: work_reflection, count: 5, time_of_day: evening, tone: supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: questions, length_style: one_line); session (focus: body_scan, duration_minutes: 12, level: beginner, goal: stress_reduction, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true).\nAnd schedule reminders: Morning Mindfulness at 07:30 (timezone America/Los_Angeles, method push_notification, recurrence daily, start_date 2025-11-10, end_date 2025-12-10); Midday Grounding at 12:00 (same settings, method push_notification); Evening Wind-down at 21:30 (same settings, method calendar_event)."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "generate_journal_prompts", "description": "Generate a set of journaling prompts tailored to a theme, time of day, tone, and format", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"theme": {"type": "string", "description": "Focus area for the prompts", "enum": ["gratitude", "anxiety_processing", "work_reflection", "self_compassion", "relationships", "goal_setting"]}, "count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of prompts", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20}, "time_of_day": {"type": "string", "description": "When the prompts will be used", "enum": ["morning", "midday", "evening", "any"]}, "tone": {"type": "string", "description": "Voice/style of prompts", "enum": ["supportive", "positive", "neutral", "reflective", "challenging"]}, "include_deep_prompt": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Include one deeper, more introspective prompt"}, "format": {"type": "string", "description": "Prompt presentation style", "enum": ["bullet_points", "questions", "affirmations", "free_write_starter"]}, "length_style": {"type": "string", "description": "Prompt length preference", "enum": ["one_line", "short_paragraph"]}}, "required": ["theme", "count", "time_of_day"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "compose_mindfulness_session", "description": "Create a guided mindfulness session plan and script", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"focus": {"type": "string", "description": "Primary practice type", "enum": ["breathwork", "body_scan", "compassion", "mindful_walking", "noting"]}, "duration_minutes": {"type": "integer", "description": "Session length in minutes", "minimum": 2, "maximum": 60}, "level": {"type": "string", "description": "Difficulty level", "enum": ["beginner", "intermediate"]}, "goal": {"type": "string", "description": "Intended outcome", "enum": ["stress_reduction", "anxiety_grounding", "gratitude", "focus", "sleep"]}, "include_opening_bell": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Add an opening bell cue"}, "include_closing_note": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Add a short closing integration note"}, "script_style": {"type": "string", "description": "Concise vs detailed scripting", "enum": ["concise", "detailed"]}, "pacing": {"type": "string", "description": "Suggested pacing of guidance", "enum": ["slow", "moderate"]}}, "required": ["focus", "duration_minutes", "level", "goal"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "schedule_reminder", "description": "Schedule a recurring reminder in a calendar or notification service", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"title": {"type": "string", "description": "Reminder title"}, "time": {"type": "string", "description": "Local time in HH:MM (24-hour)"}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone, e.g., America/Los_Angeles"}, "method": {"type": "string", "description": "Delivery method", "enum": ["calendar_event", "push_notification", "email"]}, "recurrence": {"type": "string", "description": "Recurrence rule", "enum": ["daily", "weekdays", "weekends", "custom"]}, "start_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Start date (YYYY-MM-DD)"}, "end_date": {"type": "string", "description": "End date (YYYY-MM-DD)"}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional notes or instructions"}, "tag": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional tag/category"}}, "required": ["title", "time", "timezone", "method", "recurrence", "start_date"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "0645005611cb74d95ee499a1bba6ea6c", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to create three packages in parallel:\n1. Morning: prompts + session\n2. Midday: prompts + session\n3. Evening: prompts + session\n\nAnd schedule three reminders.\n\nLet me make all these calls in parallel:\n\n1. generate_journal_prompts for morning (gratitude, 5 prompts, morning, supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: bullet_points, length_style: one_line)\n2. compose_mindfulness_session for morning (breathwork, 10 minutes, beginner, goal: gratitude, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true, script_style: detailed is default, pacing: slow is default)\n3. generate_journal_prompts for midday (anxiety_processing, 3 prompts, midday, supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: questions, length_style: one_line)\n4. compose_mindfulness_session for midday (mindful_walking, 5 minutes, beginner, goal: anxiety_grounding, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true)\n5. generate_journal_prompts for evening (work_reflection, 5 prompts, evening, supportive, include_deep_prompt: true, format: questions, length_style: one_line)\n6. compose_mindfulness_session for evening (body_scan, 12 minutes, beginner, goal: stress_reduction, include_opening_bell: true, include_closing_note: true)\n7. schedule_reminder for Morning Mindfulness (07:30, America/Los_Angeles, push_notification, daily, 2025-11-10 to 2025-12-10)\n8. schedule_reminder for Midday Grounding (12:00, America/Los_Angeles, push_notification, daily, 2025-11-10 to 2025-12-10)\n\n\n9. schedule_reminder for Evening Wind-down (21:30, America/Los_Angeles, calendar_event, daily, 2025-11-10 to 2025-12-10)\n\nI'll verify the default settings for the mindfulness session. The script style defaults to detailed, and pacing defaults to slow, which suits a beginner-focused 10-minute breathing exercise. The midday session involves mindful walking for 5 minutes at a beginner level, targeting anxiety grounding. I'll proceed with scheduling the Evening Wind-down reminder at 21:30, using a calendar event, with daily recurrence from November 10 to December 10, 2025.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"theme\": \"gratitude\", \"count\": 5, \"time_of_day\": \"morning\", \"tone\": \"supportive\", \"include_deep_prompt\": true, \"format\": \"bullet_points\", \"length_style\": \"one_line\"}", "name": "generate_journal_prompts"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_2", "function": {"arguments": "{\"focus\": \"breathwork\", \"duration_minutes\": 10, \"level\": \"beginner\", \"goal\": \"gratitude\", \"include_opening_bell\": true, \"include_closing_note\": true, \"script_style\": \"detailed\", \"pacing\": \"slow\"}", "name": "compose_mindfulness_session"}, "type": "function", "index": 1}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"theme\": \"anxiety_processing\", \"count\": 3, \"time_of_day\": \"midday\", \"tone\": \"supportive\", \"include_deep_prompt\": true, \"format\": \"questions\", \"length_style\": \"one_line\"}", "name": "generate_journal_prompts"}, "type": "function", "index": 2}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_4", "function": {"arguments": "{\"focus\": \"mindful_walking\", \"duration_minutes\": 5, \"level\": \"beginner\", \"goal\": \"anxiety_grounding\", \"include_opening_bell\": true, \"include_closing_note\": true, \"script_style\": \"detailed\", \"pacing\": \"slow\"}", "name": "compose_mindfulness_session"}, "type": "function", "index": 3}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_5", "function": {"arguments": "{\"theme\": \"work_reflection\", \"count\": 5, \"time_of_day\": \"evening\", \"tone\": \"supportive\", \"include_deep_prompt\": true, \"format\": \"questions\", \"length_style\": \"one_line\"}", "name": "generate_journal_prompts"}, "type": "function", "index": 4}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_6", "function": {"arguments": "{\"focus\": \"body_scan\", \"duration_minutes\": 12, \"level\": \"beginner\", \"goal\": \"stress_reduction\", \"include_opening_bell\": true, \"include_closing_note\": true, \"script_style\": \"detailed\", \"pacing\": \"slow\"}", "name": "compose_mindfulness_session"}, "type": "function", "index": 5}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_7", "function": {"arguments": "{\"title\": \"Morning Mindfulness\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"method\": \"push_notification\", \"recurrence\": \"daily\", \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"end_date\": \"2025-12-10\"}", "name": "schedule_reminder"}, "type": "function", "index": 6}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_8", "function": {"arguments": "{\"title\": \"Midday Grounding\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"method\": \"push_notification\", \"recurrence\": \"daily\", \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"end_date\": \"2025-12-10\"}", "name": "schedule_reminder"}, "type": "function", "index": 7}, {"id": "call_function_stnznlywl8jv_9", "function": {"arguments": "{\"title\": \"Evening Wind-down\", \"time\": \"21:30\", \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"method\": \"calendar_event\", \"recurrence\": \"daily\", \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"end_date\": \"2025-12-10\"}", "name": "schedule_reminder"}, "type": "function", "index": 8}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1464, "prompt_tokens": 2225, "total_tokens": 3689, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 528, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1787}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:38.233572", "duration_ms": 16011, "hash": "e2d036dc612d84f61a6c9fba91bde563", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 9}
{"data_index": 79, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I need help turning a long meeting transcript into concise notes and clear action items."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can do that. Please share the absolute file path and tell me your preferences: which sections to include (overview, decisions, action items, risks), how many summary bullets, a word cap, date timezone, and whether you want plain text or markdown.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a summary and action items from a transcript. I need the file path and output preferences before running a single summarization tool. I plan to call summarize_meeting_transcript once with the provided path, sections to include, bullet count, word cap, timezone, and output format."}, {"role": "user", "content": "It's a weekly product sync, exported from Zoom. I want key decisions, blockers, and task owners called out. Keep it concise."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Understood. I can produce a short overview with about 8 bullets, plus an Action Items list with owners and dates, calling out blockers. Which timezone should I use for due dates, and do you want items due soon tagged as urgent?", "reasoning_content": "The user prioritizes decisions, blockers (risks), and owners. I will prepare to call summarize_meeting_transcript with summary_focus=[decisions, action_items, risks], a concise bullet count, and plain text unless they request otherwise. I need the timezone and whether to tag near-term deadlines."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Format should be plain text. Include a short summary, decisions, action items with owners and due dates, and risks. Tag 'urgent' if due within 3 days."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. I’ll output plain text with an 8-bullet summary, Decisions, Action Items with owners and due dates, and Risks, tagging urgent if due within 3 days. Please provide the absolute file path, set a word cap, and confirm if ISO date format (YYYY-MM-DD) is okay.", "reasoning_content": "Preferences are set: plain text, include overview, decisions, action items, risks, with urgent tags for due within 3 days. I will call summarize_meeting_transcript with output_format='plain_text', summary_focus=['overview','decisions','action_items','risks'], urgent_threshold_days=3. I need the absolute path, a word cap, and date format."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'll send the file path next. The transcript's deadline mentions are in PST."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it—I'll normalize dates to America/Los_Angeles. When you send the path, I’ll run one summary pass. Do you want 8 bullets and a 600-word cap? If an item lacks an owner, should I mark it as Unassigned?", "reasoning_content": "PST maps to America/Los_Angeles for date normalization. I will call summarize_meeting_transcript with timezone='America/Los_Angeles'. I’m confirming bullet count and word cap, plus how to handle missing owners."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In a single run, read and summarize /home/acme/meetings/2025-10-29/product_sync/transcript.txt. Output plain text. Provide an 8-bullet summary, then an Action Items section listing owner names and due dates. Tag 'urgent' if a due date is within 3 days. Normalize dates to America/Los_Angeles in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD). Include decisions and risks, and cap the entire output at 600 words. If an item has no owner, mark it as Unassigned."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "summarize_meeting_transcript", "description": "Read a meeting transcript file (UTF-8) and produce a concise summary plus structured sections like decisions, action items with owners and due dates, and risks. Dates can be normalized to a specified timezone and urgent items tagged.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute file path to the transcript (UTF-8)"}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output format", "enum": ["plain_text", "markdown"], "default": "plain_text"}, "bullet_points": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of top summary bullets", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20, "default": 8}, "summary_focus": {"type": "array", "description": "Sections to emphasize in the summary", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["overview", "decisions", "action_items", "risks", "timeline"]}, "minItems": 1, "uniqueItems": true, "default": ["overview", "decisions", "action_items", "risks"]}, "max_words": {"type": "integer", "description": "Cap the total output length in words", "minimum": 50, "maximum": 2000, "default": 600}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone for normalizing dates (e.g., America/Los_Angeles)", "default": "UTC"}, "due_date_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Format for due dates", "enum": ["iso_date", "long", "short"], "default": "iso_date"}, "urgent_threshold_days": {"type": "integer", "description": "Tag items as urgent if due within this number of days", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 30, "default": 3}, "urgent_tag_label": {"type": "string", "description": "Label used for urgent items", "default": "urgent"}, "bullet_style": {"type": "string", "description": "Style for summary bullets", "enum": ["bulleted", "numbered"], "default": "bulleted"}, "owner_fallback_label": {"type": "string", "description": "Label to use when an owner is not detected", "default": "Unassigned"}, "include_unknown_owner": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Include action items even if no owner is detected", "default": true}}, "required": ["path"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500563f84293b94f9896548d7f570", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to summarize a meeting transcript. Let me extract the parameters:\n\n- Path: /home/acme/meetings/2025-10-29/product_sync/transcript.txt\n- Output format: plain_text\n- Summary bullets: 8\n- Sections: overview, decisions, action_items, risks\n- Max words: 600\n- Timezone: America/Los_Angeles\n- Due date format: iso_date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- Urgent threshold: 3 days\n- Urgent tag label: urgent\n- Bullet style: bulleted (default)\n- Owner fallback label: Unassigned\n- Include unknown owner: true (default)\n\nI need to call the summarize_meeting_transcript function with these parameters.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_vd6ll0v12iqc_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/acme/meetings/2025-10-29/product_sync/transcript.txt\", \"output_format\": \"plain_text\", \"bullet_points\": 8, \"summary_focus\": [\"overview\", \"decisions\", \"action_items\", \"risks\"], \"max_words\": 600, \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"due_date_format\": \"iso_date\", \"urgent_threshold_days\": 3, \"urgent_tag_label\": \"urgent\", \"owner_fallback_label\": \"Unassigned\"}", "name": "summarize_meeting_transcript"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 328, "prompt_tokens": 1150, "total_tokens": 1478, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 157, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 891}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:29.968675", "duration_ms": 7650, "hash": "e932a13031235ee1761b14d20abb07e9", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 80, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I just adopted a 2-year-old mixed-breed dog and want to set up a routine for vaccinations, feeding, and walks."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Congrats! To tailor a plan, please share:\n- Weight and whether he’s neutered\n- Your location (helps with vaccine risk like Leptospirosis)\n- Known vaccine dates (rabies, DHPP, Bordetella, Lepto)\n- Food brand/formula and current meal times\n- Current walk frequency and typical durations", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a tailored routine. I need core details (weight, sex/neuter, location, current vaccines, diet, current schedule) to personalize feeding amounts, walk durations, and vaccine timelines. No tools are needed; this is general pet-care guidance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "He’s a 2-year-old neutered male, 25 lb (~11.3 kg). We live in Miami, FL. Vet records show rabies and DHPP both on 2024-08-15. No Bordetella or Lepto yet. Food: Purina Pro Plan Adult Chicken & Rice dry kibble. We currently feed ~1 cup at 7:00 am and ~1 cup at 6:30 pm. Walks are 3 times daily; he’s moderately active."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great details. Here’s a starting plan:\n- Feeding: Estimated need ~690 kcal/day for a 25 lb neutered, moderately active dog. Purina Pro Plan adult kibble is roughly 360–400 kcal per cup (check your bag for the exact value). Target about 1.75–2 cups/day total. As grams, that’s ~170–190 g/day; split into two meals ≈85–95 g per meal (about 0.85–0.95 cups each).\n- Walks: Aim for 20–30 min in the morning, 15–20 min midday, and 30–45 min in the evening with some sniffing time.\n- Vaccines (Miami):\n  - Leptospirosis: Start a 2-dose series (2–4 weeks apart), then annually.\n  - Bordetella: Annually; if boarding often, consider every 6 months.\n  - Rabies: Depends on certificate (1-year vs 3-year). If 1-year, likely due August 2025.\n  - DHPP: Typically every 3 years after the adult booster; likely due in 2027.\nLet me know if your rabies certificate is 1-year or 3-year so I can pin the due date.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll estimate daily calories using MER and map that to cups/grams with a reasonable kibble density, then set a baseline walk plan and vaccine recommendations for Miami (Lepto and Bordetella). I’ll ask to confirm rabies certificate length to time the next rabies due date. No tools needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We use Zuke’s Mini treats (about 3 kcal each), usually 6–8 per day during training. Could you convert your feeding plan to exact grams and cups per meal and suggest how to offset for treats? Also, any weekly walk structure you recommend?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Feeding per meal (twice daily):\n- Start at ~85–90 g per meal (≈0.85–0.9 cups if your kibble is ~95–105 g/cup). Verify the kcal/cup on your bag and adjust by ±5 g.\nTreat offset:\n- 6–8 treats × ~3 kcal = ~18–24 kcal/day. Reduce kibble by ~10–15 g/day total (about 5–8 g per meal).\nWeekly walk structure:\n- Mon–Fri: Morning 25–30 min; midday 15–20 min; evening 35–45 min.\n- Weekend: One longer outing 60–90 min (split if it’s hot), plus a short recovery walk later.\n- Add 1–2 short “sniffy” sessions (10–15 min) on training-heavy days.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll translate the daily amount into per-meal grams/cups and subtract treat calories by reducing kibble slightly. I’ll provide a simple weekly walk structure with one longer session. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "His stool is generally firm but gets soft the day after trying new treats. Hydration-wise, how much water should he get in Miami heat, and any tips to keep him cool?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Treats:\n- Introduce one new treat at a time for 3–4 days; keep to small amounts.\n- Prefer single-ingredient treats; avoid rich/fatty options.\n- If stool softens, pause the new treat and reintroduce later in smaller amounts.\nHydration:\n- Baseline 50–80 ml/kg/day. For 11.3 kg, that’s ~565–900 ml/day. On hot days, aim toward the upper end.\n- Offer water at every outing; consider adding a splash of water to meals.\nHeat tips:\n- Walk early/late, avoid midday sun; use shade and rest breaks.\n- Paw check on hot pavement; consider cooling mat/vest.\n- Watch for heat stress: excessive panting, drooling, lethargy. If noted, stop activity, move to cool area, offer water.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll give a treat-introduction protocol and hydration targets (ml/kg/day) with Miami heat adjustments, plus cooling strategies and warning signs. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I want reminders for starting Lepto and Bordetella, and to plan ahead for rabies and DHPP. I prefer reminders on the 1st of a month. Can you lay them out for the next year?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure. Please confirm:\n- Which start month?\n- Rabies certificate length (1-year or 3-year)?\n- How often you board (rarely vs regularly)?\nThen I’ll lay out month-by-month items on the 1st of each month for the next year.", "reasoning_content": "To lay out month-by-month items, I need the start month and rabies certificate length. Boarding frequency affects Bordetella cadence. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Start in March 2025. The rabies certificate is 1-year. DHPP was the adult booster on 2024-08-15. We occasionally board (a few weekends per year)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Month-by-month (1st of each month, Mar 2025–Feb 2026):\n- Mar 1: Lepto dose 1; book dose 2 for Mar 15–29. Feeding ~85–90 g per meal; walks AM 25–30, midday 15–20, PM 35–45.\n- Apr 1: Bordetella (annual). Confirm Lepto series completed; keep feeding/walks.\n- May 1: As heat rises, plan shorter midday walks (10–15) if heat index >95°F; keep morning/evening as above.\n- Jun 1: Pre-summer check-in; ensure cooling gear; feeding unchanged unless weight shifts.\n- Jul 1: Peak heat protocol: midday 8–12 min max; add indoor enrichment.\n- Aug 1: Schedule rabies for week of Aug 8–15; add annual wellness exam and verify DHPP status (not due until 2027).\n- Sep 1: Reassess weight/BCS; adjust meals ±5% if needed; extend midday back to 15–20 if cooler.\n- Oct 1: Optional Bordetella booster if boarding this fall/winter (some facilities require within 6 months).\n- Nov 1: Cooler weather: resume midday 15–20 comfortably; feeding unchanged.\n- Dec 1: Holiday planning; stick to routine feeding/walks; pack records if traveling.\n- Jan 1: New-year check-in; confirm vaccine records, feeding amount still appropriate.\n- Feb 1: Plan Lepto annual booster next month; keep walks/feeding steady.", "reasoning_content": "I will now create a concise March 2025–February 2026 plan with items on the 1st of each month: Lepto series timing, Bordetella, rabies in August 2025, and DHPP status. I’ll include steady feeding/walk references with seasonal adjustments. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "For walks, suggest durations at 7:15 am, 12:30 pm, and 6:30 pm, with a weekend longer outing. Include adjustments for heat index over 95°F and heavy rain."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Daily:\n- 7:15 am: 25–30 min (can extend to 35 min on cooler days).\n- 12:30 pm: 15–20 min.\n- 6:30 pm: 35–45 min with sniffing stops.\nWeekend longer outing:\n- 60–90 min total (split into two sessions if hot: 40–50 min early + 20–30 min late).\nAdjustments:\n- Heat index >95°F: shorten midday to 8–12 min; shift most activity to early morning/late evening; add shade and water breaks every 10–15 min.\n- Heavy rain: 5–10 min potty-only; use indoor enrichment (nose work, puzzle feeder, hide-and-seek) for 20–30 min.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll map the user’s times to durations and give clear adjustments for high heat index and heavy rain, plus indoor alternatives. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "On longer hike days, how should we adjust food and treats? Also, what body condition score should we aim for, and how do I do a quick check?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Long hike days:\n- Add ~10–20% to daily calories. Practically, increase each meal by ~10 g or add a small third snack meal.\n- Use higher-value but light treats; keep total treat calories ≤10% of daily intake.\nBody Condition Score (BCS):\n- Aim for 4–5/9.\nQuick check:\n- Ribs: easily felt with light pressure, not sharply visible.\n- Waist: visible from above; tummy tuck from the side.\n- If ribs are hard to feel or waist is absent, reduce meals by ~5–10% and recheck in 2–3 weeks.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll provide a simple caloric bump for strenuous days, treat guidance, and a quick BCS checklist with the target range. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We’re planning a 6-hour car trip in June. What should I pack and how often should we stop? He uses a crash-tested harness. Any advice on anxiety or sedation?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Pack:\n- Water (1–2 liters), collapsible bowl, pre-portioned food, treats\n- Poop bags, towels/wipes, extra leash, ID tags/microchip info\n- Vaccine records, any meds, first-aid basics\n- Sunshade and cooling mat\nStops:\n- Every 2–3 hours for 10–15 minutes (water and potty). Avoid feeding big meals right before departure.\nAnxiety:\n- Pre-trip practice rides; familiar bed/blanket; calming chews, pheromone spray (DAP), white-noise/music.\n- If needed, ask your vet about trialing non-sedating options (e.g., trazodone or gabapentin) before travel. Avoid heavy sedatives without veterinary guidance.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll list a practical packing checklist, stopping cadence, heat precautions, and anxiety strategies, cautioning against sedatives unless vet-advised. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please give me a concise monthly care checklist for March 2025–February 2026 that I can follow. Cover vaccinations due, feeding amounts per meal, typical walk durations for my times, and note any month-specific adjustments (heat or holidays). Bullets only, no tables."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_sql_query", "description": "Execute a SQL query on a database and return results (irrelevant to pet care)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "SQL to execute"}, "database": {"type": "string", "description": "Database name or connection string"}, "timeout_ms": {"type": "integer", "description": "Timeout in milliseconds", "minimum": 100, "maximum": 60000}}, "required": ["query", "database"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "convert_image_format", "description": "Convert an image file to another format (irrelevant to pet care)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to source image"}, "target_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output image format", "enum": ["png", "jpeg", "webp"]}, "quality": {"type": "integer", "description": "Output quality (if applicable)", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 100}}, "required": ["source_path", "target_format"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500569cf188d3174be08bf32dd163", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants a concise monthly care checklist for March 2025 through February 2026. They want bullets only, no tables. They want it to cover:\n- Vaccinations due\n- Feeding amounts per meal\n- Typical walk durations for their times (7:15 am, 12:30 pm, 6:30 pm, plus weekend longer outing)\n- Month-specific adjustments (heat or holidays)\n\nLet me compile all the information from our previous conversation:\n\nVaccinations:\n- Mar 2025: Lepto dose 1; book dose 2 for Mar 15–29\n- Apr 2025: Bordetella (annual)\n- Aug 2025: Rabies (due around Aug 8-15, 1-year)\n- DHPP was adult booster on 2024-08-15, due in 2027\n- Lepto: annual booster due Feb 2026\n- Optional Bordetella: Oct 2025 if boarding fall/winter\n\nFeeding:\n- About 85–90 g per meal (twice daily), with 10–15 g reduction for treats\n- Adjust based on weight/BCS\n- Need to account for treats: 6–8 treats × ~3 kcal = ~18–24 kcal/day; reduce kibble by ~10–15 g/day\n\nWalk durations:\n- 7:15 am: 25–30 min (can extend to 35 on cooler days)\n- 12:30 pm: 15–20 min (shorten to 8–12 min if heat index >95°F)\n- 6:30 pm: 35–45 min with sniffing\n- Weekend longer outing: 60–90 min total\n\nMonth-specific adjustments:\n- Mar 2025: Lepto dose 1; start of routine\n- Apr 2025: Bordetella\n- May 2025: heat rising - plan shorter midday walks if heat index >95°F\n- Jun 2025: peak heat protocol; car trip planning\n\n\n- Jul 2025: peak heat - midday 8-12 min max; indoor enrichment\n- Aug 2025: rabies due around Aug 8-15; annual wellness exam\n- Sep 2025: reassess weight/BCS; adjust meals ±5%\n- Oct 2025: optional Bordetella if boarding fall/winter\n- Nov 2025: cooler weather\n- Dec 2025: holiday planning\n- Jan 2026: new year check-in\n- Feb 2026: plan Lepto annual booster\n\nI'll structure this as a month-by-month checklist with key care activities, ensuring all critical health and seasonal considerations are captured systematically.\n</think>\n\n**March 2025**\n- Lepto dose 1; schedule dose 2 for Mar 15–29\n- Feed ~85–90 g per meal (2× daily); reduce 5–8 g per meal if treating\n- Walks: 7:15 am 25–30 min, 12:30 pm 15–20 min, 6:30 pm 35–45 min; weekend 60–90 min outing\n\n**April 2025**\n- Bordetella (annual)\n- Feeding and walks same as March\n\n**May 2025**\n- Heat index rising; shorten midday to 10–15 min if >95°F\n- Ensure cooling mat/vest available\n- Feeding and walks same as March\n\n**June 2025**\n- Peak heat: midday 8–12 min max; walk early/late; add water breaks every 10–15 min\n- Pack car trip supplies: water, bowl, food, treats, vaccine records, cooling mat, first-aid\n- Stop every 2–3 hours on car trip\n- Feeding: add 10–20% calories on longer hike days\n\n**July 2025**\n- Peak heat protocol; use indoor enrichment\n- Walks: 7:15 am 25–30 min, 12:30 pm 8–12 min, 6:30 pm 35–45 min; weekend 60–90 min split into early + late\n\n**August 2025**\n- Rabies due around Aug 8–15; schedule vet visit\n- Annual wellness exam; verify DHPP (not due until 2027)\n- Feeding and walks same as June; reassess weight mid-month\n\n**September 2025**\n- Reassess BCS; adjust meals ±5% if needed; extend midday to 15–20 min if cooler\n- Walks: 7:15 am 25–30 min, 12:30 pm 15–20 min, 6:30 pm 35–45 min; weekend 60–90 min\n\n**October 2025**\n- Optional Bordetella booster if boarding fall/winter (within 6 months)\n- Fall check-in; feeding and walks same as September\n\n**November 2025**\n- Feeding and walks same as September; holiday planning for any travel\n\n**December 2025**\n- Stick to routine; pack vaccine records if traveling; avoid table scraps\n\n**January 2026**\n- New-year check-in; confirm vaccine records; verify feeding amount still appropriate\n- Walks: 7:15 am 25–30 min, 12:30 pm 15–20 min, 6:30 pm 35–45 min; weekend 60–90 min\n\n**February 2026**\n- Plan Lepto annual booster for March; keep feeding and walks steady\n- Mid-winter weight check; adjust if BCS >5/9", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1165, "prompt_tokens": 2478, "total_tokens": 3643, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 560, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 2235}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "stop", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:38.395459", "duration_ms": 15882, "hash": "98c308e93726ce04e26e938c8b9c7cb9", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": false, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "stop", "tool_calls_valid": null, "tool_calls_count": 0}
{"data_index": 81, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm preparing for several finals and want a spaced repetition study plan that fits my weekly schedule."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great — I can build a day-by-day plan with spaced reviews aligned to your exam dates. Please provide:\n- Start date and each subject’s exam date\n- Subjects with difficulty, target hours, and any key materials\n- Your weekly availability by day (time blocks and max minutes)\n- Preferences: algorithm (SM2/Leitner/custom intervals), session length, rest days, buffer days, review intensity\n- Constraints: max daily minutes, times to avoid, dates to skip\n- Timezone and desired output format (calendar, list, or CSV)", "reasoning_content": "The user needs a customized study plan using spaced repetition across multiple subjects. To generate it, I should collect concrete inputs (dates, subjects, availability, preferences, constraints) and then make a single call to a plan-generation tool. I will ask for: start date; each subject with exam date, difficulty, materials, target hours; daily availability per weekday with time blocks and max minutes; algorithm preference (SM2/Leitner/custom), session length, rest days, buffer days, review intensity; any constraints (max daily minutes, avoid times, blackout dates); timezone and output format. Once provided, I will call generate_spaced_repetition_plan with those parameters in one tool call."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please generate a spaced repetition plan with these details:\n- Start date: 2025-11-10\n- Subjects:\n  • Calculus I — exam 2025-12-18; difficulty hard; materials: \"Textbook Ch1–7\", \"Past exams 2019–2024\"; target_hours: 30\n  • Organic Chemistry — exam 2025-12-16; difficulty medium; materials: \"Lecture notes weeks 1–12\", \"Reactions deck\"; target_hours: 24\n  • World History — exam 2025-12-20; difficulty easy; materials: \"Textbook Ch10–18\"; target_hours: 18\n- Daily availability:\n  • Monday: max 120 min; time block 18:30–21:00\n  • Tuesday: max 120 min; time block 18:30–21:00\n  • Wednesday: max 120 min; time block 18:30–21:00\n  • Thursday: max 120 min; time block 18:30–21:00\n  • Friday: max 90 min; time block 17:30–19:00\n  • Saturday: max 180 min; time block 10:00–13:00\n  • Sunday: max 0 min (rest day)\n- Preferences: algorithm SM2; session length 45 minutes; rest days: Sunday; include buffer days: true; review intensity: normal\n- Constraints: max_daily_minutes 180; avoid_times: Wednesday 20:00–21:00 and Friday 19:00–20:00; no_sessions_on: 2025-11-28 and 2025-12-05\n- Timezone: America/New_York\n- Output format: calendar"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "generate_spaced_repetition_plan", "description": "Generate a study plan with spaced repetition across multiple subjects up to their exam dates. Returns a day-by-day schedule of study sessions and review intervals.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"start_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Planning start date in YYYY-MM-DD"}, "subjects": {"type": "array", "description": "List of subjects with exam info and goals", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string", "description": "Subject name"}, "exam_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Exam date in YYYY-MM-DD"}, "difficulty": {"type": "string", "description": "Relative difficulty", "enum": ["easy", "medium", "hard"]}, "materials": {"type": "array", "description": "Study materials references", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "target_hours": {"type": "number", "description": "Total target study hours for the subject", "minimum": 1}}, "required": ["name", "exam_date", "difficulty"]}, "minItems": 1}, "daily_availability": {"type": "array", "description": "Available study time by day of week", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"day_of_week": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]}, "max_minutes": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 600}, "time_blocks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"start": {"type": "string", "description": "Start time HH:MM (24h)"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "End time HH:MM (24h)"}}, "required": ["start", "end"]}, "minItems": 0}}, "required": ["day_of_week", "max_minutes"]}, "minItems": 7, "maxItems": 7}, "preferences": {"type": "object", "properties": {"algorithm": {"type": "string", "enum": ["SM2", "Leitner", "custom_intervals"]}, "session_length_minutes": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 20, "maximum": 120}, "rest_days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]}}, "include_buffer_days": {"type": "boolean"}, "review_intensity": {"type": "string", "enum": ["light", "normal", "aggressive"]}, "intervals": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}, "description": "Only used when algorithm is custom_intervals"}}, "required": ["algorithm", "session_length_minutes"]}, "constraints": {"type": "object", "properties": {"max_daily_minutes": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 600}, "avoid_times": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"day_of_week": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]}, "start": {"type": "string", "description": "Start time HH:MM (24h)"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "End time HH:MM (24h)"}}, "required": ["day_of_week", "start", "end"]}}, "no_sessions_on": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "description": "Date in YYYY-MM-DD"}}}}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone (e.g., America/New_York)"}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "enum": ["calendar", "list", "csv"]}}, "required": ["start_date", "subjects", "daily_availability", "preferences"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450056611449a858528e57209036f1", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to generate a spaced repetition study plan with very specific details. Let me extract all the information:\n\n**Start date:** 2025-11-10\n\n**Subjects:**\n1. Calculus I - exam 2025-12-18, difficulty hard, materials: \"Textbook Ch1–7\", \"Past exams 2019–2024\", target_hours: 30\n2. Organic Chemistry - exam 2025-12-16, difficulty medium, materials: \"Lecture notes weeks 1–12\", \"Reactions deck\", target_hours: 24\n3. World History - exam 2025-12-20, difficulty easy, materials: \"Textbook Ch10–18\", target_hours: 18\n\n**Daily availability:**\n- Monday: max 120 min, time block 18:30–21:00\n- Tuesday: max 120 min, time block 18:30–21:00\n- Wednesday: max 120 min, time block 18:30–21:00\n- Thursday: max 120 min, time block 18:30–21:00\n- Friday: max 90 min, time block 17:30–19:00\n- Saturday: max 180 min, time block 10:00–13:00\n- Sunday: max 0 min (rest day)\n\n**Preferences:**\n- algorithm: SM2\n- session_length_minutes: 45\n- rest_days: Sunday\n- include_buffer_days: true\n- review_intensity: normal\n\n**Constraints:**\n- max_daily_minutes: 180\n- avoid_times: Wednesday 20:00–21:00 and Friday 19:00–20:00\n- no_sessions_on: 2025-11-28 and 2025-12-05\n\n**Timezone:** America/New_York\n**Output format:** calendar\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON object for the tool call. Let me carefully structure each part:\n\n\nI'll map out the time blocks and daily availability, ensuring precise scheduling across different days of the week. The time blocks reflect the specific study windows, with varying durations and start times to accommodate each day's constraints.\n\nI'll break down the subjects, noting their exam dates and difficulty levels. Each subject has a targeted number of study hours, ranging from 18 to 30 hours, with exams spread across mid-December. The study plan needs to strategically allocate time based on subject complexity and proximity to exams.\n\nThe algorithm preferences are set to SM2, with 45-minute sessions and buffer days included. Wednesday evening and Friday evening have specific time slots to avoid, and there are two designated session-free dates in late November and early December. The goal is to create a structured, efficient study schedule that maximizes preparation time while allowing for rest and flexibility.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_nbvbimumsali_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"subjects\": [{\"name\": \"Calculus I\", \"exam_date\": \"2025-12-18\", \"difficulty\": \"hard\", \"materials\": [\"Textbook Ch1–7\", \"Past exams 2019–2024\"], \"target_hours\": 30}, {\"name\": \"Organic Chemistry\", \"exam_date\": \"2025-12-16\", \"difficulty\": \"medium\", \"materials\": [\"Lecture notes weeks 1–12\", \"Reactions deck\"], \"target_hours\": 24}, {\"name\": \"World History\", \"exam_date\": \"2025-12-20\", \"difficulty\": \"easy\", \"materials\": [\"Textbook Ch10–18\"], \"target_hours\": 18}], \"daily_availability\": [{\"day_of_week\": \"Mon\", \"max_minutes\": 120, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"18:30\", \"end\": \"21:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Tue\", \"max_minutes\": 120, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"18:30\", \"end\": \"21:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Wed\", \"max_minutes\": 120, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"18:30\", \"end\": \"21:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Thu\", \"max_minutes\": 120, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"18:30\", \"end\": \"21:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Fri\", \"max_minutes\": 90, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"17:30\", \"end\": \"19:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Sat\", \"max_minutes\": 180, \"time_blocks\": [{\"start\": \"10:00\", \"end\": \"13:00\"}]}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Sun\", \"max_minutes\": 0, \"time_blocks\": []}], \"preferences\": {\"algorithm\": \"SM2\", \"session_length_minutes\": 45, \"rest_days\": [\"Sun\"], \"include_buffer_days\": true, \"review_intensity\": \"normal\"}, \"constraints\": {\"max_daily_minutes\": 180, \"avoid_times\": [{\"day_of_week\": \"Wed\", \"start\": \"20:00\", \"end\": \"21:00\"}, {\"day_of_week\": \"Fri\", \"start\": \"19:00\", \"end\": \"20:00\"}], \"no_sessions_on\": [\"2025-11-28\", \"2025-12-05\"]}, \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"output_format\": \"calendar\"}", "name": "generate_spaced_repetition_plan"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1205, "prompt_tokens": 1576, "total_tokens": 2781, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 589, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1339}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:37.898535", "duration_ms": 15257, "hash": "f14b8fb6b77961b814bc71fc9a815460", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 82, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm starting two new medications this week and need help setting up reminders and checking for drug interactions."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Happy to help. Please share the medication names, doses, the times you prefer to take them, start/end dates if any, your time zone, and how you want reminders delivered (SMS, push, or email).", "reasoning_content": "The user wants medication reminders and an interaction check. I need structured details (drug names, doses, schedule, timezone, and reminder channel) to make a single tool call to create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "The meds are clarithromycin 500 mg twice daily for a week, and simvastatin 40 mg nightly. I’m in Boston."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. Clarithromycin can strongly interact with simvastatin (risk of muscle toxicity), so I’ll include warnings. What times do you want for each, and what start date? Also, where should I send reminders (e.g., SMS number)?", "reasoning_content": "I have the drug names, doses, and location. Clarithromycin can strongly interact with simvastatin. I will gather exact times, a start date, and the reminder destination to prepare parameters for create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Clarithromycin at 09:00 and 21:00. Simvastatin at 22:00. Start clarithromycin on 2025-11-10. Send reminders by SMS to +1-617-555-0142."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. I’ll use America/New_York for Boston. Do you have quiet hours to avoid late-night pings, and a short label for the reminders (e.g., “Meds”)?", "reasoning_content": "I now have times, start date, and SMS. I will confirm the time zone (America/New_York) and collect quiet hours and a label to finalize the reminders object for create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Quiet hours 23:00–07:00, and deliver reminders right after quiet hours. Label them “Meds.”"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Please provide your patient ID, any allergies, and other routine medications I should include and screen.", "reasoning_content": "Quiet hours and label received. I need a patient ID, allergies, and other routine meds to check interactions comprehensively before calling create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Patient ID is pt_92831. Allergy: penicillin. I also take metformin 1000 mg twice daily."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. What times do you take metformin, and is it ongoing or for a set duration?", "reasoning_content": "We’ll add metformin to the schedule. I need its specific times and whether it’s ongoing, then I can include it in medications for create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Metformin at 08:00 and 20:00, daily, ongoing."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Understood. Do you want reminders to arrive a set number of minutes before each dose? If so, what offset?", "reasoning_content": "Metformin schedule is clear. I’ll include clarithromycin–simvastatin warnings. I need your reminder offset (e.g., 10–15 minutes before dose) to finish the reminders config for create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes, set the offset to 15 minutes before each dose. Don’t pause simvastatin—just warn me about the interaction."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Would you like repeats if you don’t confirm (e.g., every 10 minutes up to 3 times)? Any note like “Take with water” to attach to the reminders?", "reasoning_content": "Offset and warning preference confirmed. I will gather snooze/repeat policy and any note to include, then I’ll be ready to prepare the single call to create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repeat every 10 minutes up to 3 times. Add the note “Take with water.” Deliver reminders immediately after quiet hours."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Please confirm: start all on 2025-11-10; clarithromycin for 7 days (ending 2025-11-16); time zone America/New_York; and that you acknowledge this isn’t medical advice.", "reasoning_content": "Repeat policy and note captured. I’ll confirm the start date, clarithromycin end date (7 days), timezone, and acknowledgment to finalize parameters for create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Confirmed: start 2025-11-10, clarithromycin ends 2025-11-16, America/New_York, and I acknowledge this isn’t medical advice."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Summary: pt_92831; America/New_York; clarithromycin 500 mg at 09:00 and 21:00 from 2025-11-10 to 2025-11-16; simvastatin 40 mg at 22:00 ongoing; metformin 1000 mg at 08:00 and 20:00 ongoing; SMS +1-617-555-0142; label “Meds”; offset 15 min; repeats every 10 min up to 3; quiet hours 23:00–07:00 with delivery right after. Shall I proceed?", "reasoning_content": "All inputs are complete. I’ll summarize and request a final go-ahead, then make a single call to create_medication_schedule with the patient ID, timezone, three medications (clarithromycin, simvastatin, metformin), and the reminders configuration including quiet hours and repeats."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Go ahead and set it up."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Please send a final confirmation listing patient_id, timezone, each medication (name, dose, route, fixed times, start/end dates), and the reminder settings (method, destination, label, offset, repeats, quiet hours). I’ll then create the schedule and run the interaction check in one call.", "reasoning_content": "To execute the single tool call cleanly, I’ll ask for a final structured confirmation so I can pass exact parameters to create_medication_schedule."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create the medication schedule and run the interaction check in one go for patient pt_92831, timezone America/New_York. Medications: 1) Clarithromycin 500 mg oral, fixed times 09:00 and 21:00, start 2025-11-10, end 2025-11-16, notes “Take with water”, warn interactions true; 2) Simvastatin 40 mg oral, fixed time 22:00, start 2025-11-10, ongoing, notes “Take with water”, warn interactions true; 3) Metformin 1000 mg oral, fixed times 08:00 and 20:00, start 2025-11-10, ongoing, notes “Take with water”, warn interactions true. Reminders: method SMS, destination +1-617-555-0142, label “Meds”, offset 15 minutes, repeat every 10 minutes up to 3 times, quiet hours 23:00–07:00 with delivery right after. Allergies: penicillin. Conditions: type 2 diabetes. I acknowledge the disclaimer."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "create_medication_schedule", "description": "Create medication reminders and check for interactions for a patient", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"patient_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Unique patient identifier"}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA time zone, e.g., America/New_York"}, "interaction_check": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Run a drug-drug interaction scan"}, "allergies": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Known allergies (e.g., penicillin)"}, "conditions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Known conditions (e.g., type 2 diabetes)"}, "medications": {"type": "array", "description": "List of medications to schedule", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string", "description": "Medication name"}, "dose": {"type": "object", "properties": {"amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Dose amount"}, "unit": {"type": "string", "enum": ["mg", "mcg", "g", "ml", "units"], "description": "Dose unit"}}, "required": ["amount", "unit"]}, "route": {"type": "string", "enum": ["oral", "subcutaneous", "intramuscular", "topical", "inhalation"]}, "schedule": {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["fixed_times", "interval"]}, "times": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$"}, "description": "HH:MM local times for fixed_times"}, "every_hours": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 24, "description": "Interval hours"}, "first_time": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$", "description": "First dose time for interval schedules"}}, "required": ["type"]}, "start_date": {"type": "string", "format": "date", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD start date"}, "end_date": {"type": "string", "format": "date", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD end date (omit for ongoing)"}, "prn": {"type": "boolean", "default": false, "description": "As needed"}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Reminder note or instructions"}, "warn_interactions": {"type": "boolean", "default": true, "description": "Show warnings if interactions exist"}}, "required": ["name", "dose", "route", "schedule"]}}, "reminders": {"type": "object", "properties": {"method": {"type": "string", "enum": ["sms", "push", "email"], "description": "Delivery method"}, "destination": {"type": "string", "description": "Phone number, device ID, or email"}, "label": {"type": "string", "description": "Short reminder label"}, "offset_min": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 120, "description": "Minutes before dose to notify"}, "repeat": {"type": "object", "properties": {"interval_min": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 60}, "max_times": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 10}}, "required": ["interval_min", "max_times"]}, "quiet_hours": {"type": "object", "properties": {"start": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$", "description": "HH:MM start"}, "end": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$", "description": "HH:MM end"}, "deliver_after_quiet": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Deliver suppressed reminders immediately after quiet hours"}}, "required": ["start", "end"]}}, "required": ["method", "destination", "label", "offset_min"]}, "disclaimer_ack": {"type": "boolean", "description": "User acknowledges non-medical advice"}}, "required": ["patient_id", "timezone", "medications", "reminders", "interaction_check"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500565f2dd91db6b7516b0ca1c2f5", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to create a medication schedule with all the details they've provided. Let me organize the information:\n\n- patient_id: pt_92831\n- timezone: America/New_York\n- interaction_check: true\n- allergies: [\"penicillin\"]\n- conditions: [\"type 2 diabetes\"]\n- medications:\n  1. Clarithromycin 500 mg oral, fixed times 09:00 and 21:00, start 2025-11-10, end 2025-11-16, notes \"Take with water\", warn interactions true\n  2. Simvastatin 40 mg oral, fixed time 22:00, start 2025-11-10, ongoing (no end date), notes \"Take with water\", warn interactions true\n  3. Metformin 1000 mg oral, fixed times 08:00 and 20:00, start 2025-11-10, ongoing (no end date), notes \"Take with water\", warn interactions true\n\nReminders:\n- method: SMS\n- destination: +1-617-555-0142\n- label: \"Meds\"\n- offset_min: 15\n- repeat: interval_min: 10, max_times: 3\n- quiet_hours: start: \"23:00\", end: \"07:00\", deliver_after_quiet: true\n\ndisclaimer_ack: true\n\nLet me structure this properly for the function call.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_4plg9dlmo015_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"patient_id\": \"pt_92831\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"interaction_check\": true, \"allergies\": [\"penicillin\"], \"conditions\": [\"type 2 diabetes\"], \"medications\": [{\"name\": \"Clarithromycin\", \"dose\": {\"amount\": 500, \"unit\": \"mg\"}, \"route\": \"oral\", \"schedule\": {\"type\": \"fixed_times\", \"times\": [\"09:00\", \"21:00\"]}, \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"end_date\": \"2025-11-16\", \"notes\": \"Take with water\", \"warn_interactions\": true}, {\"name\": \"Simvastatin\", \"dose\": {\"amount\": 40, \"unit\": \"mg\"}, \"route\": \"oral\", \"schedule\": {\"type\": \"fixed_times\", \"times\": [\"22:00\"]}, \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"notes\": \"Take with water\", \"warn_interactions\": true}, {\"name\": \"Metformin\", \"dose\": {\"amount\": 1000, \"unit\": \"mg\"}, \"route\": \"oral\", \"schedule\": {\"type\": \"fixed_times\", \"times\": [\"08:00\", \"20:00\"]}, \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"notes\": \"Take with water\", \"warn_interactions\": true}], \"reminders\": {\"method\": \"sms\", \"destination\": \"+1-617-555-0142\", \"label\": \"Meds\", \"offset_min\": 15, \"repeat\": {\"interval_min\": 10, \"max_times\": 3}, \"quiet_hours\": {\"start\": \"23:00\", \"end\": \"07:00\", \"deliver_after_quiet\": true}}, \"disclaimer_ack\": true}", "name": "create_medication_schedule"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 741, "prompt_tokens": 2158, "total_tokens": 2899, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 302, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1787}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:32.888955", "duration_ms": 10166, "hash": "838da28a83ed798e045461b6ae27fbd8", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 83, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm tracking my household electricity and want help analyzing usage to cut the bill."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can analyze your interval data and suggest targeted savings. Please share the absolute path to your usage file (CSV or JSON), the sampling interval, your time zone, and the date range to analyze. Also tell me your tariff plan name/type.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants an energy analysis and savings guidance. To proceed I need the data source and context. Plan: gather file path, interval, timezone, date range, and tariff details, then call analyze_electricity_usage with source_type, usage_path, interval_minutes, timezone, start/end dates, and tariff_plan."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Usage file is /data/energy/usage_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv. It's 30-minute intervals in America/Los_Angeles. Analyze 2025-06-01 through 2025-08-31. Plan is PG&E E-TOU-C in USD."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. Do you have the TOU peak/off-peak windows and rates? If you have solar generation logs, share the file path. And give a quick building profile: size, occupants, HVAC and water heater types, EV or PV.", "reasoning_content": "To estimate bills and peak-hour share I need the TOU windows and rates. If PV exists, pv_path improves self-consumption analysis. I will populate tariff_plan.tou_periods and pv_path, and I also need building_profile."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Weekdays: 16:00–21:00 peak at $0.56/kWh; off-peak otherwise at $0.32/kWh. Weekends all day $0.32/kWh. I have a 5 kW PV system; generation CSV is at /data/energy/pv_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Please share home size in sqft, number of occupants, HVAC type, water heater type, and whether you have an EV. That helps estimate standby and comfort constraints.", "reasoning_content": "Building details help model standby and HVAC impact. I will collect home size, occupants, HVAC, water heater, EV presence to fill building_profile in the tool call."}, {"role": "user", "content": "1850 sqft, 4 occupants, heat pump HVAC, heat-pump water heater, one EV, PV present."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To tailor tips, what thermostat setpoints do you use, typical occupancy hours, and any large loads (pool pump, dryer, PCs, etc.) with usual schedules?", "reasoning_content": "Setpoints, occupancy, and large-load schedules enable appliance-impact insights. I plan to add appliance_profiles (e.g., pool pump) into the analyze_electricity_usage parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Summer: 74°F evenings, 76°F daytime. Weekdays we’re away 9:00–15:00, home evenings. Loads: pool pump (1 hp) 10:00–14:00, electric dryer, induction cooktop, two desktop PCs, and two window fans."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. Do you use smart plugs or can you shift some loads manually? Any EV charging schedule? And confirm weekends use off‑peak all day under E‑TOU‑C.", "reasoning_content": "Flexibility and EV schedule affect actionable tips and cost. I’ll capture ability to shift loads, EV charging times, and confirm weekend rates in tariff_plan. I will prepare ev_profile."}, {"role": "user", "content": "No smart plugs; we can shift manually. Weekends are off-peak all day. EV usually charges at night; I'll share times if needed."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. I propose computing baseline usage, peak-hour share, standby load, PV self-consumption, EV impact, pool pump impact, bill estimate, and top savings tips. Which metrics do you want and should the report be summary or detailed?", "reasoning_content": "We need to lock in output_metrics and return_format to configure the tool call. I’ll set the requested metrics and report type for analyze_electricity_usage."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please include baseline_usage, peak_hours, standby_load, pv_self_consumption, bill_estimate, top_savings_tips, ev_impact, and pool_pump_impact. Make it detailed."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. For the CSVs, what are the column names for timestamp and kWh, and are they local time with DST? Also confirm files are UTF-8.", "reasoning_content": "To parse the CSVs I need schema mapping: timestamp/value column names and unit, plus time handling. I will add schema and confirm timezone for analyze_electricity_usage."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Usage CSV columns: datetime, consumption_kwh. PV CSV: datetime, generation_kwh. Local time with DST, UTF-8, 30-minute interval."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Any gaps or outliers in the data? I can interpolate missing intervals and flag/cap spikes. Tell me your preferences (method and limits).", "reasoning_content": "I need data cleaning settings for gaps and outliers. I will include data_cleaning (gap handling, interpolate limit, outlier detection/action) in the tool parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Interpolate linearly for gaps up to 120 minutes. Flag values above 2.5× median hourly consumption and cap them. Please don't drop rows."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Please share your EV charging details: charger power (kW), typical weekday start/end times, weekend sessions, and typical kWh per session.", "reasoning_content": "EV details are required to estimate ev_impact and savings potential. I will collect charger power, weekday and weekend schedules, and typical kWh to populate ev_profile."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Level 2 charger at 7.2 kW. Weekdays 21:30–00:30. Saturdays sometimes 20:00–22:00. About 18 kWh per session."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent. I have everything needed. With your confirmation, I’ll analyze June–August using your TOU plan, PV logs, building and EV profiles, and deliver the detailed metrics and savings tips. Shall I run it now?", "reasoning_content": "We now have all inputs: source_type=csv, usage_path and pv_path, interval=30, timezone=America/Los_Angeles, dates, schema, TOU periods, building profile, pool pump schedule, data cleaning, EV profile, output metrics, and return_format=detailed. I’m ready to call analyze_electricity_usage with these parameters once the user confirms."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes. In one run, analyze: source_type: csv; usage_path: /data/energy/usage_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv; pv_path: /data/energy/pv_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv; interval_minutes: 30; timezone: America/Los_Angeles; start_date: 2025-06-01; end_date: 2025-08-31; schema: { usage_timestamp_col: \"datetime\", usage_value_col: \"consumption_kwh\", pv_timestamp_col: \"datetime\", pv_value_col: \"generation_kwh\", unit: \"kWh\" }; tariff_plan: { type: \"tou\", name: \"PG&E E-TOU-C\", currency: \"USD\", tou_periods: [ { days: \"weekdays\", start: \"00:00\", end: \"16:00\", rate_per_kwh: 0.32 }, { days: \"weekdays\", start: \"16:00\", end: \"21:00\", rate_per_kwh: 0.56 }, { days: \"weekdays\", start: \"21:00\", end: \"24:00\", rate_per_kwh: 0.32 }, { days: \"weekends\", start: \"00:00\", end: \"24:00\", rate_per_kwh: 0.32 } ] }; building_profile: { home_size_sqft: 1850, occupants: 4, hvac_type: \"heat_pump\", water_heater: \"heat_pump\", has_ev: true, has_pv: true }; appliance_profiles: [ { name: \"pool_pump\", rated_power_kw: 0.75, schedule: { start_time: \"10:00\", end_time: \"14:00\", days_of_week: [\"Mon\",\"Tue\",\"Wed\",\"Thu\",\"Fri\"] } } ]; ev_profile: { charger_power_kw: 7.2, weekday_start: \"21:30\", weekday_end: \"00:30\", weekend_sessions: [ { day: \"Sat\", start: \"20:00\", end: \"22:00\" } ], typical_session_kwh: 18 }; data_cleaning: { gap_handling: \"interpolate_linear\", max_interpolate_minutes: 120, outlier_detection: true, outlier_factor: 2.5, outlier_action: \"cap\" }; output_metrics: [\"baseline_usage\",\"peak_hours\",\"standby_load\",\"pv_self_consumption\",\"bill_estimate\",\"top_savings_tips\",\"ev_impact\",\"pool_pump_impact\"]; return_format: \"detailed\"."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "analyze_electricity_usage", "description": "Analyze household electricity interval data to estimate key metrics, compute bills under the specified tariff plan, and generate targeted energy-saving tips.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["csv", "json"], "description": "Format of input usage data"}, "usage_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to electricity usage file"}, "pv_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to solar PV generation file (optional)"}, "interval_minutes": {"type": "integer", "description": "Sampling interval in minutes", "minimum": 5, "maximum": 120}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA time zone, e.g., America/Los_Angeles"}, "start_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Analysis window start date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "end_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Analysis window end date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"usage_timestamp_col": {"type": "string"}, "usage_value_col": {"type": "string"}, "pv_timestamp_col": {"type": "string"}, "pv_value_col": {"type": "string"}, "unit": {"type": "string", "enum": ["kWh", "Wh"]}}, "required": ["usage_timestamp_col", "usage_value_col", "unit"]}, "tariff_plan": {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["flat", "tou", "tiered", "demand"]}, "name": {"type": "string"}, "currency": {"type": "string", "enum": ["USD", "EUR", "GBP", "AUD", "CAD"]}, "tou_periods": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"days": {"type": "string", "enum": ["weekdays", "weekends", "all"]}, "start": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM 24h"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM 24h"}, "rate_per_kwh": {"type": "number", "description": "Rate in currency per kWh"}}, "required": ["days", "start", "end", "rate_per_kwh"]}}, "fixed_monthly_fee": {"type": "number", "description": "Optional fixed fee"}, "demand_charge_per_kw": {"type": "number", "description": "Optional demand charge per kW"}}, "required": ["type", "name", "currency"]}, "building_profile": {"type": "object", "properties": {"home_size_sqft": {"type": "integer"}, "occupants": {"type": "integer"}, "hvac_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["central_ac", "heat_pump", "electric_resistance", "mini_split", "none"]}, "water_heater": {"type": "string", "enum": ["gas", "electric", "heat_pump", "solar"]}, "has_ev": {"type": "boolean"}, "has_pv": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["home_size_sqft", "occupants", "hvac_type", "water_heater", "has_ev", "has_pv"]}, "appliance_profiles": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "rated_power_kw": {"type": "number"}, "schedule": {"type": "object", "properties": {"start_time": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}, "end_time": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}, "days_of_week": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]}}}, "required": ["start_time", "end_time"]}}, "required": ["name"]}}, "ev_profile": {"type": "object", "properties": {"charger_power_kw": {"type": "number"}, "weekday_start": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}, "weekday_end": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}, "weekend_sessions": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"day": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Sat", "Sun"]}, "start": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM"}}, "required": ["day", "start", "end"]}}, "typical_session_kwh": {"type": "number"}}, "required": ["charger_power_kw", "weekday_start", "weekday_end", "typical_session_kwh"]}, "data_cleaning": {"type": "object", "properties": {"gap_handling": {"type": "string", "enum": ["interpolate_linear", "carry_forward", "drop"]}, "max_interpolate_minutes": {"type": "integer"}, "outlier_detection": {"type": "boolean"}, "outlier_factor": {"type": "number"}, "outlier_action": {"type": "string", "enum": ["cap", "remove"]}}, "required": ["gap_handling", "outlier_detection"]}, "output_metrics": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["baseline_usage", "peak_hours", "standby_load", "pv_self_consumption", "bill_estimate", "top_savings_tips", "ev_impact", "pool_pump_impact"]}, "minItems": 1}, "return_format": {"type": "string", "enum": ["summary", "detailed"]}}, "required": ["source_type", "usage_path", "interval_minutes", "timezone", "start_date", "end_date", "schema", "tariff_plan", "building_profile", "data_cleaning", "output_metrics", "return_format"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450057e7ab7d0f2595ed9c61d3b35b", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user has provided all the parameters needed to run the analyze_electricity_usage function. Let me call the function with the exact parameters they specified.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_2lkavcjh1fux_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"source_type\": \"csv\", \"usage_path\": \"/data/energy/usage_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv\", \"pv_path\": \"/data/energy/pv_2025-06_to_2025-08.csv\", \"interval_minutes\": 30, \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"start_date\": \"2025-06-01\", \"end_date\": \"2025-08-31\", \"schema\": {\"usage_timestamp_col\": \"datetime\", \"usage_value_col\": \"consumption_kwh\", \"pv_timestamp_col\": \"datetime\", \"pv_value_col\": \"generation_kwh\", \"unit\": \"kWh\"}, \"tariff_plan\": {\"type\": \"tou\", \"name\": \"PG&E E-TOU-C\", \"currency\": \"USD\", \"tou_periods\": [{\"days\": \"weekdays\", \"start\": \"00:00\", \"end\": \"16:00\", \"rate_per_kwh\": 0.32}, {\"days\": \"weekdays\", \"start\": \"16:00\", \"end\": \"21:00\", \"rate_per_kwh\": 0.56}, {\"days\": \"weekdays\", \"start\": \"21:00\", \"end\": \"24:00\", \"rate_per_kwh\": 0.32}, {\"days\": \"weekends\", \"start\": \"00:00\", \"end\": \"24:00\", \"rate_per_kwh\": 0.32}]}, \"building_profile\": {\"home_size_sqft\": 1850, \"occupants\": 4, \"hvac_type\": \"heat_pump\", \"water_heater\": \"heat_pump\", \"has_ev\": true, \"has_pv\": true}, \"appliance_profiles\": [{\"name\": \"pool_pump\", \"rated_power_kw\": 0.75, \"schedule\": {\"start_time\": \"10:00\", \"end_time\": \"14:00\", \"days_of_week\": [\"Mon\", \"Tue\", \"Wed\", \"Thu\", \"Fri\"]}}], \"ev_profile\": {\"charger_power_kw\": 7.2, \"weekday_start\": \"21:30\", \"weekday_end\": \"00:30\", \"weekend_sessions\": [{\"day\": \"Sat\", \"start\": \"20:00\", \"end\": \"22:00\"}], \"typical_session_kwh\": 18}, \"data_cleaning\": {\"gap_handling\": \"interpolate_linear\", \"max_interpolate_minutes\": 120, \"outlier_detection\": true, \"outlier_factor\": 2.5, \"outlier_action\": \"cap\"}, \"output_metrics\": [\"baseline_usage\", \"peak_hours\", \"standby_load\", \"pv_self_consumption\", \"bill_estimate\", \"top_savings_tips\", \"ev_impact\", \"pool_pump_impact\"], \"return_format\": \"detailed\"}", "name": "analyze_electricity_usage"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716567, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 741, "prompt_tokens": 2965, "total_tokens": 3706, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 34, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 2683}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:33.091384", "duration_ms": 10250, "hash": "209d86335ef0dbebee6b7875298b23c8", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 84, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I’m trying to reorganize my library so I can quickly pick something for the commute, deep work, and workouts. I want the playlists grouped by mood and tempo. What’s a good approach?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Happy to help. To tailor this, please share:\n- Target number of core playlists (e.g., 6–8)\n- Main genres and languages\n- Preferred BPM bands (or I can suggest defaults)\n- App you use (Spotify/Apple/etc.)\n- Crossfade/mixing preferences and whether you want explicit-content filters\n- Moods you want to cover\nWith that, I’ll propose a clean mood×tempo structure with names and sorting rules.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a playlist organization strategy based on mood and tempo. To tailor a practical framework, I need constraints: number of playlists, genres, BPM bands, platform, crossfade/mixing preferences, and content filters. No tools are needed; I’ll ask targeted questions and then propose a mood×tempo taxonomy with naming and ordering rules."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I’m on Spotify with about 1,200 tracks (EDM—house/trance, pop, hip-hop). I’d like 8 core playlists. Moods: Chill, Focus, Happy, Night Drive, Workout, Party. I’m fine with these BPM bands: <90, 90–110, 111–128, 129–150, >150. I use a 6-sec crossfade. Prefer to avoid harsh key clashes and most profanity on commutes. Emoji in titles are welcome."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Here’s a concise outline I can expand:\n- Structure (8 slots): pair mood families with two tempo tiers.\n  • Calm (Chill/Focus) × Steady/Upbeat\n  • Drive (Night Drive) × Groove/Fast\n  • Power (Workout/Party) × Upbeat/Sprint\n- BPM mapping: your bands, with tiers: Steady ≤110, Groove 111–128, Fast 129–150, Sprint >150; Slow <90 reserved for Calm.\n- Filters: limit explicit for commute-facing lists; set instrumental/vocal mix per mood; allow EDM/pop/hip-hop.\n- Ordering: sort primarily by rising BPM; group compatible keys; keep 6-sec crossfade.\n- Transitions: allow adjacent moves only (e.g., Calm→Drive at Groove; Drive→Power at Fast) to keep flow.\nIf you’d like, I can draft the full schema with names/emojis, exact BPM/energy/danceability targets, filters, ordering rules, and a transition map.", "reasoning_content": "I now have platform, genres, desired count (8), moods, BPM bands, crossfade, and content constraints. I can outline an 8-slot framework by pairing mood families with tempo tiers, plus inclusion filters, ordering, and transition logic. No tools are required; I’ll present a concise outline and offer to expand into a full schema."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please draft the full schema: 8 playlists with emoji-coded names. For each, specify allowed genres, BPM range(s), energy and danceability targets (low/med/high), vocal vs instrumental preference, explicit-content rule, default sort order, and crossfade guidance. Add the transition rules between adjacent playlists and a short naming convention and folder layout. Keep it generic—no specific song examples."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_sql_query", "description": "Execute a SQL query on a database and return results (irrelevant tool)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "SQL to execute"}, "database": {"type": "string", "description": "Database name or path"}, "timeout_ms": {"type": "integer", "description": "Query timeout in milliseconds", "minimum": 100, "maximum": 600000}}, "required": ["query", "database"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "resize_image", "description": "Resize an image to the specified dimensions (irrelevant tool)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to the source image"}, "width": {"type": "integer", "description": "Target width in pixels", "minimum": 1}, "height": {"type": "integer", "description": "Target height in pixels", "minimum": 1}, "fit": {"type": "string", "description": "Resize mode", "enum": ["contain", "cover", "fill"]}}, "required": ["source_path", "width", "height"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_weather_forecast", "description": "Get a multi-day weather forecast for a location (irrelevant tool)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"location": {"type": "string", "description": "City name or coordinates"}, "units": {"type": "string", "description": "Temperature units", "enum": ["metric", "imperial"], "default": "metric"}, "days": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of days to forecast", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 7, "default": 3}}, "required": ["location"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500561b91eb5ec32cfe61c03a2d59", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants a full schema for reorganizing their Spotify library with 8 playlists. They want:\n\n1. 8 playlists with emoji-coded names\n2. For each playlist:\n   - Allowed genres\n   - BPM range(s)\n   - Energy targets (low/med/high)\n   - Danceability targets (low/med/high)\n   - Vocal vs instrumental preference\n   - Explicit-content rule\n   - Default sort order\n   - Crossfade guidance\n3. Transition rules between adjacent playlists\n4. Naming convention and folder layout\n5. No specific song examples\n\nThis is a music/library organization request that doesn't require any tools. I'll create a comprehensive schema based on the parameters they've provided:\n- Moods: Chill, Focus, Happy, Night Drive, Workout, Party\n- BPM bands: <90, 90–110, 111–128, 129–150, >150\n- 8 playlists total\n- Spotify with 6-sec crossfade\n- Avoid harsh key clashes and most profanity on commutes\n- Emoji in titles welcome\n\nLet me structure this into 8 playlists. They mentioned 6 moods but want 8 playlists, so I can split some moods into multiple tempo tiers:\n\n1. Chill (low BPM, relaxed) - <90\n2. Focus (medium BPM, concentration) - 90-110\n3. Happy (medium-upper BPM, uplifting) - 111-128\n4. Night Drive (medium-slow, atmospheric) - 90-128 (overlaps with Focus/Happy but different mood)\n5. Workout (high BPM, energy) - 129-150\n6. Party (high BPM, dancing) - >150 or 129-150\n7. Maybe split Night Drive into two: Night Drive (Chill) and Night Drive (Upbeat)\n8. Could do a \"Deep Work\" separate from regular Focus, or a \"Flow State\" for the 111-128 range\n\nActually, let me think about pairing moods with tempo tiers as I suggested before:\n\n\nI'll map out six distinct mood-tempo combinations that capture their musical preferences. The strategy involves creating precise playlists that match specific listening contexts while maintaining flexibility. I'll focus on energy levels, BPM ranges, and contextual suitability to ensure each playlist serves its intended purpose. The goal is a comprehensive yet streamlined music organization system that works seamlessly across different activities.\n</think>\n\n# Spotify Library Reorganization Schema\n\n## 8 Core Playlists\n\n| # | Playlist Name | Genres | BPM Range | Energy | Danceability | Vocal | Explicit | Sort Order | Crossfade |\n|---|---------------|--------|-----------|--------|--------------|-------|----------|------------|-----------|\n| 1 | 🌙 Chill Zone | house (deep/lofi), downtempo, ambient pop | <90 | low | low | vocal OK | minimal | BPM ↑, key compatibility | 6s, keep smooth |\n| 2 | 🎯 Deep Focus | ambient, lo-fi hip-hop, cinematic, minimal techno | 90–110 | low–med | low | instrumental preferred | avoid | BPM ↑, key compatibility | 6s, no gaps |\n| 3 | ☀️ Easy Happy | pop, indie pop, tropical house, melodic hip-hop | 90–128 | med | med–high | vocal | limited (commute) | BPM ↑, key compatibility | 6s |\n| 4 | 🚗 Night Drive | synthwave, dark electro, trap (atmospheric), progressive house | 111–128 | med–high | med | vocal OK | limited | BPM ↑, key compatibility | 6s, keep flow |\n| 5 | 🔥 Cardio Crush | big room, electro house, hardstyle, drum & bass | 129–150 | high | high | vocal OK | allowed | BPM ↑, energy curve | 6s, maintain momentum |\n| 6 | 💪 Heavy Lift | techno (hard), trance, dubstep, psytrance | 129–150, >150 | high | med–high | instrumental OK | allowed | BPM ↑, energy curve | 6s, stay heavy |\n| 7 | 🎉 Party Starter | hip-hop, pop, electro pop, garage | 111–150 | high | high | vocal | allowed | BPM ↑, energy curve | 6s, keep high |\n| 8 | ⚡ Endorphin Rush | trap, dubstep, hardstyle, speed garage | >150 | very high | high | vocal OK | allowed | BPM ↑, peak energy | 6s, max impact |\n\n---\n\n## Folder Structure\n\n```\n📁 My Library\n├── 📁 Commute Safe\n│   ├── 🌙 Chill Zone\n│   ├── 🎯 Deep Focus\n│   ├── ☀️ Easy Happy\n│   └── 🚗 Night Drive\n├── 📁 Power Sessions\n│   ├── 🔥 Cardio Crush\n│   ├── 💪 Heavy Lift\n│   └── ⚡ Endorphin Rush\n└── 📁 Social\n    └── 🎉 Party Starter\n```\n\n---\n\n## Transition Rules\n\n```\n🌙 Chill Zone ←→ 🎯 Deep Focus  (both low energy, overlapping BPM)\n🎯 Deep Focus ←→ ☀️ Easy Happy  (energy rise into daytime)\n☀️ Easy Happy ←→ 🚗 Night Drive  (mood shift, BPM overlap OK)\n🚗 Night Drive ←→ 🔥 Cardio Crush  (night → workout transition)\n🔥 Cardio Crush ←→ 💪 Heavy Lift  (both high energy, BPM overlap)\n💪 Heavy Lift ←→ ⚡ Endorphin Rush  (peak energy tier)\n🎉 Party Starter connects to: 🔥 Cardio Crush, ☀️ Easy Happy\n```\n\n**Adjacent-only rule:** never jump from Chill Zone → Cardio Crush or similar energy jumps. Use transition playlists as bridges if needed.\n\n---\n\n## Naming Convention\n\n- **Emoji prefix** signals energy tier (🌙=calm, 🎯=focus, ☀️=uplift, 🚗=night, 🔥=cardio, 💪=strength, 🎉=social, ⚡=peak)\n- **Main word** describes use case or mood\n- **Optional suffix** (e.g., \"Mix\", \"Flow\") if you add variations later\n\n---\n\n## Additional Guidelines\n\n- **Key sorting:** arrange tracks by compatible keys (circle of fifths neighbors) within each BPM tier to avoid clashes\n- **Explicit filter:** apply for playlists marked \"limited\" or \"avoid\"—audit quarterly\n- **Crossfade:** 6s works across all; adjust down to 4s for high-energy transitions if tracks overlap poorly\n- **Energy curve:** for workout playlists, sort by rising intensity within each BPM block (build → peak → finish)\n\nThis structure gives you clear separation for commute vs. workouts while keeping transitions smooth within energy clusters. Want me to refine any specific playlist parameters?", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1425, "prompt_tokens": 1095, "total_tokens": 2520, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 491, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 891}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "stop", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:46.630119", "duration_ms": 23691, "hash": "a615c40923e37000d86a81af2d68e95b", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": false, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "stop", "tool_calls_valid": null, "tool_calls_count": 0}
{"data_index": 85, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm coordinating in-home care for my dad and need to set up caregiver shifts and medication logging. Can you help me design this?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. To set this up, please share:\n- Resident ID and timezone (IANA, e.g., America/New_York)\n- Caregivers (IDs, names), their typical availability, and preferred assignments\n- Daily coverage window, preferred shift lengths, overlap and break rules\n- Start date and timeframe (e.g., first week)\n- Home address for shift location\n- Medication list (name, dose, route, schedule), PRN rules, and any hold parameters\n- Required logging fields (e.g., who, time, lot, vitals) and alert thresholds\n- Notification method (e.g., SMS) and where to export logs (path)\nOnce I have this, I can create shift assignments and medication reminders, and set up templates for logging.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a structured plan for shifts and medication logs. I should collect core parameters (resident ID, timezone, caregivers/coverage, shift rules, meds, logging fields, alerts) to prepare for parallel creation of shift assignments and med reminders. Later I will call create_shift_assignment and create_medication_reminder per item; log_medication_administration can be used when doses are actually given."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Timezone: America/New_York. Resident ID: R-7782. Caregivers: CG-101 Maria Gomez, CG-104 James Reed, CG-112 Priya Patel. Daily coverage 07:00–21:00. Preferred shift lengths are 4h or 6h; mornings preferred for Maria, evenings for James. Handover overlap 15 minutes; break rule 30 minutes per 6 hours. Meds: Lisinopril 10 mg oral at 08:00 daily; Metformin 500 mg oral at 08:00 and 18:30 with meals; Atorvastatin 20 mg oral at 21:00; PRN Acetaminophen 500 mg oral q6h PRN headache, max 3/day. Logging fields: who administered, time, dose, lot, pre-dose BP for Lisinopril, pre-meal BG for Metformin, and notes. Allergies: none."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. I can structure weekdays as 3×4h blocks and weekends as 2×6h, with a 15‑minute overlap. For meds, I’ll set reminders at 08:00, 18:30, and 21:00, plus a PRN template.\nPlease confirm:\n- Start date and initial timeframe (e.g., one week)\n- Mealtimes for breakfast/dinner\n- Home address for the shift location\n- Notification preference (SMS/email) and caregiver phone numbers\n- Daily summary time\n- Export paths for CSV (e.g., /home/...)\nOnce confirmed, I’ll be ready to create shift assignments and reminders.", "reasoning_content": "They provided timezone, resident, caregivers, coverage, and medication details. I should confirm remaining setup: start dates, address, mealtimes, notifications, export paths, daily summary time. Then I can proceed to parallel calls to create_shift_assignment (per shift) and create_medication_reminder (per med schedule)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Start Monday 2025-03-10 through Sunday 2025-03-16 for the first week. Mealtimes: breakfast 08:00, dinner 18:30. Weekdays prefer 4h shifts; weekends 6h. Address: 123 Maple Ave, Syracuse, NY 13210. Daily summary at 21:30 by SMS. No EHR; export CSV to /home/care/exports/med_admin.csv and /home/care/exports/shifts.csv. Send alerts to caregivers by SMS."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. Proposed blocks:\n- Weekdays: 07:00–11:00, 11:00–15:00, 15:00–19:00 (15‑min overlap baked in)\n- Weekends: 09:00–15:00, 15:00–21:00\nMed reminders: 08:00 Lisinopril + Metformin, 18:30 Metformin, 21:00 Atorvastatin.\nTo enable alerts, please provide caregiver mobile numbers and your mobile for escalations. Also confirm alert thresholds (BP high/low, BG high/low) and what constitutes a missed dose (e.g., >30 minutes late).", "reasoning_content": "We now have timeframe, mealtimes, address, summary time, and export paths. I’ll outline the default shift blocks and med reminders, and request phone numbers and alert thresholds so that when they submit items I can call the tools in parallel."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Numbers: Maria +1-315-555-0111, James +1-315-555-0144, Priya +1-315-555-0177. My number: +1-315-555-0100. Alert thresholds: BP high >150/90, low <100/60; BG high >180 mg/dL, low <90 mg/dL. Missed dose = not administered within 30 minutes of the scheduled time. Please include a midday fall risk check and hourly hydration reminders in each shift. FYI the door key code is 2351—please keep that secure."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. For security, we won’t store the door code; we’ll note “door access code on file.” I’ll add ‘fall_risk_check’ to midday tasks and hourly ‘hydration_reminder’ across shifts.\nDo you want holds configured as: hold Lisinopril if BP <100/60 and hold Metformin if BG <90, with escalation to your nurse and you? Please share your nurse’s contact, and confirm the specific weekend caregiver assignments.", "reasoning_content": "I have phone numbers and thresholds. I should handle the door code securely (not stored), add fall risk and hydration tasks, and confirm med hold rules and nurse contact plus weekend assignments. Then I’ll be set to create items via create_shift_assignment and create_medication_reminder."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes, hold Lisinopril if BP <100/60 and hold Metformin if BG <90, escalate to our nurse and to me. Nurse: Alex Chen, RN (ID RN-45), +1-315-555-0200. Weekend coverage: Saturday Priya 09:00–15:00 and James 15:00–21:00; Sunday Maria 09:00–15:00 and Priya 15:00–21:00. We'll use geofenced check-in/out on arrival and departure. Please set the schedule starting 2025-03-10 and create the medication reminders accordingly."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great—everything is configured. Please send 2–5 items to create now in parallel. You can mix shift assignments and medication reminders. Include ISO times and specify timezone America/New_York.\nExample:\n- Shift: caregiver_id CG-101, start 2025-03-11T07:00, end 2025-03-11T11:00\n- Reminder: medication Lisinopril 10 mg oral at 2025-03-11T08:00 assigned to CG-101\nWhen you send them, I’ll create them right away.", "reasoning_content": "All rules and contacts are set. Before executing, I need a concrete batch (2–5 items) to process in parallel. On receipt, I will call create_shift_assignment for each shift (with resident_id R-7782, timezone America/New_York, overlap 15, tasks, address, notify_caregiver true) and create_medication_reminder for each reminder (with dose, route, scheduled_time, timezone, caregiver_id, precheck, hold_rules, notes)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "In parallel, create the following for 2025-03-11 (America/New_York) for resident R-7782:\n\nShifts:\n1) caregiver_id CG-101, start 2025-03-11T07:00, end 2025-03-11T11:00, tasks [fall_risk_check, hydration_reminder, meal_prep, bp_check, bg_check]\n2) caregiver_id CG-112, start 2025-03-11T11:00, end 2025-03-11T15:00, tasks [fall_risk_check, hydration_reminder, companionship]\n3) caregiver_id CG-104, start 2025-03-11T15:00, end 2025-03-11T19:00, tasks [hydration_reminder, meal_prep, bg_check]\n\nMedication reminders:\n4) Lisinopril 10 mg oral at 2025-03-11T08:00 handled by CG-101; precheck [bp]; hold if BP_systolic < 100 or BP_diastolic < 60; notes \"Record pre-dose BP; hold and call RN-45 if below\"\n5) Metformin 500 mg oral at 2025-03-11T18:30 handled by CG-104; precheck [bg]; hold if BG < 90 mg/dL; notes \"Check BG before dose; if <90 hold and call RN-45\"\n\nUse location address 123 Maple Ave, Syracuse, NY 13210, handover overlap 15 minutes, and notify caregivers by SMS."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "create_shift_assignment", "description": "Create a caregiver shift assignment for a resident, with tasks and notification options", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"caregiver_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Caregiver unique ID (e.g., CG-101)"}, "resident_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Resident unique ID (e.g., R-7782)"}, "start": {"type": "string", "description": "Shift start time in ISO 8601 (local or with offset)"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "Shift end time in ISO 8601 (local or with offset)"}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone (e.g., America/New_York)"}, "handover_overlap_mins": {"type": "integer", "description": "Minutes of overlap for handover", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 60, "default": 15}, "tasks": {"type": "array", "description": "Planned tasks for the shift", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["fall_risk_check", "hydration_reminder", "bp_check", "bg_check", "meal_prep", "transport", "housekeeping", "companionship", "med_reminder"]}, "uniqueItems": true}, "location_address": {"type": "string", "description": "Service location address"}, "notify_caregiver": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Send assignment notification to caregiver", "default": true}}, "required": ["caregiver_id", "resident_id", "start", "end", "timezone"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "create_medication_reminder", "description": "Create a scheduled medication reminder for a resident with prechecks and hold rules", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"resident_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Resident unique ID (e.g., R-7782)"}, "medication_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Medication name (e.g., Lisinopril)"}, "dose": {"type": "string", "description": "Dose with units (e.g., 10 mg)"}, "route": {"type": "string", "description": "Route of administration", "enum": ["oral", "sublingual", "topical", "inhalation", "ophthalmic", "intranasal"]}, "scheduled_time": {"type": "string", "description": "Scheduled time in ISO 8601 (local or with offset)"}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone (e.g., America/New_York)"}, "caregiver_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Assigned caregiver ID for administering the dose"}, "precheck": {"type": "array", "description": "Vitals to check before administration", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["bp", "bg", "none"]}, "uniqueItems": true}, "hold_rules": {"type": "object", "description": "Thresholds that trigger holding a dose", "properties": {"bp_systolic_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Min systolic BP to proceed"}, "bp_diastolic_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Min diastolic BP to proceed"}, "bg_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Min blood glucose mg/dL to proceed"}}}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Special instructions to display"}, "notify": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Send reminder notification to caregiver", "default": true}}, "required": ["resident_id", "medication_name", "dose", "route", "scheduled_time", "timezone"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "log_medication_administration", "description": "Record an actual medication administration event with vitals and notes", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"resident_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Resident unique ID (e.g., R-7782)"}, "medication_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Medication name"}, "dose_given": {"type": "string", "description": "Dose actually given with units (e.g., 10 mg)"}, "route": {"type": "string", "description": "Route of administration", "enum": ["oral", "sublingual", "topical", "inhalation", "ophthalmic", "intranasal"]}, "scheduled_time": {"type": "string", "description": "Scheduled time for the dose in ISO 8601", "nullable": true}, "administered_time": {"type": "string", "description": "Actual administration time in ISO 8601"}, "caregiver_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Caregiver ID who administered the dose"}, "lot_number": {"type": "string", "description": "Medication lot/batch number", "nullable": true}, "vitals": {"type": "object", "description": "Relevant vital signs", "properties": {"bp_systolic": {"type": "integer"}, "bp_diastolic": {"type": "integer"}, "glucose_mg_dl": {"type": "integer"}}}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Free-text notes", "nullable": true}}, "required": ["resident_id", "medication_name", "dose_given", "route", "administered_time"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "0645005651b6b184650ee3fbc7f936b6", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to create 5 items in parallel for 2025-03-11:\n- 3 shift assignments\n- 2 medication reminders\n\nLet me structure each call properly.\n\nFor shifts, I need:\n- create_shift_assignment with:\n  - caregiver_id\n  - resident_id: R-7782\n  - start (ISO 8601)\n  - end (ISO 8601)\n  - timezone: America/New_York\n  - location_address\n  - handover_overlap_mins: 15\n  - tasks: array\n  - notify_caregiver: true\n\nFor medication reminders, I need:\n- create_medication_reminder with:\n  - resident_id: R-7782\n  - medication_name\n  - dose\n  - route: oral\n  - scheduled_time (ISO 8601)\n  - timezone: America/New_York\n  - caregiver_id\n  - precheck\n  - hold_rules (with the appropriate thresholds)\n  - notes\n  - notify: true\n\nLet me create all 5 calls in parallel.\n\nShift 1: CG-101, 07:00-11:00, tasks: fall_risk_check, hydration_reminder, meal_prep, bp_check, bg_check\nShift 2: CG-112, 11:00-15:00, tasks: fall_risk_check, hydration_reminder, companionship\nShift 3: CG-104, 15:00-19:00, tasks: hydration_reminder, meal_prep, bg_check\n\nMedication 1: Lisinopril 10 mg at 08:00 by CG-101, precheck bp, hold if BP <100/60\nMedication 2: Metformin 500 mg at 18:30 by CG-104, precheck bg, hold if BG <90\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_nyiyhq0eywc5_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"caregiver_id\": \"CG-101\", \"resident_id\": \"R-7782\", \"start\": \"2025-03-11T07:00\", \"end\": \"2025-03-11T11:00\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"location_address\": \"123 Maple Ave, Syracuse, NY 13210\", \"handover_overlap_mins\": 15, \"tasks\": [\"fall_risk_check\", \"hydration_reminder\", \"meal_prep\", \"bp_check\", \"bg_check\"], \"notify_caregiver\": true}", "name": "create_shift_assignment"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}, {"id": "call_function_nyiyhq0eywc5_2", "function": {"arguments": "{\"caregiver_id\": \"CG-112\", \"resident_id\": \"R-7782\", \"start\": \"2025-03-11T11:00\", \"end\": \"2025-03-11T15:00\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"location_address\": \"123 Maple Ave, Syracuse, NY 13210\", \"handover_overlap_mins\": 15, \"tasks\": [\"fall_risk_check\", \"hydration_reminder\", \"companionship\"], \"notify_caregiver\": true}", "name": "create_shift_assignment"}, "type": "function", "index": 1}, {"id": "call_function_nyiyhq0eywc5_3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"caregiver_id\": \"CG-104\", \"resident_id\": \"R-7782\", \"start\": \"2025-03-11T15:00\", \"end\": \"2025-03-11T19:00\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"location_address\": \"123 Maple Ave, Syracuse, NY 13210\", \"handover_overlap_mins\": 15, \"tasks\": [\"hydration_reminder\", \"meal_prep\", \"bg_check\"], \"notify_caregiver\": true}", "name": "create_shift_assignment"}, "type": "function", "index": 2}, {"id": "call_function_nyiyhq0eywc5_4", "function": {"arguments": "{\"resident_id\": \"R-7782\", \"medication_name\": \"Lisinopril\", \"dose\": \"10 mg\", \"route\": \"oral\", \"scheduled_time\": \"2025-03-11T08:00\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"caregiver_id\": \"CG-101\", \"precheck\": [\"bp\"], \"hold_rules\": {\"bp_systolic_min\": 100, \"bp_diastolic_min\": 60}, \"notes\": \"Record pre-dose BP; hold and call RN-45 if below\", \"notify\": true}", "name": "create_medication_reminder"}, "type": "function", "index": 3}, {"id": "call_function_nyiyhq0eywc5_5", "function": {"arguments": "{\"resident_id\": \"R-7782\", \"medication_name\": \"Metformin\", \"dose\": \"500 mg\", \"route\": \"oral\", \"scheduled_time\": \"2025-03-11T18:30\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"caregiver_id\": \"CG-104\", \"precheck\": [\"bg\"], \"hold_rules\": {\"bg_min\": 90}, \"notes\": \"Check BG before dose; if <90 hold and call RN-45\", \"notify\": true}", "name": "create_medication_reminder"}, "type": "function", "index": 4}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1242, "prompt_tokens": 2963, "total_tokens": 4205, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 388, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 2683}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:37.054317", "duration_ms": 14008, "hash": "1ffb7a8174cf940a831ef6c27565fe22", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 5}
{"data_index": 86, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Plan a single 5-day Tokyo city itinerary in detailed format for two adults from 2025-10-12 to 2025-10-16. Hotel: Park Hotel Tokyo, Shiodome Media Tower, 1-7-1 Higashi Shimbashi, Minato City, Tokyo 105-7227, Japan. Pace: moderate. Interests: architecture, food, art, technology. Must-visits: Senso-ji, teamLab Planets TOKYO, Tokyo Skytree, Meiji Jingu, Nezu Museum. Avoid long hikes. Use public transit and walking only; cap any walking segment at 25 minutes. Start days at 09:00 and end by 21:00. Budget: midrange; meal preferences: local and seafood. Include estimated one-way commute times from the hotel to the first stop each day and between consecutive stops, and summarize total travel time per day."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "plan_city_itinerary", "description": "Generate a multi-day city itinerary with daily attractions, meals, and estimated commute times from the hotel to each first stop and between consecutive stops. Returns day-by-day schedule with time blocks, travel mode suggestions, and total travel time per day.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"city": {"type": "string", "description": "Target city and country (e.g., 'Tokyo, Japan')"}, "start_date": {"type": "string", "format": "date", "description": "Trip start date (YYYY-MM-DD)"}, "end_date": {"type": "string", "format": "date", "description": "Trip end date (YYYY-MM-DD)"}, "days": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of days in the itinerary", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 21}, "group_size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of travelers", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20}, "hotel_address": {"type": "string", "description": "Base hotel address for commute calculations"}, "travel_pace": {"type": "string", "description": "Daily activity density", "enum": ["relaxed", "moderate", "packed"]}, "transport_mode": {"type": "string", "description": "Primary transport mode preference", "enum": ["public_transit", "walking", "rideshare_taxi", "rental_car", "mixed"]}, "interests": {"type": "array", "description": "Interests to emphasize", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["architecture", "museums", "food", "parks", "nightlife", "history", "art", "technology", "shopping", "family"]}, "minItems": 1}, "must_visit": {"type": "array", "description": "Specific attractions to include if feasible", "items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 0}, "avoid": {"type": "array", "description": "Constraints to avoid", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["hiking", "long_queues", "expensive", "outdoors", "indoors"]}, "minItems": 0}, "daily_start_time": {"type": "string", "description": "Earliest start time (HH:MM, 24h)", "pattern": "^(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"}, "daily_end_time": {"type": "string", "description": "Latest end time (HH:MM, 24h)", "pattern": "^(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"}, "budget_level": {"type": "string", "description": "Overall budget level", "enum": ["economy", "midrange", "luxury"]}, "meal_preferences": {"type": "array", "description": "Meal focus", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["local", "vegetarian", "vegan", "seafood", "halal", "kosher", "no_pork", "gluten_free", "desserts"]}, "minItems": 0}, "include_commute_times": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Include estimated travel times between stops"}, "walking_max_minutes": {"type": "integer", "description": "Max walking segment minutes", "minimum": 5, "maximum": 120, "default": 30}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Level of detail in the output", "enum": ["detailed", "summary"]}, "notes": {"type": "string", "description": "Additional constraints or context (optional)"}}, "required": ["city", "start_date", "end_date", "days", "hotel_address", "travel_pace", "transport_mode", "interests", "daily_start_time", "daily_end_time", "budget_level", "include_commute_times", "output_format"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500565644a0ef7be5d46b70e61405", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to create a detailed 5-day Tokyo itinerary. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n- City: Tokyo, Japan\n- Dates: 2025-10-12 to 2025-10-16 (5 days)\n- Hotel: Park Hotel Tokyo, Shiodome Media Tower, 1-7-1 Higashi Shimbashi, Minato City, Tokyo 105-7227, Japan\n- Travelers: 2 adults\n- Pace: moderate\n- Interests: architecture, food, art, technology\n- Must-visits: Senso-ji, teamLab Planets TOKYO, Tokyo Skytree, Meiji Jingu, Nezu Museum\n- Avoid: long hikes\n- Transport: public transit and walking only\n- Walking max: 25 minutes\n- Daily start: 09:00\n- Daily end: 21:00\n- Budget: midrange\n- Meal preferences: local and seafood\n- Include commute times from hotel to first stop and between stops\n- Summarize total travel time per day\n- Output: detailed format\n\nI need to use the plan_city_itinerary function with all these parameters.\n\nLet me construct the arguments:\n- city: \"Tokyo, Japan\"\n- start_date: \"2025-10-12\"\n- end_date: \"2025-10-16\"\n- days: 5\n- group_size: 2\n- hotel_address: \"Park Hotel Tokyo, Shiodome Media Tower, 1-7-1 Higashi Shimbashi, Minato City, Tokyo 105-7227, Japan\"\n- travel_pace: \"moderate\"\n- transport_mode: \"public_transit\" (the user said public transit and walking only)\n- interests: [\"architecture\", \"food\", \"art\", \"technology\"]\n- must_visit: [\"Senso-ji\", \"teamLab Planets TOKYO\", \"Tokyo Skytree\", \"Meiji Jingu\", \"Nezu Museum\"]\n- avoid: [\"long_queues\", \"hiking\"] (user said avoid long hikes)\n\n\n- daily_start_time: \"09:00\"\n- daily_end_time: \"21:00\"\n- budget_level: \"midrange\"\n- meal_preferences: [\"local\", \"seafood\"]\n- include_commute_times: true\n- walking_max_minutes: 25\n- output_format: \"detailed\"\n\nI'll carefully consider the walking constraints. The user specified walking segments should be capped at 25 minutes, which impacts route planning. I'll ensure the itinerary respects this limitation while incorporating the specified interests and must-visit locations.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_51jzoleu6ssh_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"city\": \"Tokyo, Japan\", \"start_date\": \"2025-10-12\", \"end_date\": \"2025-10-16\", \"days\": 5, \"group_size\": 2, \"hotel_address\": \"Park Hotel Tokyo, Shiodome Media Tower, 1-7-1 Higashi Shimbashi, Minato City, Tokyo 105-7227, Japan\", \"travel_pace\": \"moderate\", \"transport_mode\": \"public_transport\", \"interests\": [\"architecture\", \"food\", \"art\", \"technology\"], \"must_visit\": [\"Senso-ji\", \"teamLab Planets TOKYO\", \"Tokyo Skytree\", \"Meiji Jingu\", \"Nezu Museum\"], \"avoid\": [\"hiking\"], \"daily_start_time\": \"09:00\", \"daily_end_time\": \"21:00\", \"budget_level\": \"midrange\", \"meal_preferences\": [\"local\", \"seafood\"], \"include_commute_times\": true, \"walking_max_minutes\": 25, \"output_format\": \"detailed\"}", "name": "plan_city_itinerary"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 865, "prompt_tokens": 1201, "total_tokens": 2066, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 541, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 891}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:34.745910", "duration_ms": 11620, "hash": "3df094973f4c6ce62f52bc27ac557f9c", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": false, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 87, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I’m trying to get organized with my dog’s care — vaccinations, feeding, and walks. Can you help me set up something I can actually stick to?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. To tailor a simple, sustainable plan, please share:\n- Dog’s name, age, breed, weight, any health issues\n- Typical weekday/weekend schedule (wake time, work hours)\n- Current feeding times, food type/amount, and treats\n- Walk/exercise routine (durations, dog walker times)\n- Last vaccine dates you have (rabies, DHPP/DAPP, leptospirosis, bordetella), fecal test, and monthly preventives\n- Time zone and how you want to track (printable, iPhone Calendar, Google Sheets)\nOnce I have this, I’ll draft a weekly schedule plus vaccination and daily log templates you can stick to.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants a practical plan to manage pet care. I will collect key details (dog profile, daily schedule, current feeding/walk routine, vaccine history, and preferred formats) to tailor a simple weekly schedule and trackers. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Dog: Max, male Labrador, 2 years old, 72 lb, neutered, high energy, no known health issues. I work 9–5:30 with a 30-minute commute each way. We’re in Seattle. Feeding: 7:15 am and 6:30 pm, Purina Pro Plan Sport 30/20 kibble, 1 cup each meal, plus 3–4 small training treats. Walks: 20 min in the morning, dog walker around 12:30 for 25–30 min on weekdays, and 25–30 min in the evening; weekends we usually do a 60-minute hike once or twice. Vet records I have: DHPP 2023-09-18; rabies (3-year) 2022-10-05; bordetella (intranasal) 2024-04-10; leptospirosis 2023-09-18; fecal 2024-04-10 negative. He’s crate trained, chews a lot, and pulls on leash sometimes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great — here’s a practical baseline and what’s likely due next.\n\nDaily care\n- Feeding: Keep 7:15 am and 6:30 pm. Stay at 1 cup/meal for now; adjust ±10% based on body condition (aim BCS 4–5/9). Treats ≤10% of daily calories. Consider a slow-feeder or snuffle mat.\n- Walks/exercise: Morning 20 min + midday 25–30 min (walker) + evening 25–30 min meets 70–90 min total most days; add weekend 60-min hikes. Add 5–10 min of loose-leash practice daily; a front-clip harness can help with pulling.\n- Enrichment: Rotate safe chews, short training games (impulse control, settle on mat), and sniffy walks.\n\nVaccines/tests (approximate timelines)\n- Rabies (3-yr): next around 2025-10-05 (confirm with your vet/local rules).\n- DHPP/DAPP: next around 2026-09-18 (many vets boost every 3 years for adults).\n- Bordetella: next around 2025-04-10; some daycares require every 6 months.\n- Leptospirosis: annual — next around 2024-09-18; if not boosted since then, schedule soon.\n- Fecal test: annual — next around 2025-04-10.\n- Heartworm: annual test; monthly heartworm/flea/tick prevention on a recurring day.\n\nWould you like me to generate a one-page weekly schedule and simple trackers? If yes, please confirm:\n- Time zone (Seattle/Pacific?) and exact times you want on the schedule\n- Whether to include a stool-quality (1–5) and notes field\n- Preferred reminder platform(s) (iPhone Calendar) and a Google Sheets header row", "reasoning_content": "I have enough context to propose a baseline schedule, enrichment, and vaccine timelines using standard intervals. I’ll keep advice practical and note that exact due dates depend on local regulations and the vet. I’ll also ask about preferred reminders and logs before generating templates. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes, Seattle (US/Pacific). I use iPhone Calendar and Google Sheets. Please keep it plain text. The walker usually comes at 12:30 Mon–Fri. I want a stool quality 1–5 and a notes field. Monthly heartworm/flea/tick is fine on the 1st."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. I can provide:\n- A one-page weekly schedule aligned to your routine (feed 7:15 am and 6:30 pm; walks at 7:30 am, 12:30 pm Mon–Fri, and 7:00 pm; Saturday long hike at 9:00 am if applicable).\n- A vaccination tracker including the due approximations we discussed.\n- A monthly prevention reminder on the 1st.\n- Sample iPhone Calendar reminder text and a Google Sheets header row.\nBefore I generate, please confirm the exact times you want on the schedule (7:15 am feed, 7:30 am walk; 12:30 pm weekday walk; 6:30 pm feed; 7:00 pm walk; Saturday hike 9:00 am) and whether to include those vaccine due approximations. I’ll keep everything concise and in plain text.", "reasoning_content": "The user confirmed time zone, platforms, midday walker time, and monthly prevention day. I will outline exactly what I’ll generate and request final confirmation of key times and whether to include vaccine due approximations before producing the templates. No tools are needed."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please generate the one-page weekly schedule and vaccination tracker for Max now, in plain text, including: feeding at 7:15 am and 6:30 pm; walks at 7:30 am, 12:30 pm (Mon–Fri), and 7:00 pm; a Saturday long hike at 9:00 am; stool quality (1–5) and notes fields; a monthly preventive reminder on the 1st at 8:00 pm; sample iPhone Calendar reminders; and a Google Sheets header row I can paste. Include the vaccine due approximations you listed and keep it concise."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "resize_image", "description": "Resize and reformat a local image file", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute file path to the image"}, "width": {"type": "integer", "description": "Target width in pixels", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10000}, "height": {"type": "integer", "description": "Target height in pixels", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10000}, "keep_aspect": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Preserve aspect ratio when only one dimension is provided"}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output image format", "enum": ["jpg", "png", "webp"]}, "output_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute output file path"}}, "required": ["path"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_sql_query", "description": "Execute a SQL query on a database and return results", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "SQL to execute"}, "connection_uri": {"type": "string", "description": "Database connection URI"}, "timeout_ms": {"type": "integer", "description": "Timeout in milliseconds", "minimum": 100, "maximum": 600000}}, "required": ["query", "connection_uri"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "064500568d2f4bbe9adcd7ecd18d951c", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to generate a one-page weekly schedule and vaccination tracker for Max, their 2-year-old Labrador in Seattle. They want it in plain text with:\n\n1. Feeding at 7:15 am and 6:30 pm\n2. Walks at 7:30 am, 12:30 pm (Mon-Fri), and 7:00 pm\n3. Saturday long hike at 9:00 am\n4. Stool quality (1-5) and notes fields\n5. Monthly preventive reminder on the 1st at 8:00 pm\n6. Sample iPhone Calendar reminders\n7. Google Sheets header row\n8. Vaccine due approximations\n\nI need to output this as plain text in a format that's easy to read and use. Let me create a comprehensive but concise document.\n\nSince the user asked for plain text and the previous tool calls weren't relevant here (they were for image/database work), I'll just generate the text directly.\n\nLet me structure:\n1. Weekly schedule\n2. Vaccination tracker with due dates\n3. Monthly prevention reminder\n4. iPhone Calendar sample reminders\n5. Google Sheets header row\n\nI should keep it concise as requested. Let me generate this.\n</think>\n\n# MAX'S WEEKLY CARE SCHEDULE — PACIFIC TIME\n\n## DAILY ROUTINE\n\n| TIME | ACTIVITY | NOTES |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| 7:15 am | Breakfast — 1 cup Purina Pro Plan Sport 30/20 | |\n| 7:30 am | Morning walk — 20 min | Leash practice; watch for pulling |\n| 12:30 pm | Midday walk (Mon–Fri) — 25–30 min | Dog walker |\n| 6:30 pm | Dinner — 1 cup Purina Pro Plan Sport 30/20 | |\n| 7:00 pm | Evening walk — 25–30 min | Sniffy walk allowed |\n| — | Treats — 3–4 small training treats/day | Keep ≤10% daily calories |\n| — | Enrichment — rotate chews, short training games | |\n\n## WEEKEND\n\n| TIME | ACTIVITY | NOTES |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| 7:15 am | Breakfast — 1 cup | |\n| 9:00 am | Long hike — 60 min | Optional: 1–2x/week |\n| 12:30 pm | Midday walk — 25–30 min | |\n| 6:30 pm | Dinner — 1 cup | |\n| 7:00 pm | Evening walk — 25–30 min | |\n\n---\n\n## VACCINATION & PREVENTIVE TRACKER\n\n| VACCINE/TEST | LAST DATE | NEXT DUE (APPROX) |\n|--------------|-----------|-------------------|\n| Rabies (3-year) | 2022-10-05 | 2025-10-05 |\n| DHPP/DAPP | 2023-09-18 | 2026-09-18 |\n| Bordetella (intranasal) | 2024-04-10 | 2025-04-10 |\n| Leptospirosis | 2023-09-18 | 2024-09-18 — SCHEDULE SOON |\n| Fecal test | 2024-04-10 | 2025-04-10 |\n| Heartworm test | — | Annual |\n| Heartworm/flea/tick preventive | — | Monthly on 1st |\n\n---\n\n## iPHONE CALENDAR REMINDERS — SAMPLE TEXT\n\n**Daily:**\n- \"7:15 am — Feed Max breakfast (1 cup)\"\n- \"7:30 am — Morning walk Max (20 min)\"\n- \"6:30 pm — Feed Max dinner (1 cup)\"\n- \"7:00 pm — Evening walk Max (25–30 min)\"\n\n**Monthly:**\n- \"8:00 pm — Heartworm/flea/tick preventive for Max\"\n\n**Vaccine reminders (set 2 weeks out):**\n- \"Schedule Max leptospirosis vaccine — due ~Sept 2024\"\n- \"Schedule Max bordetella — due ~April 2025\"\n\n---\n\n## GOOGLE SHEETS HEADER ROW\n\n```\nDate | Day | Breakfast Time | Dinner Time | Morning Walk | Midday Walk (M-F) | Evening Walk | Weekend Hike | Stool Quality (1-5) | Treats Given | Notes\n```\n\n---\n\n## DAILY LOG ENTRY EXAMPLE\n\n```\n2024-07-15 | Mon | 7:15 am | 6:30 pm | 7:30 am (20 min) | 12:30 pm (30 min) | 7:00 pm (25 min) | — | 3 | 3 | Pulled on leash AM; good settle after\n```\n\n---\n\nPrint or save this sheet, fill in daily, and review weekly. Adjust portions if Max's weight/ BCS changes. The monthly preventive reminder on the 1st at 8:00 pm keeps prevention consistent year-round.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716566, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1053, "prompt_tokens": 1637, "total_tokens": 2690, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 254, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1339}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "stop", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:39.126802", "duration_ms": 15925, "hash": "cc7b29eea93859d814b6bef4fc783f51", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": false, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "stop", "tool_calls_valid": null, "tool_calls_count": 0}
{"data_index": 88, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I want to track my daily water intake and get reminders, but I don't want it to be annoying."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can set a daily goal and schedule reminders tailored to your routine. Please share:\n- Target daily intake (in milliliters)\n- Your timezone (IANA, e.g., America/Los_Angeles)\n- Reminder style: fixed times or every N minutes\n- Days of week to receive reminders\n- Preferred notification type (push, SMS, or email)\n- Any quiet hours to avoid pings", "reasoning_content": "The user wants hydration tracking with gentle reminders. I should gather the exact schedule preferences, timezone, notification channel, goal, and any quiet hours. Once confirmed, I will call a single scheduling tool to create the reminder plan and goal. The tool would be create_hydration_schedule with parameters: user_id, schedule_type (fixed_times or interval), times or interval, timezone (IANA), days_of_week, delivery_channel, daily_goal_ml, start_date/end_date, and quiet_hours."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Goal is 2400 ml/day. Timezone is America/Los_Angeles. Fixed times would be best: mid‑morning, lunch, mid‑afternoon, and early evening. Weekdays only. Quiet hours from 22:00 to 07:00. Push notifications only."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on your routine, I suggest reminders at 09:30, 12:00, 15:00, and 18:30, Monday–Friday. If that works, please provide:\n- Your user ID\n- Start date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- Optional label (e.g., \"Workday hydration\") and end date (if any)\nI’ll set the schedule with quiet hours 22:00–07:00, push notifications, and a 2400 ml daily goal.", "reasoning_content": "The user prefers fixed times on weekdays with quiet hours and a 2400 ml goal in America/Los_Angeles via push. I will propose specific times that match the stated windows, then ask for user_id and start date. Once confirmed, I will make a single call to create_hydration_schedule with schedule_type=fixed_times, times=[09:30,12:00,15:00,18:30], timezone=America/Los_Angeles, days_of_week=[Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu,Fri], delivery_channel=push, daily_goal_ml=2400, quiet_hours={22:00–07:00}, and start_date/end_date as provided."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please set it up: user_id u-23988; schedule_type fixed_times; times 09:30, 12:00, 15:00, 18:30; timezone America/Los_Angeles; days Mon–Fri; delivery push; daily_goal_ml 2400; quiet_hours start 22:00 end 07:00; start_date 2025-11-10; no end_date; label \"Workday hydration\"."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "create_hydration_schedule", "description": "Create or update a hydration reminder schedule and daily water intake goal for a user", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"user_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Unique user identifier"}, "schedule_type": {"type": "string", "description": "Reminder schedule type", "enum": ["fixed_times", "interval"]}, "times": {"type": "array", "description": "Reminder times in 24-hour format HH:MM", "items": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"}, "minItems": 1}, "repeat_interval_minutes": {"type": "integer", "description": "Interval in minutes for periodic reminders (used when schedule_type=interval)", "minimum": 15, "maximum": 720}, "timezone": {"type": "string", "description": "IANA timezone, e.g., America/Los_Angeles"}, "days_of_week": {"type": "array", "description": "Days of week to send reminders", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"]}, "minItems": 1}, "delivery_channel": {"type": "string", "description": "Notification channel", "enum": ["push", "sms", "email"]}, "daily_goal_ml": {"type": "integer", "description": "Daily water intake goal in milliliters", "minimum": 250, "maximum": 10000}, "start_date": {"type": "string", "description": "Start date (YYYY-MM-DD)", "format": "date"}, "end_date": {"type": "string", "description": "End date (YYYY-MM-DD), omit for no end", "format": "date"}, "quiet_hours": {"type": "object", "description": "Quiet hours window to suppress notifications", "properties": {"start_time": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM 24-hour", "pattern": "^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"}, "end_time": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM 24-hour", "pattern": "^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"}}, "required": ["start_time", "end_time"]}, "label": {"type": "string", "description": "Human-readable schedule label"}}, "required": ["user_id", "schedule_type", "times", "timezone", "days_of_week", "delivery_channel"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450059b95f7a9e73688940713eaf7c", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants to create a hydration schedule with the following parameters:\n- user_id: \"u-23988\"\n- schedule_type: \"fixed_times\"\n- times: [\"09:30\", \"12:00\", \"15:00\", \"18:30\"]\n- timezone: \"America/Los_Angeles\"\n- days_of_week: [\"Mon\", \"Tue\", \"Wed\", \"Thu\", \"Fri\"]\n- delivery_channel: \"push\"\n- daily_goal_ml: 2400\n- quiet_hours: {\"start_time\": \"22:00\", \"end_time\": \"07:00\"}\n- start_date: \"2025-11-10\"\n- end_date: not provided (optional)\n- label: \"Workday hydration\"\n\nI have all the required parameters, so I can make the function call now.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_gc3aeozutzya_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"user_id\": \"u-23988\", \"schedule_type\": \"fixed_times\", \"times\": [\"09:30\", \"12:00\", \"15:00\", \"18:30\"], \"timezone\": \"America/Los_Angeles\", \"days_of_week\": [\"Mon\", \"Tue\", \"Wed\", \"Thu\", \"Fri\"], \"delivery_channel\": \"push\", \"daily_goal_ml\": 2400, \"quiet_hours\": {\"start_time\": \"22:00\", \"end_time\": \"07:00\"}, \"start_date\": \"2025-11-10\", \"label\": \"Workday hydration\"}", "name": "create_hydration_schedule"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716569, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 368, "prompt_tokens": 1110, "total_tokens": 1478, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 174, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 891}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:32.623832", "duration_ms": 9312, "hash": "504277d63a19d46c11dabaa133be8799", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 89, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We're rolling out bed management automation and want to assign inpatient beds using acuity and specialty. Can you help us set this up?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. To configure safe, policy-compliant assignments, I’ll need:\n- Your placement rules: acuity-to-level-of-care (ICU/Stepdown/MedSurg), isolation requirements, telemetry needs, same-gender policy for semi-private rooms, specialty matching, and closed/blocked wards.\n- Patient profile: ID, age, gender, acuity, specialty, isolation type, telemetry requirement, any negative-pressure need, language, fall risk, expected LOS.\n- Candidate bed inventory: for each bed — bed_id, ward, unit type (ICU/Stepdown/MedSurg), specialty, room type (private/semi-private), roommate gender if applicable, telemetry capability, isolation support, negative pressure, occupied/hold status, ward open/closed, nurse ratio, distance to nurse station.\nOnce you share those, I can run a single assignment and return the top match with reasoning.", "reasoning_content": "The user needs a structured approach for assigning beds based on clinical and operational rules. I will clarify policies (acuity-to-level-of-care, isolation, telemetry, gender in semi-private rooms, specialty matching, closed wards) and the data I’ll need (patient profile and candidate bed inventory). For execution, I plan a single call to an assign_bed tool that accepts a patient object, a list of beds, constraints, and scoring weights to return the best match."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Policies:\n- Acuity mapping: 4–5 -> ICU, 3 -> Stepdown, 1–2 -> MedSurg.\n- Keep patients on a matching specialty unit when available.\n- Telemetry required for non-ICU cardiology patients and for arrhythmias.\n- Isolation: contact/droplet/airborne must match room capability; airborne requires negative pressure.\n- No mixed gender in semi-private rooms.\n- Exclude closed wards: \"West-3\".\nWhat data format do you prefer?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Use a simple JSON structure:\n- Patient: { patient_id, age, gender (M/F/Other), acuity (1–5), specialty (e.g., cardiology), isolation (none/contact/droplet/airborne), requires_telemetry (bool), requires_negative_pressure (bool), preferred_language, fall_risk, expected_los_days }\n- Bed: { bed_id, ward, unit_type (ICU/Stepdown/MedSurg), specialty, room_id, room_type (private/semi-private), roommate_gender (None/M/F), telemetry_capable, negative_pressure, isolation_supported [contact|droplet|airborne], occupied, hold_type (none/maintenance/cleaning), ward_status (open/closed), nursing_ratio, distance_to_nurse_station_m }\n- Constraints: { closed_wards, allowed_unit_types, enforce_same_specialty, enforce_isolation, allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender, tie_breakers }\n- Weights (optional): { specialty_match, unit_match, has_telemetry, isolation_capability, gender_compatible, nurse_ratio, distance, single_room }\nWhen you send a patient and a candidate bed list in that shape, I’ll run one assignment and return the best fit with reasoning.", "reasoning_content": "They provided clear rules. I’ll propose a compact JSON-style structure for patient and bed entities that aligns with a single-call assign_bed tool. I’ll also mention tie-breakers and scoring weights so they can customize prioritization."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Here’s the patient:\n- patient_id: P-44721\n- age: 68\n- gender: M\n- acuity: 3\n- specialty: cardiology\n- isolation: contact\n- requires_telemetry: true\n- requires_negative_pressure: false\n- preferred_language: Spanish\n- fall_risk: high\n- expected_los_days: 4\nWhat else do you need to run an assignment?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Please provide the candidate bed list with full attributes (bed_id, ward, unit_type, specialty, room_type, roommate_gender, telemetry_capable, negative_pressure, isolation_supported, occupied, hold_type, ward_status, nursing_ratio, distance_to_nurse_station_m). Also confirm:\n- Closed wards (you mentioned \"West-3\").\n- Whether Stepdown is a strict requirement for acuity 3, or just a preference.\n- Tie-breakers (e.g., specialty match > lower nurse ratio > closer to station > private room).", "reasoning_content": "I have the patient profile. To run a single call, I need the bed inventory with all required attributes, plus any closed wards and tie-breaker preferences. Based on acuity 3, the allowed unit should be Stepdown. I’ll request the bed list and confirm tie-breakers and weights so I can populate the tool parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Initial candidate beds:\n- E2-201-B (Cardio Stepdown East-2): unit Stepdown, specialty cardiology, room E2-201 semi-private, roommate M, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact,droplet.\n- E2-210-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2): unit Stepdown, specialty cardiology, room E2-210 semi-private, roommate F, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact.\n- E4-410-A (Medical East-4): unit MedSurg, specialty med_surg, private room, telemetry no, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact.\n- N1-105-A (ICU North-1): unit ICU, specialty cardiology, private room, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact,airborne,droplet.\n- W3-310-A (General West-3): unit MedSurg, specialty med_surg, private room, telemetry no, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact. (Note: West-3 is closed.)\n- E2-230-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2): unit Stepdown, specialty cardiology, semi-private, roommate M, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported droplet only."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. A few confirmations before I run the assignment:\n- Is Stepdown a strict requirement for acuity 3 (i.e., disallow MedSurg and ICU), or a strong preference?\n- Tie-breakers order — do you prefer: specialty match first, then lower nurse ratio, then closer to nurse station, then private room?\n- Should we exclude any bed that is occupied or on a hold (maintenance/cleaning)? If so, please share each bed’s occupied/hold status plus nurse ratio and distance.", "reasoning_content": "I’ll validate the list against policies. For acuity 3, Stepdown likely required. I need to confirm if Stepdown is strict, tie-breakers, and whether any rooms on holds or already occupied should be excluded. Then I can structure a single assign_bed call with constraints and optional weights."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Stepdown is a strict requirement for acuity 3. No mixed gender in semi-private rooms. Tie-breakers: match specialty, then lower nurse ratio, then closer to nurse station, then private room. Exclude any bed that is occupied or on hold."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. Please provide for each candidate bed: occupied (true/false), hold_type (none/maintenance/cleaning), ward_status (open/closed), nursing_ratio, and distance_to_nurse_station_m. Also confirm the list of closed wards (you mentioned West-3).", "reasoning_content": "Now I know Stepdown is required and mixed gender is disallowed. I need the operational statuses and metrics (occupied, hold, nurse ratio, distance) to complete the single-call parameters. I’ll ask for those details so the assign_bed tool can compute a ranked list."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Updated statuses and metrics:\n- E2-201-B: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 3.0, distance 12m.\n- E2-210-A: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 3.0, distance 18m.\n- E4-410-A: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 5.0, distance 35m.\n- N1-105-A: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 2.0, distance 10m.\n- W3-310-A: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status closed, nursing_ratio 4.0, distance 22m.\n- E2-230-A: occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 3.0, distance 20m.\nAdding two more:\n- E2-215-B (Cardio Stepdown East-2): unit Stepdown, specialty cardiology, semi-private, roommate None, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact,droplet, occupied false, hold_type cleaning, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 3.0, distance 16m.\n- E2-205-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2): unit Stepdown, specialty cardiology, semi-private, roommate M, telemetry yes, negative pressure no, isolation supported contact,droplet, occupied false, hold_type none, ward_status open, nursing_ratio 3.0, distance 14m.\nClosed wards list: [\"West-3\"]."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Pre-screening with your rules:\n- Eligible: E2-201-B, E2-205-A (both Stepdown, cardiology, telemetry, contact isolation, same-gender or no roommate, open, no holds).\n- Excluded: E2-210-A (roommate F), E2-230-A (no contact isolation), E2-215-B (cleaning hold), E4-410-A (MedSurg, telemetry no), N1-105-A (ICU), W3-310-A (ward closed).\nReady to run the assignment. Do you want the top 1 or top 2 results, with detailed reasoning?", "reasoning_content": "I can pre-screen: Stepdown only, open wards, no holds, telemetry yes, isolation includes contact, and gender-compatible. Likely candidates: E2-201-B and E2-205-A. E2-210-A fails gender; E2-230-A lacks contact isolation; E2-215-B on cleaning hold; MedSurg and ICU excluded; West-3 closed. I’m ready to run one assign_bed call for patient P-44721 with constraints and return the top 1–2 beds with reasoning."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Negative pressure is not required for this patient. Use these weights: specialty_match 5, unit_match 4, has_telemetry 4, isolation_capability 6, gender_compatible 3, nurse_ratio 1.5, distance 1, single_room 0.5. Tie-breakers: lower nurse ratio, then closer to nurse station, then private room. Return the top 2 beds with detailed reasoning."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Got it. I’ll use your weights and tie-breakers, enforce Stepdown-only for acuity 3, and exclude closed or held/occupied beds. Say “Assign now” (or provide the instruction) and I’ll run it and return the top 2 beds with detailed reasoning.", "reasoning_content": "They confirmed weights and tie-breakers. I’ll prepare a single assign_bed call specifying: patient=P-44721, beds=[E2-201-B,E2-205-A plus the full list for completeness], constraints={closed_wards:[\"West-3\"], allowed_unit_types:[\"Stepdown\"], enforce_same_specialty:true, enforce_isolation:true, allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender:false, tie_breakers:[\"lower_nurse_ratio\",\"closer_to_station\",\"single_room_preference\"]}, scoring_weights as provided, output_format=\"detailed\", return_top_n=2. I’ll ask for a final go-ahead to execute."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Assign now for patient P-44721 using the candidate beds and statuses provided. Stepdown is required, same specialty enforced, isolation enforced, no mixed gender in semi-private, and exclude closed wards [\"West-3\"]. Use the weights I gave and return the top 2 in detailed format."}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "assign_bed", "description": "Assign the most suitable hospital bed to a patient given rules, candidate beds, and weights; returns the best match(es) and reasoning.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"patient": {"type": "object", "properties": {"patient_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Patient identifier"}, "age": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0}, "gender": {"type": "string", "enum": ["M", "F", "Other"]}, "acuity": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 5}, "specialty": {"type": "string", "enum": ["cardiology", "neurology", "oncology", "surgery", "med_surg", "pediatrics", "obstetrics", "orthopedics", "psychiatry"]}, "isolation": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "contact", "droplet", "airborne"]}, "requires_telemetry": {"type": "boolean"}, "requires_negative_pressure": {"type": "boolean"}, "preferred_language": {"type": "string", "enum": ["English", "Spanish", "Chinese", "French", "Other"]}, "fall_risk": {"type": "string", "enum": ["low", "medium", "high"]}, "expected_los_days": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0}}, "required": ["patient_id", "gender", "acuity", "specialty", "isolation", "requires_telemetry", "requires_negative_pressure"]}, "beds": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"bed_id": {"type": "string"}, "ward": {"type": "string"}, "unit_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ICU", "Stepdown", "MedSurg", "Pediatrics", "OB", "Psych"]}, "specialty": {"type": "string", "enum": ["cardiology", "neurology", "oncology", "surgery", "med_surg", "pediatrics", "obstetrics", "orthopedics", "psychiatry"]}, "room_id": {"type": "string"}, "room_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["private", "semi_private"]}, "roommate_gender": {"type": "string", "enum": ["None", "M", "F"]}, "telemetry_capable": {"type": "boolean"}, "negative_pressure": {"type": "boolean"}, "isolation_supported": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["contact", "droplet", "airborne"]}}, "occupied": {"type": "boolean"}, "hold_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "maintenance", "cleaning", "isolation_terminal_clean"]}, "ward_status": {"type": "string", "enum": ["open", "closed"]}, "nursing_ratio": {"type": "number"}, "distance_to_nurse_station_m": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0}, "notes": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["bed_id", "ward", "unit_type", "specialty", "room_type", "telemetry_capable", "negative_pressure", "isolation_supported", "occupied", "hold_type", "ward_status"]}, "minItems": 1}, "constraints": {"type": "object", "properties": {"closed_wards": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "allowed_unit_types": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ICU", "Stepdown", "MedSurg"]}, "minItems": 1}, "enforce_same_specialty": {"type": "boolean"}, "enforce_isolation": {"type": "boolean"}, "allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender": {"type": "boolean"}, "tie_breakers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["specialty_match", "unit_preference", "lower_nurse_ratio", "closer_to_station", "single_room_preference"]}}}, "required": ["closed_wards", "allowed_unit_types", "enforce_same_specialty", "enforce_isolation", "allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender", "tie_breakers"]}, "scoring_weights": {"type": "object", "properties": {"specialty_match": {"type": "number"}, "unit_match": {"type": "number"}, "has_telemetry": {"type": "number"}, "isolation_capability": {"type": "number"}, "gender_compatible": {"type": "number"}, "nurse_ratio": {"type": "number"}, "distance": {"type": "number"}, "single_room": {"type": "number"}}}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "enum": ["summary", "detailed"], "default": "summary"}, "return_top_n": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 5, "default": 1}}, "required": ["patient", "beds", "constraints"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450059b591ff04c467c52729267753", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to run the assignment for patient P-44721 with the specific constraints and weights they provided. Let me organize the data:\n\n**Patient P-44721:**\n- patient_id: P-44721\n- age: 68\n- gender: M\n- acuity: 3\n- specialty: cardiology\n- isolation: contact\n- requires_telemetry: true\n- requires_negative_pressure: false\n- preferred_language: Spanish\n- fall_risk: high\n- expected_los_days: 4\n\n**Constraints:**\n- closed_wards: [\"West-3\"]\n- allowed_unit_types: [\"Stepdown\"] (acuity 3 -> Stepdown)\n- enforce_same_specialty: true\n- enforce_isolation: true\n- allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender: false\n- tie_breakers: [\"specialty_match\", \"lower_nurse_ratio\", \"closer_to_station\", \"single_room_preference\"]\n\n**Scoring Weights:**\n- specialty_match: 5\n- unit_match: 4\n- has_telemetry: 4\n- isolation_capability: 6\n- gender_compatible: 3\n- nurse_ratio: 1.5\n- distance: 1\n- single_room: 0.5\n\n**Candidate Beds:**\n\n1. E2-201-B (Cardio Stepdown East-2)\n   - unit: Stepdown\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: semi-private\n   - roommate_gender: M\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\", \"droplet\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 3.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 12\n\n2. E2-210-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2)\n   - unit: Stepdown\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: semi-private\n   - roommate_gender: F\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 3.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 18\n\n3. E4-410-A (Medical East-4)\n   - unit: MedSurg\n   - specialty: med_surg\n   - room_type: private\n   - telemetry_capable: false\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 5.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 35\n\n4. N1-105-A (ICU North-1)\n   - unit: ICU\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: private\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\", \"airborne\", \"droplet\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 2.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 10\n\n5. W3-310-A (General West-3)\n   - unit: MedSurg\n   - specialty: med_surg\n   - room_type: private\n   - telemetry_capable: false\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: closed\n   - nursing_ratio: 4.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 22\n\n6. E2-230-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2)\n   - unit: Stepdown\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: semi-private\n   - roommate_gender: M\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"droplet\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 3.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 20\n\n7. E2-215-B (Cardio Stepdown East-2)\n   - unit: Stepdown\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: semi-private\n   - roommate_gender: None\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\", \"droplet\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: cleaning\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 3.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 16\n\n8. E2-205-A (Cardio Stepdown East-2)\n   - unit: Stepdown\n   - specialty: cardiology\n   - room_type: semi-private\n   - roommate_gender: M\n   - telemetry_capable: true\n   - negative_pressure: false\n   - isolation_supported: [\"contact\", \"droplet\"]\n   - occupied: false\n   - hold_type: none\n   - ward_status: open\n   - nursing_ratio: 3.0\n   - distance_to_nurse_station_m: 14\n\nI'm ready to run the assignment using the function.\n\nFirst, I'll filter out beds that don't meet the requirements. The patient needs Stepdown, so E4-410-A and W3-310-A are out. E2-230-A fails because it lacks contact isolation. E2-215-B is eliminated since it's under cleaning. N1-105-A doesn't work as it's ICU. That leaves me with three options: E2-201-B, E2-210-A, and E2-205-A.\n\nNow checking E2-210-A - the patient is male but the roommate is female, which violates the gender compatibility rule. This means all three candidates fail to qualify.\n\nI should verify my function is receiving the correct parameters to execute this filtering properly.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_5zd92ujoryie_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"patient\": {\"patient_id\": \"P-44721\", \"age\": 68, \"gender\": \"M\", \"acuity\": 3, \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"isolation\": \"contact\", \"requires_telemetry\": true, \"requires_negative_pressure\": false, \"preferred_language\": \"Spanish\", \"fall_risk\": \"high\", \"expected_los_days\": 4}, \"beds\": [{\"bed_id\": \"E2-201-B\", \"ward\": \"Cardio Stepdown East-2\", \"unit_type\": \"Stepdown\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"E2-201\", \"room_type\": \"semi_private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"M\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\", \"droplet\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 3.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 12}, {\"bed_id\": \"E2-210-A\", \"ward\": \"Cardio Stepdown East-2\", \"unit_type\": \"Stepdown\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"E2-210\", \"room_type\": \"semi_private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"F\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 3.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 18}, {\"bed_id\": \"E4-410-A\", \"ward\": \"Medical East-4\", \"unit_type\": \"MedSurg\", \"specialty\": \"med_surg\", \"room_id\": \"E4-410\", \"room_type\": \"private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"None\", \"telemetry_capable\": false, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 5.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 35}, {\"bed_id\": \"N1-105-A\", \"ward\": \"ICU North-1\", \"unit_type\": \"ICU\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"N1-105\", \"room_type\": \"private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"None\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\", \"airborne\", \"droplet\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 2.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 10}, {\"bed_id\": \"W3-310-A\", \"ward\": \"General West-3\", \"unit_type\": \"MedSurg\", \"specialty\": \"med_surg\", \"room_id\": \"W3-310\", \"room_type\": \"private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"None\", \"telemetry_capable\": false, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"closed\", \"nursing_ratio\": 4.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 22}, {\"bed_id\": \"E2-230-A\", \"ward\": \"Cardio Stepdown East-2\", \"unit_type\": \"Stepdown\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"E2-230\", \"room_type\": \"semi_private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"M\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"droplet\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 3.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 20}, {\"bed_id\": \"E2-215-B\", \"ward\": \"Cardio Stepdown East-2\", \"unit_type\": \"Stepdown\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"E2-215\", \"room_type\": \"semi_private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"None\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\", \"droplet\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"cleaning\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 3.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 16}, {\"bed_id\": \"E2-205-A\", \"ward\": \"Cardio Stepdown East-2\", \"unit_type\": \"Stepdown\", \"specialty\": \"cardiology\", \"room_id\": \"E2-205\", \"room_type\": \"semi_private\", \"roommate_gender\": \"M\", \"telemetry_capable\": true, \"negative_pressure\": false, \"isolation_supported\": [\"contact\", \"droplet\"], \"occupied\": false, \"hold_type\": \"none\", \"ward_status\": \"open\", \"nursing_ratio\": 3.0, \"distance_to_nurse_station_m\": 14}], \"constraints\": {\"closed_wards\": [\"West-3\"], \"allowed_unit_types\": [\"Stepdown\"], \"enforce_same_specialty\": true, \"enforce_isolation\": true, \"allow_semiprivate_mixed_gender\": false, \"tie_breakers\": [\"specialty_match\", \"lower_nurse_ratio\", \"closer_to_station\", \"single_room_preference\"]}, \"scoring_weights\": {\"specialty_match\": 5, \"unit_match\": 4, \"has_telemetry\": 4, \"isolation_capability\": 6, \"gender_compatible\": 3, \"nurse_ratio\": 1.5, \"distance\": 1, \"single_room\": 0.5}, \"output_format\": \"detailed\", \"return_top_n\": 2}", "name": "assign_bed"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716569, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 2667, "prompt_tokens": 3231, "total_tokens": 5898, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 1319, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 3131}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sensitive": false, "output_sensitive": false, "input_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_type": 0, "output_sensitive_int": 0, "base_resp": {"status_code": 0, "status_msg": ""}}, "status": "success", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "last_run_at": "2026-05-02T18:09:48.352296", "duration_ms": 24967, "hash": "e47545dd738f280ca558e5726d31564f", "provider": "", "expected_tool_call": true, "error_only_reasoning_checked": 1, "error_only_reasoning": false, "tool_calls_finish_reason": "tool_calls", "tool_calls_valid": true, "tool_calls_count": 1}
{"data_index": 90, "request": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are MiniMax M2, an AI assistant developed by Minimax. You are a helpful assistant."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We’re trying to balance reservations and walk-ins for tonight’s dinner service to keep waits low. Can you help us figure out a strategy?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Absolutely. To build a workable plan, please share: date and service window, table inventory (IDs or counts and areas), the absolute path to your reservations file, typical dining time, expected walk-in arrivals by 15-minute slot and party-size mix, and any rules like reservation grace periods or whether tables can be combined.", "reasoning_content": "The user wants to minimize wait times across reservations and walk-ins. I need concrete shift details and constraints to build an optimization. I plan to call a single optimization tool (optimize_shift_plan) once I have date, service window, table inventory/IDs, reservation data path, dining time assumptions, walk-in arrivals/mix, and policy constraints (grace periods, table combining, kitchen throttle, targets)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Service is 17:00–22:00 on 2025-11-08. We have a mix of 2-, 4-, and 6-tops. Typical dining time is 75–90 minutes. Walk-ins are about 25–30% of nightly covers. We want average quoted wait under 15 minutes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks. Please provide table IDs (or exact counts per size and area), whether the patio is in play and its hours, whether tables can be combined, and the absolute reservations file path. Also share your 15-minute walk-in arrival curve and party-size mix. I’ll use those to set up the optimization.", "reasoning_content": "We have the date, window, and high-level goals. To parameterize the optimization, I need exact table IDs/counts, whether the patio is included with different hours, table-combining policy, the absolute path to reservations, and the 15-minute walk-in arrival curve plus party-size mix. With those, I can call optimize_shift_plan in a single run."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Tables: 2-tops x12, 4-tops x10, 6-tops x4. Patio has 4 two-tops that open at 18:00 and close at 20:30 due to weather."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Please confirm table IDs, whether table combining is allowed, your reservation grace period, typical no-show and cancellation rates, and the bus/reset time between seatings. Also send the reservations file path and walk-in curve and mix by 15 minutes.", "reasoning_content": "We have counts and patio hours. I still need table IDs, combining policy, reservation grace/no-show/cancellation rates, and bus/reset time to be precise. Once I have those plus the reservations file path and walk-in curve, I can invoke optimize_shift_plan with all parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "We don’t combine tables. Parties of 2 go to 2-tops, 3–4 go to 4-tops, 5–6 go to 6-tops. Reservation grace is 15 minutes. No-shows about 4%, cancellations about 6%. Waitlist limit is 30 parties. We have 2 hosts. Staffing is 3 servers per 10 tables. Kitchen can handle up to 70 covers per hour; we want to throttle seatings to 18 per 15 minutes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Understood. Please share the absolute path to your reservations file, your walk-in arrival curve by 15-minute intervals and party-size mix, and choose a quoting strategy (log-normal, exponential, or conservative fixed). Also confirm your exact target metrics (e.g., average wait ≤12 or 15 minutes, 90th percentile wait ≤20).", "reasoning_content": "Policies and capacity constraints are clear. I need the reservations file path, your walk-in arrival curve and party-size mix, and the quoting strategy. I will include target metrics (avg wait ≤12–15 min and p90 ≤20 min) when calling optimize_shift_plan."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Reservations file is at /data/restaurant/reservations_2025-11-08.json. Walk-in arrivals (parties per 15 min): 17:00 6, 17:15 5, 17:30 6, 17:45 7, 18:00 8, 18:15 8, 18:30 9, 18:45 8, 19:00 8, 19:15 7, 19:30 6, 19:45 5, 20:00 4, 20:15 4, 20:30 3, 20:45 2, 21:00 2. Party-size mix: couples 48%, 3–4-person parties 42%, 5–6-person parties 10%. Average dining time 82 minutes with SD 18."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Perfect. Please confirm targets (e.g., average wait ≤12 minutes, 90th percentile ≤20 minutes, walk-in acceptance ≥85%, seat utilization ≥88%), list table IDs (e.g., T2-01..12, T4-01..10, T6-01..04, patio P2-01..04), tell me if you want to hold back any tables for reservations, and provide the shift ID.", "reasoning_content": "We have the data path and walk-in forecast. To finalize, I need target metrics, table IDs, any holdback tables for reservations, and a shift ID. Then I’ll call optimize_shift_plan with these parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Targets: 90th percentile wait ≤20 min, average wait ≤12 min, walk-in acceptance ≥85%, seat utilization >88%. Use log-normal quoting. Table IDs: T2-01..12, T4-01..10, T6-01..04; patio tables P2-01..04. Bus/reset time is 10 minutes. Hold back 2 tables for reservations. Shift ID is DINNER_2025-11-08."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great. Do you have any blocked tables or availability windows to apply (e.g., patio closing at 20:30, VIP holds, deep-clean blocks)? Also confirm final staff counts for servers and hosts so I can include them.", "reasoning_content": "Most inputs are ready. I need any blocked intervals and exact availability limits per table (patio open/close, VIP, deep clean), plus final staff counts. I will encode these per table and then call optimize_shift_plan with all parameters."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Yes: patio opens at 18:00 and closes at 20:30. Block T4-03 from 18:00–18:45 for a VIP event. Deep clean T6-02 from 20:00–20:30. We have 9 servers total and 2 hosts."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Excellent. Say “run it” and I’ll execute the optimization with your inputs and return a detailed seating, pacing, and quoting plan.", "reasoning_content": "All required inputs are provided. The next step is a single optimization run. I will call optimize_shift_plan with the shift_id, date, service window, reservations_path, full table list (IDs, areas, availability, blocks), reset time, combining=false, walk-in arrivals and mix, service-time stats, grace/no-show/cancel rates, waitlist limit, kitchen throttle, staffing counts, quoting strategy, holdback tables, target constraints, and request a detailed output."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Run it now. Use these exact parameters for a single optimization and return a detailed plan:\nshift_id: DINNER_2025-11-08\ndate: 2025-11-08\nservice_start: 17:00\nservice_end: 22:00\nreservations_path: /data/restaurant/reservations_2025-11-08.json\ntables:\n- {id: T2-01, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-02, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-03, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-04, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-05, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-06, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-07, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-08, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-09, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-10, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-11, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T2-12, size: 2, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-01, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-02, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-03, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00, blocked: [{start: 18:00, end: 18:45, reason: VIP hold}]}\n- {id: T4-04, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-05, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-06, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-07, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-08, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-09, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T4-10, size: 4, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T6-01, size: 6, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T6-02, size: 6, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00, blocked: [{start: 20:00, end: 20:30, reason: deep clean}]}\n- {id: T6-03, size: 6, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: T6-04, size: 6, area: main, available_from: 17:00, available_until: 22:00}\n- {id: P2-01, size: 2, area: patio, available_from: 18:00, available_until: 20:30}\n- {id: P2-02, size: 2, area: patio, available_from: 18:00, available_until: 20:30}\n- {id: P2-03, size: 2, area: patio, available_from: 18:00, available_until: 20:30}\n- {id: P2-04, size: 2, area: patio, available_from: 18:00, available_until: 20:30}\nreset_time_min: 10\ntable_combining_allowed: false\nwalkin_arrivals:\n- {time: 17:00, expected_parties: 6}\n- {time: 17:15, expected_parties: 5}\n- {time: 17:30, expected_parties: 6}\n- {time: 17:45, expected_parties: 7}\n- {time: 18:00, expected_parties: 8}\n- {time: 18:15, expected_parties: 8}\n- {time: 18:30, expected_parties: 9}\n- {time: 18:45, expected_parties: 8}\n- {time: 19:00, expected_parties: 8}\n- {time: 19:15, expected_parties: 7}\n- {time: 19:30, expected_parties: 6}\n- {time: 19:45, expected_parties: 5}\n- {time: 20:00, expected_parties: 4}\n- {time: 20:15, expected_parties: 4}\n- {time: 20:30, expected_parties: 3}\n- {time: 20:45, expected_parties: 2}\n- {time: 21:00, expected_parties: 2}\nwalkin_party_mix: {two: 0.48, three_to_four: 0.42, five_to_six: 0.10}\nservice_time_mean_min: 82\nservice_time_sd_min: 18\nreservation_grace_min: 15\nno_show_rate_pct: 4\ncancellation_rate_pct: 6\nwaitlist_limit_parties: 30\nkitchen_max_covers_per_15min: 18\nserver_count: 9\nhost_count: 2\nquoting_strategy: log_normal\nholdback_tables_for_reservations: 2\ntarget_constraints: {p90_wait_max_min: 20, avg_wait_max_min: 12, walkin_acceptance_min_pct: 85, seat_utilization_min_pct: 88}\noutput_format: detailed"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "optimize_shift_plan", "description": "Optimize seating, reservation pacing, and waitlist quoting for one restaurant shift to minimize guest wait while meeting service constraints.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"shift_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Unique shift identifier"}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Shift date in YYYY-MM-DD"}, "service_start": {"type": "string", "description": "Shift start time HH:MM"}, "service_end": {"type": "string", "description": "Shift end time HH:MM"}, "reservations_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute path to reservations JSON/CSV"}, "tables": {"type": "array", "description": "List of tables with size, area, and availability", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "description": "Table ID"}, "size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of seats", "enum": [2, 4, 6, 8]}, "area": {"type": "string", "description": "Area of the restaurant", "enum": ["main", "patio", "bar"]}, "available_from": {"type": "string", "description": "Available start time HH:MM"}, "available_until": {"type": "string", "description": "Available end time HH:MM"}, "blocked": {"type": "array", "description": "Blocked intervals", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"start": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM start"}, "end": {"type": "string", "description": "HH:MM end"}, "reason": {"type": "string", "description": "Block reason"}}, "required": ["start", "end", "reason"]}}}, "required": ["id", "size", "area"]}}, "reset_time_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Bus/reset time between seatings in minutes"}, "table_combining_allowed": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Whether tables can be combined"}, "walkin_arrivals": {"type": "array", "description": "Expected walk-in parties per 15-min interval", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"time": {"type": "string", "description": "Interval HH:MM"}, "expected_parties": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of walk-in parties expected"}}, "required": ["time", "expected_parties"]}}, "walkin_party_mix": {"type": "object", "description": "Proportion of walk-in party sizes", "properties": {"two": {"type": "number", "description": "Share of 2-person parties (0–1)"}, "three_to_four": {"type": "number", "description": "Share of 3–4-person parties (0–1)"}, "five_to_six": {"type": "number", "description": "Share of 5–6-person parties (0–1)"}}, "required": ["two", "three_to_four", "five_to_six"]}, "service_time_mean_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Mean dining time in minutes"}, "service_time_sd_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Standard deviation of dining time in minutes"}, "reservation_grace_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Grace period for reservations"}, "no_show_rate_pct": {"type": "number", "description": "No-show rate percentage"}, "cancellation_rate_pct": {"type": "number", "description": "Cancellation rate percentage"}, "waitlist_limit_parties": {"type": "integer", "description": "Max waitlist size in parties"}, "kitchen_max_covers_per_15min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Kitchen throttle limit per 15 minutes"}, "server_count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of servers on shift"}, "host_count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of hosts on shift"}, "quoting_strategy": {"type": "string", "description": "Wait estimate method", "enum": ["log_normal", "exponential", "conservative_fixed"]}, "holdback_tables_for_reservations": {"type": "integer", "description": "Number of tables reserved as holdback"}, "target_constraints": {"type": "object", "description": "Performance targets for optimization", "properties": {"p90_wait_max_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Max 90th percentile wait (minutes)"}, "avg_wait_max_min": {"type": "integer", "description": "Max average wait (minutes)"}, "walkin_acceptance_min_pct": {"type": "number", "description": "Minimum walk-in acceptance percentage"}, "seat_utilization_min_pct": {"type": "number", "description": "Minimum seat utilization percentage"}}, "required": ["p90_wait_max_min", "avg_wait_max_min", "walkin_acceptance_min_pct", "seat_utilization_min_pct"]}, "output_format": {"type": "string", "description": "Output detail level", "enum": ["summary", "detailed"]}}, "required": ["shift_id", "date", "service_start", "service_end", "reservations_path", "tables", "reset_time_min", "table_combining_allowed", "walkin_arrivals", "walkin_party_mix", "service_time_mean_min", "service_time_sd_min", "reservation_grace_min", "no_show_rate_pct", "cancellation_rate_pct", "waitlist_limit_parties", "kitchen_max_covers_per_15min", "server_count", "host_count", "quoting_strategy", "holdback_tables_for_reservations", "target_constraints", "output_format"]}}}], "model": "minimax-m2.5"}, "response": {"id": "06450058c2620c83fdb406d2bc39adec", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "<think>\nThe user wants me to run the optimization with the exact parameters they've provided. Let me construct the function call with all the parameters they've specified.\n</think>\n\n\n", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_function_sy6mkvirm8na_1", "function": {"arguments": "{\"shift_id\": \"DINNER_2025-11-08\", \"date\": \"2025-11-08\", \"service_start\": \"17:00\", \"service_end\": \"22:00\", \"reservations_path\": \"/data/restaurant/reservations_2025-11-08.json\", \"tables\": [{\"id\": \"T2-01\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-02\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-03\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-04\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-05\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-06\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-07\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-08\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-09\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-10\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-11\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T2-12\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-01\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-02\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-03\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\", \"blocked\": [{\"start\": \"18:00\", \"end\": \"18:45\", \"reason\": \"VIP hold\"}]}, {\"id\": \"T4-04\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-05\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-06\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-07\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-08\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-09\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T4-10\", \"size\": 4, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T6-01\", \"size\": 6, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T6-02\", \"size\": 6, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\", \"blocked\": [{\"start\": \"20:00\", \"end\": \"20:30\", \"reason\": \"deep clean\"}]}, {\"id\": \"T6-03\", \"size\": 6, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"T6-04\", \"size\": 6, \"area\": \"main\", \"available_from\": \"17:00\", \"available_until\": \"22:00\"}, {\"id\": \"P2-01\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"patio\", \"available_from\": \"18:00\", \"available_until\": \"20:30\"}, {\"id\": \"P2-02\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"patio\", \"available_from\": \"18:00\", \"available_until\": \"20:30\"}, {\"id\": \"P2-03\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"patio\", \"available_from\": \"18:00\", \"available_until\": \"20:30\"}, {\"id\": \"P2-04\", \"size\": 2, \"area\": \"patio\", \"available_from\": \"18:00\", \"available_until\": \"20:30\"}], \"reset_time_min\": 10, \"table_combining_allowed\": false, \"walkin_arrivals\": [{\"time\": \"17:00\", \"expected_parties\": 6}, {\"time\": \"17:15\", \"expected_parties\": 5}, {\"time\": \"17:30\", \"expected_parties\": 6}, {\"time\": \"17:45\", \"expected_parties\": 7}, {\"time\": \"18:00\", \"expected_parties\": 8}, {\"time\": \"18:15\", \"expected_parties\": 8}, {\"time\": \"18:30\", \"expected_parties\": 9}, {\"time\": \"18:45\", \"expected_parties\": 8}, {\"time\": \"19:00\", \"expected_parties\": 8}, {\"time\": \"19:15\", \"expected_parties\": 7}, {\"time\": \"19:30\", \"expected_parties\": 6}, {\"time\": \"19:45\", \"expected_parties\": 5}, {\"time\": \"20:00\", \"expected_parties\": 4}, {\"time\": \"20:15\", \"expected_parties\": 4}, {\"time\": \"20:30\", \"expected_parties\": 3}, {\"time\": \"20:45\", \"expected_parties\": 2}, {\"time\": \"21:00\", \"expected_parties\": 2}], \"walkin_party_mix\": {\"two\": 0.48, \"three_to_four\": 0.42, \"five_to_six\": 0.1}, \"service_time_mean_min\": 82, \"service_time_sd_min\": 18, \"reservation_grace_min\": 15, \"no_show_rate_pct\": 4, \"cancellation_rate_pct\": 6, \"waitlist_limit_parties\": 30, \"kitchen_max_covers_per_15min\": 18, \"server_count\": 9, \"host_count\": 2, \"quoting_strategy\": \"log_normal\", \"holdback_tables_for_reservations\": 2, \"target_constraints\": {\"p90_wait_max_min\": 20, \"avg_wait_max_min\": 12, \"walkin_acceptance_min_pct\": 85, \"seat_utilization_min_pct\": 88}, \"output_format\": \"detailed\"}", "name": "optimize_shift_plan"}, "type": "function", "index": 0}], "name": "MiniMax AI", "audio_content": ""}}], "created": 1777716568, "model": "MiniMax-M2.5", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1930, "prompt_tokens": 4087, "total_tokens": 6017, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 32, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 4027}, "total_characters": 0}, "input_sen